patibility.","Check completed versus build-recorded behavior, Epic progress and Task validation/status presentation against originating requirements.","Inspect necessary relationship and UX artifacts and actual renderings where available; assess board, contract and conversion-verification test coverage."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Whole-design requirement and contract consistency","selectors":[],"concerns":["Check missing ISSUE requirements and acceptance traceability across all substantive assessments.","Reconcile completion, repair and board contracts, failure semantics, lifecycle ownership, ordering and compatibility claims.","Check actual upstream alignment, citation support, necessary artifact verification and cross-chunk contradictions.","Ensure demonstrated findings, advice and inspection limitations remain distinct and the final status follows the required precedence."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 25 inventory units map to substantive chunks. Broad contract, model, error and test selectors intentionally recur so each implementation responsibility is reviewed with its interfaces, logic, failures and verification together. Citation ownership follows the behavior it supports. Scope establishes upstream applicability, completion defines lifecycle behavior, repair applies it to stored records, and the board consumes the resulting model. The final consistency chunk depends on every substantive chunk and does not substitute for unit coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitI