":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"delivery-board-lld-s1","attempt":3,"artifactId":"LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1","status":"changes_requested","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":7,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned scope sections align with the originating ISSUE’s reader, lifecycle, repair and recurrence-prevention requirements. The common-model DEF and recorded owner decisions establish the applicable contracts without requiring HLD ancestry. The LLD explicitly describes its Task-completion divergence, preserves the explicit-override requirement for live approvals, and distinguishes historical migration settlement. No blocking scope defect was identified.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","document:line:24","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md:5-13","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:84-90","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:196","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — Gap 12 migration requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Label the context paragraph as standalone issue work rather than a standalone feature, and mention the applicable common-model contracts there so the empty HLD contract lists cannot suggest that no upstream requirements apply."]},{"chunkId":"completion","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The completion approach is coherent, but live completion can overlook missing declared Tasks, and the recovery path does not specify how a later approval override is durably recorded.","findings":[{"id":"completion-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/0","message":"Live Story completion needs to validate TASKS membership before evaluating counted Tasks. The proposed reader discovers existing child heads; a TASKS entry whose TASK head is absent never enters that listing. Consequently, an approved BUILD with clean review can complete the Story when the remaining Task heads pass, or when none exist. The design detects this condition only during repair, despite making TASKS authoritative for board membership. Specify live validation of listed Task heads, distinguish genuinely taskless routes from incomplete Task creation, and add approval-path tests for both cases.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.1, 2.3, 2.7 and 4","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts: countedChildren and ChildStatusReader","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: scanChildren","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts: TasksPayload.taskIds","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan and syncOnPlanApproval"]},{"id":"completion-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/1","message":"The promised recovery by approving again with an explicit override lacks a persistence contract. The first approval deliberately commits even when failed Tasks hold the Story. On the next approval, approveArtifactByJsonPath leaves an already-approved BUILD unchanged, so the new override is not recorded on its approval. The new storyApprovalOverride evidence is defined to read that recorded reason. It therefore either cannot release the hold, or relies on transient request context that disappears during deferred signoff completion or repair. Define an audited operation for recording the subsequent override without undoing the committed approval, and test initial hold → override retry → deferred completion/retry.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.1, 4 and 5","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md: explicit override is recorded on the BUILD approval","src/workflow/gates.ts: approveArtifactByJsonPath, approved-or-beyond branch at lines 690–699","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: CompletionEvidenceOptions.overrideReview and storedOverride","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: deferred completeIfRolledUp call"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: scanChildren","src/workflow/gates.ts: approval and completion paths","src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts","src/cli/services/workflow.ts: approveOutcomeOf","src/workflow/storage.ts: prepareArtifactWrite and lifecycleKeepingSignoffs","src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts: artifact persistence","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tracker/unit-head.ts","src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts: persistBuildRecord","src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts","src/workflow/resolve-comment.ts: resolveTargetQuestion","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: completion holds and deferred settlement","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-rollup.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-members.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/storage-signoff-history.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/gates-lifecycle-service.test.ts: override coverage","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/completion-evidence.test.ts: override coverage"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make the existing-lifecycle preservation change explicit in section 3.2. prepareArtifactWrite currently preserves an omitted incoming lifecycle only when prior signoff history exists; storage-signoff-history.test.ts explicitly expects lifecycle loss without that history. The proposed rewrite-preservation tests should cover identical and changed content without signoffs and replace that obsolete expectation.","Retain signoff holds in the completion integration tests, including a held Epic after its Story completes. The current service supports these holds, but the proposed test list does not explicitly exercise them."]},{"chunkId":"repair","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Repair discovery and historical settlement are defined, but the execution sequence omits legacy normalization prerequisites, partial-write reporting covers only settlement, and Task round backfill can confuse Task numbers with plan-row identities.","findings":[{"id":"repair-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/4","message":"The advertised repair-at-any-schema contract is incompatible with the specified execution order. Repair starts with applyFeedback and migrateHeads, but both use History with the stored artifact id; History rejects uppercase S001 ids. Normalizing Story discovery does not rename those files or references. Flat amendments also require conversion before migrateHeads, which skips records without meta. Specify the prerequisite normalization/conversion sequence, or explicitly route unconverted repositories through conversion first. Add repair fixtures containing uppercase heads with feedback and approved flat amendments.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.5, 3.5 and 6","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts: requireId, feedback and appendLog","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: STORY_RE and ArtifactIds.parse","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts: migrateHeads and applyConversion prerequisite ordering","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts: repairFlatAmendments","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts: uppercase heads with feedback and approved flat amendment fixture"]},{"id":"repair-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths","message":"Partial-write reporting is specified only for settlement failures, although feedback migration, head migration and unit/Task creation also perform multiple independent writes. For example, feedback and several migrated heads can commit before a later migration write fails. The existing handler catches such failures as { error }, losing the list of committed changes; the proposed design supplies no replacement reporting or continuation contract for these phases. Extend RepairReport handling across every mutating phase, define which dependent operations stop after a failure, and test a failure before settlement followed by a safe retry.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.4, 3.5, 4 and migration steps 4–5","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts: handleRepoConvert catch","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts: applyFeedback","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts: migrateHeads","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts: writeMigratedHead","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan"]},{"id":"repair-003","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/4","message":"Repair must use the plan-row identity when backfilling Task build rounds. The referenced applyTasks currently selects the first Task matching either planTaskId or its own Task number. When Task t1 represents plan row t2 and Task t2 represents row t1, a passing BUILD result for row t1 can therefore be written onto Task t1, which represents the wrong row. The design explicitly recognizes differing Task numbers and plan rows but corrects only the board join. Specify an unambiguous backfill join, preserve existing rounds, and test crossed identities before live-rule settlement.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.5–3.7 and differing Task-number edge case","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts: applyTasks set.tasks.find predicate","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan number allocation and existingTasks mapping","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts: existing fixtures use matching Task numbers and plan-row ids"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: S009 acceptance and lifecycle/identity constraints","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts","src/workflow/convert/run.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/rename.ts","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/backfill.ts","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts","src/workflow/convert/raw-heads.ts","src/workflow/convert/legacy-view.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar-store.ts","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts: approved lifecycle status mapping","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-preview.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-repeat.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: git reflog confirming main-to-v2 checkout on 2026-11-07","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: commit 5c5bc0cf1 src/workflow/storage.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Explicitly retain conversion verification regression coverage in the test strategy. The ISSUE names it as required behavior, and verifyConversion shares the loader, graph and gates changed here.","Add preview/apply parity checks covering proposed head creation and settlement, and PLAN eligibility tests for statuses beyond approved.","Define COMPLETION_RULE_FROM as an immutable timestamp with a timezone and document how it relates to daemon activation, so historical attribution remains stable across releases."]},{"chunkId":"board","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The board design addresses unit association, active Task membership, plan-row identity, ordering and lifecycle-based completion. Two contract gaps remain: DIAG records are omitted despite the all-common-kinds contract, and existing unit heads without lifecycles cannot be represented by the proposed unit field.","findings":[{"id":"board-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/5","message":"The proposed kind expansion still excludes DIAG, contradicting liftStoreFile's promise to accept every common-model kind and the ISSUE's expected behavior. DIAG is a registered common-model artifact with supported storage codecs and Story ownership. Adding only EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS leaves a valid DIAG head classified as unknown-kind, producing the same false unreadable notices this fix targets. Include DIAG in the loader/type contract and define its evidence association, with a valid DIAG fixture that loads without notices. Retain the explicitly intended TESTS exclusion.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.6, 3.6 and 5","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md: Expected behavior and Fix intent","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: ArtifactIdKind and SHAPES.DIAG","src/workflow/artifact-core/codecs.ts: CODECS registration for DIAG","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/pass-through-codecs.test.ts: supported DIAG heads","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts: kindOfFile and unknown-kind handling","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: S002 acceptance criteria ac4–ac6"]},{"id":"board-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/6","message":"The published unit shape cannot represent an existing EPIC, STORY or TASK head without a lifecycle. Section 3.7 requires status: Status and reserves unit: null for a missing head, while sections 2.6 and 3.8 explicitly admit heads without lifecycles as unmigrated. Status contains no unmigrated or unknown value. Consequently, this supported input requires inventing a lifecycle status, violating the null contract, or emitting an invalid snapshot. Define an explicit representation for an existing unmigrated unit, propagate it through stage derivation and client labels, and test it through the daemon snapshot and plugin details.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:237","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:249","src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts:105 — Status union","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts: assembleSnapshot and itemOf","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts: DeliveryItemView","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md: unmigrated records must be reported as needing migration"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/5","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts","src/workflow/delivery/types.ts","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts","src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts","src/workflow/delivery/currency.ts","src/workflow/delivery/notice.ts","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/tasks/__tests__/task-build-rounds.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts: Status","src/workflow/artifact-core/codecs.ts: registered kinds","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: taskBuildPassed","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: common-model kind definitions","src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts: recordTaskRound","src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/load.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/contract.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts: TaskRowView","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts: Task and Epic rendering source","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/delivery-client.test.ts","jetbrains-plugin: delivery-consumer search"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Define whether Task validation intentionally remains the BUILD record's result or follows the latest Task history round used by completion. These sources can differ; add coverage showing how the board explains a completion hold when its displayed BUILD result passed.","Add explicit tests for TASKS-authoritative membership, withdrawn/superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, missing unit migration notices and Task status presentation. Retain conversion-verification regression coverage alongside the new loader and graph tests.","Carry Task status through TaskRowView and the actual webview renderer, and verify the rendered result during implementation. No authored/generated visual artifacts or renderings accompany this LLD; the relationship prose adequately describes the model, and no visual verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"passed","summary":"Completed whole-design consistency review against the originating ISSUE, applicable common-model requirements, recorded decisions and all four current completed assessments. The live document matches the checkpoint baseline. No additional distinct defect was identified; the substantive chunks retain seven MED findings that require changes.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md: lifecycle completion, Task ownership and migration requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts: applyInQueue, completeIfRolledUp, completeMember and reopenMember","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json: attempt 3 completedChunks scope, completion, repair and board",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json: empty attachments and absence of visual definitions","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001: artifact inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Coordinate completion-001 with repair-001 and board-002: live completion, repair and board derivation need consistent handling of missing or unmigrated unit heads and authoritative TASKS membership.","Resolve completion-002 before relying on repair's live-rule settlement: a later explicit override must remain auditable and available after request context disappears.","Resolve repair-003 across migration and board fixtures so plan-row identity consistently determines Task evidence, completion eligibility and displayed validation.","Retain conversion-verification regression coverage explicitly. The originating ISSUE requires it, and verifyConversion consumes the loader, graph and gates changed here.","Define or replace acceptance labels ac1–ac6 with identifiable requirement text; the originating ISSUE supplies narrative requirements rather than those numbered criteria.","Qualify the invariant that no Task completes unless its Story does: the documented partial-write recovery deliberately permits completed members before the Story head commits.","No authored or generated diagrams or renderings accompany this LLD. Relationship prose adequately describes the model; no visual verification is claimed. Verify the Task status rendering through the actual webview during implementation."]}],"limitations":[],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"fedc7d32a036c4fc9c9df730184ac4c886076fbf560c43e268adffe7e76108e6"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-09T13:07:48.472Z"}],"applicableAttempt":3,"status":"changes_requested","binding":{"sourceRevision":{"number":3,"contentHash":"d382bed22b7735a8841cb91513d089154e0f8a5d32106f5aaa8e311810568c08"},"reviewedContentIdentity":"fedc7d32a036c4fc9c9df730184ac4c886076fbf560c43e268adffe7e76108e6","documentDigest":"6e3dc78799e00102e03571f23b046a9183d1d69b9e581a90a0fa3462298d0b6d","workflowDigest":"dd955a89d39cb591e2337f3f6772d855e35c740768e66f0c36e89d09894750a3","author":"controller"},"preservationDigest":"3e33629c9a9dddd442d3315e9ec9b0f6b1f1c077989989778bffd0517e0bd201"}}}}
