":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"delivery-board-lld-s1","attempt":3,"artifactId":"LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1","status":"changes_requested","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":7,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned scope sections align with the originating ISSUE’s reader, lifecycle, repair and recurrence-prevention requirements. The common-model DEF and recorded owner decisions establish the applicable contracts without requiring HLD ancestry. The LLD explicitly describes its Task-completion divergence, preserves the explicit-override requirement for live approvals, and distinguishes historical migration settlement. No blocking scope defect was identified.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","document:line:24","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md:5-13","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:84-90","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:196","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — Gap 12 migration requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Label the context paragraph as standalone issue work rather than a standalone feature, and mention the applicable common-model contracts there so the empty HLD contract lists cannot suggest that no upstream requirements apply."]},{"chunkId":"completion","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The completion approach is coherent, but live completion can overlook missing declared Tasks, and the recovery path does not specify how a later approval override is durably recorded.","findings":[{"id":"completion-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/0","message":"Live Story completion needs to validate TASKS membership before evaluating counted Tasks. The proposed reader discovers existing child heads; a TASKS entry whose TASK head is absent never enters that listing. Consequently, an approved BUILD with clean review can complete the Story when the remaining Task heads pass, or when none exist. The design detects this condition only during repair, despite making TASKS authoritative for board membership. Specify live validation of listed Task heads, distinguish genuinely taskless routes from incomplete Task creation, and add approval-path tests for both cases.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.1, 2.3, 2.7 and 4","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts: countedChildren and ChildStatusReader","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: scanChildren","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts: TasksPayload.taskIds","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan and syncOnPlanApproval"]},{"id":"completion-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/1","message":"The promised recovery by approving again with an explicit override lacks a persistence contract. The first approval deliberately commits even when failed Tasks hold the Story. On the next approval, approveArtifactByJsonPath leaves an already-approved BUILD unchanged, so the new override is not recorded on its approval. The new storyApprovalOverride evidence is defined to read that recorded reason. It therefore either cannot release the hold, or relies on transient request context that disappears during deferred signoff completion or repair. Define an audited operation for recording the subsequent override without undoing the committed approval, and test initial hold → override retry → deferred completion/retry.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.1, 4 and 5","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md: explicit override is recorded on the BUILD approval","src/workflow/gates.ts: approveArtifactByJsonPath, approved-or-beyond branch at lines 690–699","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: CompletionEvidenceOptions.overrideReview and storedOverride","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: deferred completeIfRolledUp call"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: scanChildren","src/workflow/gates.ts: approval and completion paths","src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts","src/cli/services/workflow.ts: approveOutcomeOf","src/workflow/storage.ts: prepareArtifactWrite and lifecycleKeepingSignoffs","src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts: artifact persistence","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tracker/unit-head.ts","src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts: persistBuildRecord","src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts","src/workflow/resolve-comment.ts: resolveTargetQuestion","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: completion holds and deferred settlement","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-rollup.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-members.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/storage-signoff-history.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/gates-lifecycle-service.test.ts: override coverage","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/completion-evidence.test.ts: override coverage"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make the existing-lifecycle preservation change explicit in section 3.2. prepareArtifactWrite currently preserves an omitted incoming lifecycle only when prior signoff history exists; storage-signoff-history.test.ts explicitly expects lifecycle loss without that history. The proposed rewrite-preservation tests should cover identical and changed content without signoffs and replace that obsolete expectation.","Retain signoff holds in the completion integration tests, including a held Epic after its Story completes. The current service supports these holds, but the proposed test list does not explicitly exercise them."]},{"chunkId":"repair","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Repair discovery and historical settlement are defined, but the execution sequence omits legacy normalization prerequisites, partial-write reporting covers only settlement, and Task round backfill can confuse Task numbers with plan-row identities.","findings":[{"id":"repair-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/4","message":"The advertised repair-at-any-schema contract is incompatible with the specified execution order. Repair starts with applyFeedback and migrateHeads, but both use History with the stored artifact id; History rejects uppercase S001 ids. Normalizing Story discovery does not rename those files or references. Flat amendments also require conversion before migrateHeads, which skips records without meta. Specify the prerequisite normalization/conversion sequence, or explicitly route unconverted repositories through conversion first. Add repair fixtures containing uppercase heads with feedback and approved flat amendments.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.5, 3.5 and 6","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts: requireId, feedback and appendLog","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: STORY_RE and ArtifactIds.parse","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts: migrateHeads and applyConversion prerequisite ordering","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts: repairFlatAmendments","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts: uppercase heads with feedback and approved flat amendment fixture"]},{"id":"repair-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths","message":"Partial-write reporting is specified only for settlement failures, although feedback migration, head migration and unit/Task creation also perform multiple independent writes. For example, feedback and several migrated heads can commit before a later migration write fails. The existing handler catches such failures as { error }, losing the list of committed changes; the proposed design supplies no replacement reporting or continuation contract for these phases. Extend RepairReport handling across every mutating phase, define which dependent operations stop after a failure, and test a failure before settlement followed by a safe retry.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.4, 3.5, 4 and migration steps 4–5","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts: handleRepoConvert catch","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts: applyFeedback","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts: migrateHeads","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts: writeMigratedHead","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan"]},{"id":"repair-003","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/4","message":"Repair must use the plan-row identity when backfilling Task build rounds. The referenced applyTasks currently selects the first Task matching either planTaskId or its own Task number. When Task t1 represents plan row t2 and Task t2 represents row t1, a passing BUILD result for row t1 can therefore be written onto Task t1, which represents the wrong row. The design explicitly recognizes differing Task numbers and plan rows but corrects only the board join. Specify an unambiguous backfill join, preserve existing rounds, and test crossed identities before live-rule settlement.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.5–3.7 and differing Task-number edge case","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts: applyTasks set.tasks.find predicate","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan number allocation and existingTasks mapping","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts: existing fixtures use matching Task numbers and plan-row ids"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: S009 acceptance and lifecycle/identity constraints","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts","src/workflow/convert/run.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/rename.ts","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/backfill.ts","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts","src/workflow/convert/raw-heads.ts","src/workflow/convert/legacy-view.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar-store.ts","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts: approved lifecycle status mapping","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-preview.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-repeat.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: git reflog confirming main-to-v2 checkout on 2026-11-07","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: commit 5c5bc0cf1 src/workflow/storage.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Explicitly retain conversion verification regression coverage in the test strategy. The ISSUE names it as required behavior, and verifyConversion shares the loader, graph and gates changed here.","Add preview/apply parity checks covering proposed head creation and settlement, and PLAN eligibility tests for statuses beyond approved.","Define COMPLETION_RULE_FROM as an immutable timestamp with a timezone and document how it relates to daemon activation, so historical attribution remains stable across releases."]},{"chunkId":"board","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The board design addresses unit association, active Task membership, plan-row identity, ordering and lifecycle-based completion. Two contract gaps remain: DIAG records are omitted despite the all-common-kinds contract, and existing unit heads without lifecycles cannot be represented by the proposed unit field.","findings":[{"id":"board-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/5","message":"The proposed kind expansion still excludes DIAG, contradicting liftStoreFile's promise to accept every common-model kind and the ISSUE's expected behavior. DIAG is a registered common-model artifact with supported storage codecs and Story ownership. Adding only EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS leaves a valid DIAG head classified as unknown-kind, producing the same false unreadable notices this fix targets. Include DIAG in the loader/type contract and define its evidence association, with a valid DIAG fixture that loads without notices. Retain the explicitly intended TESTS exclusion.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.6, 3.6 and 5","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md: Expected behavior and Fix intent","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: ArtifactIdKind and SHAPES.DIAG","src/workflow/artifact-core/codecs.ts: CODECS registration for DIAG","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/pass-through-codecs.test.ts: supported DIAG heads","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts: kindOfFile and unknown-kind handling","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: S002 acceptance criteria ac4–ac6"]},{"id":"board-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/6","message":"The published unit shape cannot represent an existing EPIC, STORY or TASK head without a lifecycle. Section 3.7 requires status: Status and reserves unit: null for a missing head, while sections 2.6 and 3.8 explicitly admit heads without lifecycles as unmigrated. Status contains no unmigrated or unknown value. Consequently, this supported input requires inventing a lifecycle status, violating the null contract, or emitting an invalid snapshot. Define an explicit representation for an existing unmigrated unit, propagate it through stage derivation and client labels, and test it through the daemon snapshot and plugin details.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:237","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:249","src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts:105 — Status union","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts: assembleSnapshot and itemOf","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts: DeliveryItemView","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md: unmigrated records must be reported as needing migration"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/5","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts","src/workflow/delivery/types.ts","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts","src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts","src/workflow/delivery/currency.ts","src/workflow/delivery/notice.ts","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/tasks/__tests__/task-build-rounds.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts: Status","src/workflow/artifact-core/codecs.ts: registered kinds","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: taskBuildPassed","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: common-model kind definitions","src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts: recordTaskRound","src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/load.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/contract.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts: TaskRowView","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts: Task and Epic rendering source","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/delivery-client.test.ts","jetbrains-plugin: delivery-consumer search"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Define whether Task validation intentionally remains the BUILD record's result or follows the latest Task history round used by completion. These sources can differ; add coverage showing how the board explains a completion hold when its displayed BUILD result passed.","Add explicit tests for TASKS-authoritative membership, withdrawn/superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, missing unit migration notices and Task status presentation. Retain conversion-verification regression coverage alongside the new loader and graph tests.","Carry Task status through TaskRowView and the actual webview renderer, and verify the rendered result during implementation. No authored/generated visual artifacts or renderings accompany this LLD; the relationship prose adequately describes the model, and no visual verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"passed","summary":"Completed whole-design consistency review against the originating ISSUE, applicable common-model requirements, recorded decisions and all four current completed assessments. The live document matches the checkpoint baseline. No additional distinct defect was identified; the substantive chunks retain seven MED findings that require changes.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md: lifecycle completion, Task ownership and migration requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts: applyInQueue, completeIfRolledUp, completeMember and reopenMember","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json: attempt 3 completedChunks scope, completion, repair and board",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json: empty attachments and absence of visual definitions","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001: artifact inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Coordinate completion-001 with repair-001 and board-002: live completion, repair and board derivation need consistent handling of missing or unmigrated unit heads and authoritative TASKS membership.","Resolve completion-002 before relying on repair's live-rule settlement: a later explicit override must remain auditable and available after request context disappears.","Resolve repair-003 across migration and board fixtures so plan-row identity consistently determines Task evidence, completion eligibility and displayed validation.","Retain conversion-verification regression coverage explicitly. The originating ISSUE requires it, and verifyConversion consumes the loader, graph and gates changed here.","Define or replace acceptance labels ac1–ac6 with identifiable requirement text; the originating ISSUE supplies narrative requirements rather than those numbered criteria.","Qualify the invariant that no Task completes unless its Story does: the documented partial-write recovery deliberately permits completed members before the Story head commits.","No authored or generated diagrams or renderings accompany this LLD. Relationship prose adequately describes the model; no visual verification is claimed. Verify the Task status rendering through the actual webview during implementation."]}],"limitations":[],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"fedc7d32a036c4fc9c9df730184ac4c886076fbf560c43e268adffe7e76108e6"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-09T13:07:48.472Z"},{"number":4,"status":"changes_requested","preparationKind":"impact","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"30aaeaf6469ee60cac028004f7f0083e95e604d5da034c5a13408994286b28e5","document":"27a86da5b3a8d09df803de2ac001e66264f636c7b049398ccb2f831c63a52030"},"contentIdentity":"3cb9ac15ef2beee2cf8dcaa44bc61971868b9552c76c7c6fa4c3395db91d3b02","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"design.story\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794229933602-ie4di8\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-09T13:17:16.709Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-09T05:00:05.847Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-claude\",\n          \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 302735,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"eedc4519199b24b4\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact\",\n    \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n    \"hldBaseRunId\": \"wf-1794229933602-ie4di8\",\n    \"hldEffectiveHash\": \"1d17e3d5a79a2451328357e8be478671c72e4fd4fffad3a446232ea754fa0073\",\n    \"hldAmendmentsApplied\": [],\n    \"storyTitle\": \"Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\",\n    \"standalone\": true,\n    \"sizeClass\": \"bugfix\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"envelope\": {\n      \"attachments\": []\n    },\n    \"revision\": 4\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"audience\": \"product\",\n      \"prose\": \"Approving a build now really completes its Story and Tasks and, once every Story the Epic declares is done, the Epic, which never happened before. A Task that failed its latest build, or was never finished, holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override, which can also be given after the first approval. New records have a lifecycle from the moment they are written. A repair run brings existing records up to date at any schema version and reports, step by step, what it planned, did, held and could not do. The delivery board shows Epic, Story and Task status from those records.\"\n    },\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\"\n      },\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {}\n    },\n    \"contractDetails\": {\n      \"surfaceLevel\": \"internal-shared\",\n      \"api\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"rollUp\",\n          \"signature\": \"rollUp(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader, evidence: CompletionEvidence): Promise<Status | undefined>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"id\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The TASK, STORY or EPIC head to evaluate\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reader\",\n              \"type\": \"ChildStatusReader\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Reads child listings and statuses\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"evidence\",\n              \"type\": \"CompletionEvidence\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Build, review, Task-list, override and declared-Story facts\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<Status | undefined>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"'completed' when the condition holds. TASK: its latest build round passed (unchanged). STORY: its BUILD is approved, its review is clean or overridden, and either storyTasks answers none-required, or storyTasks answers listed and every listed Task that is not withdrawn or superseded has a head whose latest round passed, or the BUILD's approval carries an explicit override. A listed Task with no head, and an answer of not-created, count as unfinished. EPIC: every counted Story is completed, and every Story its DEF declares has a head that is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"UnreadableChildError\",\n              \"condition\": \"A head of the counted child kind cannot be read\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"id parses as an artifact id\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Reads only\",\n            \"A STORY's condition reads each Task's latest round, not its status, so a later failing round always counts\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"unitMembers\",\n          \"signature\": \"unitMembers(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader): Promise<string[]>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"id\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The unit\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reader\",\n              \"type\": \"ChildStatusReader\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Reads the unit's children\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<string[]>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"For a STORY, also its TASK children, so its open Tasks complete with it\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"A member that is completed, withdrawn or superseded is left alone, as completeMember already does\",\n            \"Each frozen Task's log entry names the Story in frozenBy, and reopening the Story reopens the Tasks it froze\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"approveArtifactByJsonPath\",\n          \"signature\": \"approveArtifactByJsonPath(jsonPath: string, opts: ApproveOptions): Promise<ApprovalResult>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"jsonPath\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The record being approved\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"opts\",\n              \"type\": \"ApproveOptions\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The lifecycle service, actor and any override reason\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<ApprovalResult>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"As today. For a BUILD already approved or in signoff that is given an explicit override different from the one it carries, the override is first saved by the 'record-override' operation.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"IllegalTransitionError\",\n              \"condition\": \"The BUILD's status does not allow an override to be recorded, for example it is completed\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"The BUILD's status, revision and approval time do not change when an override is recorded\",\n            \"Other kinds, and a repeat of the same reason, record nothing\",\n            \"The batch approval then runs completeThroughService, so the held Story completes when the rule now holds\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"completeThroughService\",\n          \"signature\": \"completeThroughService(jsonPath: string): Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"jsonPath\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The approved record's path\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"For a BUILD, an outcome of kind 'story-completion' with ok, a note and the ids completed. Undefined for other kinds. It never rejects.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"The record was just approved or re-approved\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"The Story's and Epic's heads, and a head for every Story the DEF declares, exist before the walk\",\n            \"The walk starts at the STORY, and the only path that completes a Task is its Story's cascade\",\n            \"A failure leaves the approval standing and is reported with ok false\",\n            \"A Story held back is reported with ok true and a note naming the Tasks that hold it, including listed Tasks with no head\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"handleWorkflowApprove\",\n          \"signature\": \"handleWorkflowApprove(params: unknown, deps?: WorkflowApproveDeps): Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"params\",\n              \"type\": \"WorkflowApproveRequest\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The approval request\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"deps\",\n              \"type\": \"WorkflowApproveDeps\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The post-approval seam\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"followOn holds the approval's own outcomes followed by the seam's\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"A seam that returns outcomes no longer discards the story-completion outcome\",\n            \"src/cli/services/workflow.ts exposes the story-completion outcome in its result\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"handleRepoConvert\",\n          \"signature\": \"handleRepoConvert(params: unknown, repoEnv: string | undefined): Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"params\",\n              \"type\": \"RepoConvertParams\",\n              \"purpose\": \"repo and mode; mode gains 'repair-preview' and 'repair'\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"repoEnv\",\n              \"type\": \"string | undefined\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Fallback repository path\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Repair modes answer a RepairReport and work at any schema version. Once a repair has begun writing it always answers a RepairReport; { error } means nothing was written.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"{ error: string }\",\n              \"condition\": \"Unknown mode, or a repository that is not a directory, or the plan lists a problem such as a rename collision, in which case nothing is written\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"'repair-preview' writes nothing and lists the same changes 'repair' then applies\",\n            \"A second 'repair' lists no changes\",\n            \"The schema marker and the preview and apply modes are unchanged\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"applyTasks\",\n          \"signature\": \"applyTasks(repo: string, deps: ConversionDeps): Promise<TasksResult>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"repo\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The repository\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"deps\",\n              \"type\": \"ConversionDeps\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Store, history and Task sets\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<TasksResult>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"The Task sets created and the Tasks given a back-filled round\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"A BUILD result is matched to a Task by planTaskId alone, so a Task whose number equals another Task's plan row cannot receive it\",\n            \"A Task that already has a build round is left as it is\",\n            \"A PLAN at approved or any later status qualifies, as the units step does for repair\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"liftStoreFile\",\n          \"signature\": \"liftStoreFile(fileName: string, parsed: unknown): ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"fileName\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The store file name\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"parsed\",\n              \"type\": \"unknown\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The parsed file\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\",\n            \"meaning\": \"A record for every kind of the common model, including DIAG; TESTS stays deliberately skipped. A head with no lifecycle has approval state 'unmigrated'.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"No legacy approval field is read\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"buildWorkItemGraph\",\n          \"signature\": \"buildWorkItemGraph(recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet): WorkItemGraph\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"recordSet\",\n              \"type\": \"ArtifactRecordSet\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The loaded records\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"WorkItemGraph\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Each epic, story and task node carries its unit head, or null. A story's tasks come from its TASKS head when it has one, else from its PLAN.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Unit records are not counted as evidence; a DIAG head is evidence of the Story its id names\",\n            \"Active Tasks are those the TASKS head lists and that are not withdrawn or superseded\",\n            \"A task node carries planRowId and taskOrder from its TASK head\",\n            \"For a task node with a head, sourceIds holds the plan row id and not the Task's own number, so no alias can collide with another Task's plan row\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"storyStage\",\n          \"signature\": \"storyStage(route: DeliveryRoute, evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[], issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined, unit: UnitHead | null): { stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"route\",\n              \"type\": \"DeliveryRoute\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The story's route\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"evidence\",\n              \"type\": \"readonly ArtifactRecord[]\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The story's records\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"issue\",\n              \"type\": \"ArtifactRecord | undefined\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The issue behind a fix story\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"unit\",\n              \"type\": \"UnitHead | null\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The STORY head\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"{ stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\",\n            \"meaning\": \"'complete' only when the STORY head is completed. An approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays 'build-recorded', and its text states the STORY head's status, that the head is not migrated, or that there is no STORY head.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"An approved BUILD alone no longer yields 'complete'\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dataModelChanges\": [\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"CompletionEvidence\",\n        \"change\": \"field-add\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds storyBuildApproved(epicHash, storyId), true when the BUILD status is approved or later; storyApprovalOverride(epicHash, storyId), the explicit override reason on the BUILD's approval, or undefined; declaredStories(epicHash), the Story ids the DEF lists, empty when there is no DEF; and storyTasks(epicHash, storyId), answering { kind: 'listed'; taskIds: string[] } | { kind: 'not-created' } | { kind: 'none-required' }. listed holds the TASKS head's ids when it has at least one, else the Story's child TASK heads when there are any. Otherwise not-created when the Story's PLAN is approved or later, because Task creation did not finish, and none-required when it has no such PLAN, as on a small bugfix or trivial route. A clean review is not an override. The override extends k8 by the decision recorded in DECISIONS.md: on the BUILD approval it also waives failed or unfinished Tasks.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:48\",\n          \"src/workflow/tasks/types.ts:30\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Lifecycle operation record-override\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"A new lifecycle operation, valid on a BUILD whose status is approved, in-signoff or signed-off. It sets lifecycle.approval.override to the reason and leaves the status, the revision and the approval time unchanged. It appends one log entry with the actor, the time and outcome { result: 'override', summary: reason }, so the audit trail keeps each override even if a later one replaces it on the head. The reason is then found by storedOverride and storyApprovalOverride after the request is gone, including in deferred signoff completion and repair. The relationship is one BUILD approval to at most one current override and any number of logged ones.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/gates.ts:690\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:41\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts:20\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:41\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"New and rewritten workflow heads\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"Both sites that write a finished workflow artifact call one helper in src/workflow/storage.ts that settles meta.lifecycle before the write. No prior head, or a prior head with no lifecycle: a draft lifecycle. A prior head with a lifecycle and unchanged content: that lifecycle. A prior head with a lifecycle and changed content: a draft for the new revision, keeping its Signoff entries, because approval and review belong to the revision they were made at. Only these two sites change, so the writeArtifact behaviour that storage-signoff-history.test.ts pins stays as it is. Today such a head has no lifecycle until a lifecycle operation adds one, and a rewrite drops one that has no Signoff entries. A guard test fails if a production 'content' write of a delivery kind can create a head without a lifecycle.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93\",\n          \"src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349\",\n          \"src/workflow/storage.ts:178\",\n          \"src/workflow/storage.ts:224\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"FollowOnOutcome\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds kind 'story-completion' and optional completed: string[]. Additive.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/gates.ts:854\",\n          \"src/workflow/gates.ts:881\",\n          \"src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts:58\",\n          \"src/cli/services/workflow.ts:152\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"RepairReport\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"{ mode: 'repair-preview' | 'repair'; plan: ConversionPlan; result?: { applied: ConversionChange[]; remaining: ConversionChange[]; stoppedAt?: { step: RepairStep; reason: string }; held: UnitOutcome[]; failed: UnitOutcome[] } }, where UnitOutcome is { artifactId, reason, completedMembers: string[] } and RepairStep is every conversion step except the marker, plus 'settle'. After the run the plan is computed again from the files: remaining is what it still lists, and applied is every planned change it no longer lists. This covers every step without each one having to report its own writes. A step that throws stops the run, stoppedAt names it, and later steps do not run because each depends on the one before; nothing settles after a stop. Settling alone continues per unit: held units were left by the completion rule or a signoff hold, and failed ones hit a conflict or write error. completedMembers lists members already completed when a settlement failed. ConversionRule gains 'settle-unit'.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/convert/types.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/repo-convert.ts:54\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Repair order, discovery and eligibility\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"Repair runs the conversion's own steps in their fixed order, each of which can be repeated: applyRenames, applyStamps, applyAmendments, applyFeedback, migrateHeads, applyUnits, applyTasks, applyStoryHistory, then settle. Renames come first because History refuses an uppercase Story id, and amendments before migration because migrateHeads skips a record with no meta. It does not use the progress file or write the schema marker. A plan with a problem writes nothing, as conversion does. This store has 152 uppercase heads, no collisions and no flat amendments. A Story is known from a DEF declaration or from any LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR head naming its hash and story id, with S001 read as s1 in the preview, before the rename has run; each known hash gets an EPIC head. An ISSUE with no such record creates nothing. A PLAN qualifies for Tasks at approved or any later status. A TASKS head listing a Task with no head is reported as failed and left unchanged, and the Story is not settled; this store has none. Settling: COMPLETION_RULE_FROM is a fixed UTC timestamp with a Z suffix, written into the code when this change is committed and never recomputed, so the attribution of old approvals cannot move between releases. A Story whose BUILD approval time is before it is settled with storyCodeReview answering overridden and storyApprovalOverride answering 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration, because that approval passed the gate of its time. A later approval, including one made before the new daemon is running, is settled only by the live rule, so repair cannot complete a Story the live rule holds and such a Story is reported in result.held.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/rename.ts:135\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/amendments.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/units.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:92\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts:29\",\n          \"src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:154\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"DeliveryArtifactKind\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and DIAG. Relationship: one EPIC head has many STORY heads (by epicHash); one STORY has zero or one TASKS head, zero or more TASK heads and zero or more DIAG heads (by epicHash and storyId); a TASK references one plan row by planTaskId, and re-planning can change that row while the Task keeps its number. Each work item references at most one unit head of its own level, in the direction item to head. TESTS stays skipped by name.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/types.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:49\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"WorkItemNode, DeliveryItem and TaskValidation\",\n        \"change\": \"field-add\",\n        \"details\": \"WorkItemNode and DeliveryItem add unit: { artifactId: string; status: UnitStatus } | null, where UnitStatus is Status | 'unmigrated'. unit is set for epics, stories and tasks, is null only when there is no head, and has status 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. They also add planRowId: string | null and taskOrder: number | null for tasks. TaskValidation adds taskOrder; a story's tasks array is sorted by taskOrder, then by task item id. A task's validation result stays the one in the BUILD record, and the Story roll-up uses the Task's latest round: the two can differ, in which case the row can show passed while its Story is held, and the reason is in the approval's story-completion note. board-details.ts joins PLAN rows and dependencies on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null, and the client renders the tasks array in the order it receives. The plugin shows an Epic as complete only when its unit status is completed, keeps the child count as progress, and carries a Task's unit status through TaskRowView to the webview beside its validation result.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/types.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"ApprovalState, NoticeCode and AttentionReason\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"ApprovalState adds 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. NoticeCode and AttentionReason add 'needs-migration', raised for an unmigrated record or a story, epic or active task with no head or an unmigrated head, so such a record never counts as pending-decision. The plugin gains labels for these and for the unmigrated unit status.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"interactionWithShared\": [],\n    \"errorPaths\": {\n      \"errorCases\": [\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The completion walk fails after the BUILD approval is committed, for example a child head cannot be read or a write conflicts.\",\n          \"detection\": \"completeThroughService catches the rejection from completeIfRolledUp or from ensuring the heads.\",\n          \"response\": \"The approval stands. The answer carries a story-completion outcome with ok false and the failure as its note; handleWorkflowApprove merges it with the seam's outcomes so it reaches the caller.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The build shows as approved and the caller is told the Story did not complete and why. A re-approval or a repair run finishes it.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A listed Task's latest build round failed, a listed Task has no round or no head, or Task creation did not finish, and the BUILD approval carries no explicit override.\",\n          \"detection\": \"rollUp for the STORY reads storyTasks, then statusOf and taskBuildPassed for each listed Task, then storyApprovalOverride.\",\n          \"response\": \"rollUp returns undefined, so the Story and its Tasks are left unchanged. The outcome has ok true and a note naming the Tasks that hold it.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The approval is recorded and the Story stays open on the board. Approving the BUILD again with an explicit override records the reason and completes the Story.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"An override is given for a BUILD whose status does not allow one to be recorded, for example it is completed.\",\n          \"detection\": \"nextLifecycle refuses 'record-override' from that status with IllegalTransitionError.\",\n          \"response\": \"The batch approval lists the path in skipped with the reason, and nothing changes.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The caller is told the override was not recorded.\",\n          \"recoverable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A repair step throws part-way, for example a write fails during head migration.\",\n          \"detection\": \"The repair runner catches the throw around each step and computes the plan again from the files.\",\n          \"response\": \"The run stops, later steps do not run and nothing settles. The answer is a RepairReport with stoppedAt, applied and remaining, not { error }.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The report shows the step, why it stopped, what was written and what is left. Running repair again continues from the files, and a step's earlier writes are not repeated.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The repair plan lists a problem, such as a renamed file colliding with a different existing one.\",\n          \"detection\": \"planConversion lists it in plan.problems before any write.\",\n          \"response\": \"It answers { error } naming the problems and writes nothing, as conversion does.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The store is untouched and the conflicting files are named.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A repair settlement fails after some of the unit's members were already completed, because members are written one at a time before the unit head.\",\n          \"detection\": \"The settle step catches the write failure for that unit and re-reads each member's status.\",\n          \"response\": \"The unit is listed in result.failed with reason and completedMembers. Other units continue. A later repair run completes the rest, and completeMember skips the members already terminal.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The report names the unit and the members already completed; running repair again finishes it.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A TASKS head lists a Task id that has no TASK head during repair.\",\n          \"detection\": \"The repair's Task step compares the TASKS listing against the store's TASK heads.\",\n          \"response\": \"The Story is listed in result.failed, is left unchanged and is not settled; createFromPlan is not run over it.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The report names the Story and the missing Task for manual attention. This store has none today.\",\n          \"recoverable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A store file is unreadable or is not a recognised artifact when the board loads.\",\n          \"detection\": \"liftStoreFile returns a RecordLoadFailure for the file.\",\n          \"response\": \"The failure is reported as a load notice, as today, and the rest of the board is built.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The board still opens and shows a notice for that file.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"repo.convert receives an unknown mode, or a repository path that is not a directory.\",\n          \"detection\": \"handleRepoConvert validates the mode against the accepted set and checks the path.\",\n          \"response\": \"It answers { error } and writes nothing.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The caller sees the reason and nothing changes.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"edgeCases\": [\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Story with an approved BUILD and clean review, no TASKS head, no child TASK heads and no PLAN at approved or later, such as a small bugfix or trivial route.\",\n          \"expected\": \"storyTasks answers none-required and it completes.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Story with an approved PLAN and no TASKS head or child TASK heads.\",\n          \"expected\": \"storyTasks answers not-created, and the Story is held unless the approval carries an override.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Story held by a failed Task, then the BUILD is approved again with an explicit override.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The override is saved on the approval and logged, the status, revision and approval time do not change, and the Story completes.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A BUILD approved again with the override it already carries.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Nothing new is recorded; completion is attempted again.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A held Story's override was recorded, and the Story is in signoff so it completes later.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The deferred completion reads the stored override and completes it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An Epic's signoff hold after its last Story completes.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The Story completes, the Epic stays open until its signoff finishes, and the outcome says so.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Task's earlier round passed and its latest round failed.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The latest round decides, so the Story is held back without an override.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A listed Task is withdrawn or superseded.\",\n          \"expected\": \"It is not counted, and the cascade leaves it alone.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An Epic whose DEF declares a Story that has no head.\",\n          \"expected\": \"completeThroughService creates the head first, and the Epic stays open until that Story is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An Epic with no DEF, such as a standalone ISSUE route.\",\n          \"expected\": \"declaredStories is empty and the Epic rolls up from its counted Stories only.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with Tasks whose latest round failed.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair settles it with the override 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A BUILD approved on or after COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with a failed latest round and no explicit override.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair does not complete it and lists it in result.held.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Task t1 represents plan row t2 and Task t2 represents plan row t1.\",\n          \"expected\": \"A BUILD result for row t1 goes to Task t2 in repair, and the board joins each Task to its own row.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Task that already has a build round when repair back-fills.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Its rounds are left as they are.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A head with an uppercase Story id and body.feedback.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair renames it first, then saves the feedback under the new id, then migrates it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An approved flat amendment.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair converts it to a head before migration, and it stays approved.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Repair is run twice, or again after stopping part-way.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The second run after a complete one lists no changes, and a run after a stop lists only what remained, with no feedback line added twice.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A repository with no artifact records.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair reports an empty plan and writes nothing.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An ISSUE with no DEF, LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR naming its hash.\",\n          \"expected\": \"No EPIC or STORY head is created for it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A head with no lifecycle is loaded by the board, including an EPIC, STORY or TASK head.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Its approval state is 'unmigrated', a unit head has unit.status 'unmigrated', it raises needs-migration and it does not count as pending-decision.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A DIAG head in the store.\",\n          \"expected\": \"It loads with no notice and is evidence of the Story its id names.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A finished workflow artifact is written again over a head with a lifecycle and no Signoff entries, with changed content.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The head gets a draft lifecycle for the new revision, so it never has none.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"The same, with unchanged content.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The lifecycle is kept.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"invariantsToPreserve\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"An approval that was committed is never undone by a later completion failure.\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"A Task is completed only through its Story's cascade, so a held Story leaves its Tasks unchanged and an earlier status cannot hide a later failing round. A write failure part-way through a cascade can leave some members completed before the Story head; the next run finishes the unit.\",\n          \"source\": \"c2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Approved records stay approved through repair, and repair preview writes nothing.\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Local feedback on a record is carried through head migration, and no line is added twice on a re-run.\",\n          \"source\": \"c4\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"testStrategy\": {\n      \"testFramework\": \"node:test via tsx; vscode-plugin uses its own node:test run\",\n      \"testLevels\": [\n        {\n          \"level\": \"unit\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The completion rule, evidence, cascade and board derivation, on in-memory fixtures.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"rollUp for STORY: approved BUILD with clean review and all listed Tasks' latest rounds passed completes\",\n            \"rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it\",\n            \"rollUp for STORY: a listed Task with no head holds back\",\n            \"rollUp for STORY: an approved PLAN with no Tasks holds back, and a Story with no PLAN and no Tasks completes\",\n            \"rollUp for STORY: a listed withdrawn or superseded Task is not counted; a clean review is not an override\",\n            \"rollUp for EPIC: a declared Story without a terminal head holds it; an Epic with no DEF rolls up from its counted Stories\",\n            \"unitMembers includes TASK heads, and a held Story leaves every Task unchanged\",\n            \"reopening a Story reopens only the Tasks it froze\",\n            \"record-override keeps status, revision and approval time, logs the actor and reason, and is refused from a completed BUILD\",\n            \"liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and a valid DIAG with no notice, gives a head with no lifecycle the state unmigrated, and TESTS stays skipped\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: TASKS-listed membership, withdrawn and superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, unit, planRowId and taskOrder, and a Task whose number differs from its plan row has no number alias in sourceIds\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: unit is null for a missing head and has status unmigrated for a head with no lifecycle\",\n            \"a missing or unmigrated unit raises needs-migration and not pending-decision\",\n            \"gate sorts tasks by taskOrder then id\",\n            \"storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head, and an approved BUILD otherwise stays build-recorded with text giving the head's status, that it is not migrated, or that there is no head\",\n            \"board-details joins on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null\",\n            \"board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status\",\n            \"TaskRowView carries a Task's unit status, including unmigrated\",\n            \"the storage helper: a first write gets a draft lifecycle; a rewrite with unchanged content keeps the lifecycle; a rewrite with changed content gets a draft and keeps Signoff entries, with no Signoff entries and with them\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"src/workflow/__tests__/lifecycle-fixtures.ts\",\n            \"in-memory delivery records as in src/workflow/delivery/__tests__\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Real store writes through approval, first write and repair.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD: the outcome merges the approval's own followOn with the seam's, and the Story, its Tasks and its Epic complete\",\n            \"a walk failure leaves the approval standing and reports ok false\",\n            \"a live approval with a listed Task missing its head is held and named in the note\",\n            \"initial approval held, then re-approval with an override records it and completes the Story, then a failure injected in that completion is finished by a later re-approval using the stored override\",\n            \"a held Story in signoff completes later from the stored override\",\n            \"an Epic with a signoff hold stays open after its Story completes\",\n            \"the CLI adapter exposes the story-completion outcome\",\n            \"both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle\",\n            \"guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle\",\n            \"repair-preview writes nothing, and the changes 'repair' applies are the ones the preview listed, including proposed head creation and settlement\",\n            \"repair on a store with an uppercase head holding body.feedback and an approved flat amendment: the head is renamed, the feedback survives under the new id, and the amendment stays approved\",\n            \"repair on an already converted repository creates missing EPIC, STORY, TASKS and TASK heads, including from a PLAN at a status beyond approved\",\n            \"repair with crossed Task numbers and plan rows gives each BUILD result to the Task with that planTaskId and leaves existing rounds alone, before the live rule settles the Story\",\n            \"repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override\",\n            \"repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed and lists it in result.held\",\n            \"a failure injected in the head migration step answers a RepairReport with stoppedAt, applied and remaining and settles nothing, and the next run finishes with no feedback line added twice\",\n            \"a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit\",\n            \"a TASKS head listing a missing Task is reported failed and not settled\",\n            \"a plan with a rename collision answers an error and writes nothing\",\n            \"a second repair lists no changes\",\n            \"an unknown mode answers an error and writes nothing\",\n            \"verifyConversion keeps passing on a converted fixture with the changed loader, graph and gates\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"a temporary repository with a seeded .insrc/artifacts store\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"contract\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The daemon and plugin agree on the new board fields and labels.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts carries unit (including status unmigrated), planRowId, taskOrder, unmigrated and needs-migration through the snapshot\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/delivery-client.test.ts reads the same shape\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"smoke\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The Task status renders in the real board webview.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"Render the board webview during the build and confirm a Task row shows its unit status, including an unmigrated one\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac1\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and a valid DIAG with no notice\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: TASKS-listed membership, withdrawn and superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, unit, planRowId and taskOrder\",\n            \"the contract tests carry the new fields\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac2\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and its Epic\",\n            \"storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head\",\n            \"board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac3\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it\",\n            \"a live approval with a listed Task missing its head is held and named in the note\",\n            \"initial approval held, then re-approval with an override records it and completes the Story\",\n            \"a held Story leaves every Task unchanged\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac4\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle\",\n            \"the storage helper: a rewrite never leaves a head with no lifecycle\",\n            \"guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac5\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"repair on an already converted repository creates missing heads\",\n            \"repair on a store with an uppercase head holding body.feedback and an approved flat amendment\",\n            \"repair with crossed Task numbers and plan rows\",\n            \"repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override\",\n            \"repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed\",\n            \"verifyConversion keeps passing on a converted fixture\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac6\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"repair-preview writes nothing, and the changes 'repair' applies are the ones the preview listed\",\n            \"a second repair lists no changes\",\n            \"a failure injected in the head migration step answers a RepairReport, and the next run finishes\",\n            \"a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"migration\": {\n      \"stateBefore\": \"No unit ever reaches completed: the walk in src/workflow/gates.ts:959 starts at the STORY, rollUp (src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336) needs every Task completed, and nothing completes a Task. The store has EPIC 53 draft, STORY 250 draft, TASK 1,972 approved and 42 draft, and 252 approved builds have no STORY head. A second approval of an approved BUILD records nothing (src/workflow/gates.ts:690). Two sources leave heads with no lifecycle. First, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93 and src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349 still write a new head without one, and src/workflow/storage.ts:178 only reconciles a lifecycle the next head carries; 4 records created on 2026-11-09 and awaiting approval have none (3 ISSUE, 1 LLD). Second, the installed daemon ran commit 5c5bc0cf1 from main, which has no lifecycle code, until 2026-11-07. In all, 273 records have no lifecycle, and 152 heads have an uppercase Story id. The board (src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35) admits neither EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS nor DIAG, and storyStage calls any approved BUILD complete. planConversion (src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121) does nothing at schema version 2, so a converted repository cannot be repaired.\",\n      \"stateAfter\": \"Approving a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and, when every declared Story is done, its Epic, or reports why not. A Task whose latest round failed, or that is unfinished, holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override, which can be recorded after the first approval and is kept with an audit entry. Every workflow head has a lifecycle from its first write and through any rewrite. Repair brings existing records into the common model and settles units at any schema version, and is previewable, re-runnable and reports each step. The board reads the status of Epics, Stories and Tasks from their heads, labels anything not yet migrated, and no longer calls an approved BUILD complete on its own.\",\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"action\": \"Ship the code: the completion rule, the record-override operation, the first-write lifecycle, the follow-on merge, the board's new kinds and fields, and the repair modes. Write COMPLETION_RULE_FROM as a fixed UTC timestamp in that commit.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"action\": \"Update and restart the daemon, and release the plugin with the new fields and labels.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 3,\n          \"action\": \"Run repair-preview on the repository and read the plan, including the renames and the Stories it would settle.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 4,\n          \"action\": \"Make sure no workflow is writing to the repository, then copy .insrc/artifacts and the docs folder aside. Repair renames files and rewrites references, so this copy is the way back.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 5,\n          \"action\": \"Run repair, with the steps in order: rename ids and files, stamp, convert flat amendments, save body.feedback, migrate heads, create missing EPIC and STORY heads, create missing TASKS and TASK heads, move Story history, settle units.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 6,\n          \"action\": \"Read result.applied, remaining, stoppedAt, held and failed. Re-run repair after a stop or a failed unit that can finish, and act by hand on those it cannot.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 7,\n          \"action\": \"Open the board and confirm that no record still raises needs-migration, then commit the changed store.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"New fields on the board's types, FollowOnOutcome, the new lifecycle operation and the repair modes are additive. The existing preview and apply modes of repo.convert and the schema marker are unchanged. handleWorkflowApprove now returns the approval's own outcomes and the seam's together instead of only the seam's. A second approval of an approved BUILD with a new override now records it, where before it did nothing. A consumer of the operation list sees one more operation. applyTasks no longer matches a BUILD result on a Task's number or id; every Task in this store has a planTaskId. An older plugin against the new daemon ignores the new fields but will see Stories it used to call complete shown as build-recorded until repair settles them. The STORY rule deliberately diverges from S007:FR001: a Task completes with its Story rather than before it, so a held Story cannot be hidden by an earlier Task status. Heads written by a daemon on main still have no lifecycle; the board labels them needs-migration and repair handles them. writeArtifact itself is unchanged. Steps 5 and 6 cannot be rolled back automatically; restoring the copy made in step 4 undoes them.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": false,\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": true\n    },\n    \"alternativesConsidered\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"name\": \"Tasks complete with their Story at BUILD approval\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"At BUILD approval a Story completes, with all its open Tasks, when every Task it lists has a latest round that passed or the approval carries an explicit override.\",\n        \"approach\": \"The Story roll-up reads the Tasks the TASKS head lists and each one's latest build round rather than its status. When the rule holds, completing the Story freezes its open Tasks through the cascade; when it does not, the Story and its Tasks stay as they are, and the outcome names the Tasks. A later explicit override is saved on the approved BUILD by its own audited operation. New records carry a draft lifecycle from their first write. A repair mode runs the conversion's ordered steps at any schema version, then settles units, applying the old approval rule only to approvals older than the new one. The board publishes unit status, a plan row key and an order.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"A later failing round can never be hidden, because no Task is completed before its Story\",\n          \"One decision point, the existing walk and the existing cascade\",\n          \"Repair reuses steps that are already repeatable\",\n          \"Follows k8 for clean approvals, and DECISIONS.md for overrides\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"A Task's status changes only when its Story completes\",\n          \"Touches the lifecycle, the conversion and the board in one Story\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"L\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"name\": \"Complete passing Tasks first, then roll up\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"BUILD approval completes each passing Task, then rolls up the Story by Task status.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Walk each counted Task so passing ones complete, then roll up the Story by Task status, reopening a completed Task when a later round fails. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"A passing Task shows complete even while its Story is held\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Needs a reopen path on recordBuildRound so a later failing round cannot be hidden\",\n          \"Adds a lifecycle dependency to the validate path\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Partial on status-is-reliable: a Task completed before its Story can be hidden by a later failing round, and it would need its own reopen path.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a3\",\n        \"name\": \"Any approved BUILD completes the Story\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"A Story completes on an approved BUILD with a clean or overridden review, whatever its Tasks show.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Drop the Task condition from the Story roll-up and cascade to all open Tasks. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"One rule with no Task condition\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Contradicts k8 and the owner's decision: a clean approval would complete a Story with a failed Task\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Violates failed-task-holds-story: any approved BUILD would complete a Story with a failed Task.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"chosenAlternative\": \"a1\",\n    \"openQuestions\": []\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/gates.ts:959\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts:29\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c9\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c10\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"git reflog: 756d5adf4 HEAD@{2026-11-07 17:54:07 +0530} checkout: moving from main to v2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c11\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/gates.ts:690\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c12\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1 -->\n\n# LLD: STORY-eedc4519199b24b4-s1 — Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\n\n## Summary\n\n**Epic:** `make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact`\n**HLD base run:** `wf-1794229933602-ie4di8`\n**HLD effective hash:** `1d17e3d5a79a...`\n\nApproving a build now really completes its Story and Tasks and, once every Story the Epic declares is done, the Epic, which never happened before. A Task that failed its latest build, or was never finished, holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override, which can also be given after the first approval. New records have a lifecycle from the moment they are written. A repair run brings existing records up to date at any schema version and reports, step by step, what it planned, did, held and could not do. The delivery board shows Epic, Story and Task status from those records.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [HLD context](#1-hld-context)\n2. [Contract details](#2-contract-details)\n3. [Data model changes](#3-data-model-changes)\n4. [Error paths](#4-error-paths)\n5. [Test strategy](#5-test-strategy)\n6. [Migration](#6-migration)\n7. [Alternatives considered](#7-alternatives-considered)\n8. [References](#8-references)\n\n## 1. HLD context\n\n**Framework:** Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\n**Rollout phase:** standalone\n\n## 2. Contract details\n\n**Surface level:** internal-shared\n\n### 2.1 `rollUp`\n\n```typescript\nrollUp(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader, evidence: CompletionEvidence): Promise<Status | undefined>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `id: string` — The TASK, STORY or EPIC head to evaluate\n- `reader: ChildStatusReader` — Reads child listings and statuses\n- `evidence: CompletionEvidence` — Build, review, Task-list, override and declared-Story facts\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<Status | undefined>` — 'completed' when the condition holds. TASK: its latest build round passed (unchanged). STORY: its BUILD is approved, its review is clean or overridden, and either storyTasks answers none-required, or storyTasks answers listed and every listed Task that is not withdrawn or superseded has a head whose latest round passed, or the BUILD's approval carries an explicit override. A listed Task with no head, and an answer of not-created, count as unfinished. EPIC: every counted Story is completed, and every Story its DEF declares has a head that is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `UnreadableChildError` when A head of the counted child kind cannot be read\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- id parses as an artifact id\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Reads only\n- A STORY's condition reads each Task's latest round, not its status, so a later failing round always counts\n\n### 2.2 `unitMembers`\n\n```typescript\nunitMembers(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader): Promise<string[]>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `id: string` — The unit\n- `reader: ChildStatusReader` — Reads the unit's children\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<string[]>` — For a STORY, also its TASK children, so its open Tasks complete with it\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A member that is completed, withdrawn or superseded is left alone, as completeMember already does\n- Each frozen Task's log entry names the Story in frozenBy, and reopening the Story reopens the Tasks it froze\n\n### 2.3 `approveArtifactByJsonPath`\n\n```typescript\napproveArtifactByJsonPath(jsonPath: string, opts: ApproveOptions): Promise<ApprovalResult>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `jsonPath: string` — The record being approved\n- `opts: ApproveOptions` — The lifecycle service, actor and any override reason\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<ApprovalResult>` — As today. For a BUILD already approved or in signoff that is given an explicit override different from the one it carries, the override is first saved by the 'record-override' operation.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `IllegalTransitionError` when The BUILD's status does not allow an override to be recorded, for example it is completed\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The BUILD's status, revision and approval time do not change when an override is recorded\n- Other kinds, and a repeat of the same reason, record nothing\n- The batch approval then runs completeThroughService, so the held Story completes when the rule now holds\n\n### 2.4 `completeThroughService`\n\n```typescript\ncompleteThroughService(jsonPath: string): Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `jsonPath: string` — The approved record's path\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>` — For a BUILD, an outcome of kind 'story-completion' with ok, a note and the ids completed. Undefined for other kinds. It never rejects.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- The record was just approved or re-approved\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The Story's and Epic's heads, and a head for every Story the DEF declares, exist before the walk\n- The walk starts at the STORY, and the only path that completes a Task is its Story's cascade\n- A failure leaves the approval standing and is reported with ok false\n- A Story held back is reported with ok true and a note naming the Tasks that hold it, including listed Tasks with no head\n\n### 2.5 `handleWorkflowApprove`\n\n```typescript\nhandleWorkflowApprove(params: unknown, deps?: WorkflowApproveDeps): Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `params: WorkflowApproveRequest` — The approval request\n- `deps: WorkflowApproveDeps` _(optional)_ — The post-approval seam\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>` — followOn holds the approval's own outcomes followed by the seam's\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A seam that returns outcomes no longer discards the story-completion outcome\n- src/cli/services/workflow.ts exposes the story-completion outcome in its result\n\n### 2.6 `handleRepoConvert`\n\n```typescript\nhandleRepoConvert(params: unknown, repoEnv: string | undefined): Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `params: RepoConvertParams` — repo and mode; mode gains 'repair-preview' and 'repair'\n- `repoEnv: string | undefined` — Fallback repository path\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>` — Repair modes answer a RepairReport and work at any schema version. Once a repair has begun writing it always answers a RepairReport; { error } means nothing was written.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `{ error: string }` when Unknown mode, or a repository that is not a directory, or the plan lists a problem such as a rename collision, in which case nothing is written\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- 'repair-preview' writes nothing and lists the same changes 'repair' then applies\n- A second 'repair' lists no changes\n- The schema marker and the preview and apply modes are unchanged\n\n### 2.7 `applyTasks`\n\n```typescript\napplyTasks(repo: string, deps: ConversionDeps): Promise<TasksResult>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `repo: string` — The repository\n- `deps: ConversionDeps` — Store, history and Task sets\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<TasksResult>` — The Task sets created and the Tasks given a back-filled round\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A BUILD result is matched to a Task by planTaskId alone, so a Task whose number equals another Task's plan row cannot receive it\n- A Task that already has a build round is left as it is\n- A PLAN at approved or any later status qualifies, as the units step does for repair\n\n### 2.8 `liftStoreFile`\n\n```typescript\nliftStoreFile(fileName: string, parsed: unknown): ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `fileName: string` — The store file name\n- `parsed: unknown` — The parsed file\n\n**Returns:** `ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure` — A record for every kind of the common model, including DIAG; TESTS stays deliberately skipped. A head with no lifecycle has approval state 'unmigrated'.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- No legacy approval field is read\n\n### 2.9 `buildWorkItemGraph`\n\n```typescript\nbuildWorkItemGraph(recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet): WorkItemGraph\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet` — The loaded records\n\n**Returns:** `WorkItemGraph` — Each epic, story and task node carries its unit head, or null. A story's tasks come from its TASKS head when it has one, else from its PLAN.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Unit records are not counted as evidence; a DIAG head is evidence of the Story its id names\n- Active Tasks are those the TASKS head lists and that are not withdrawn or superseded\n- A task node carries planRowId and taskOrder from its TASK head\n- For a task node with a head, sourceIds holds the plan row id and not the Task's own number, so no alias can collide with another Task's plan row\n\n### 2.10 `storyStage`\n\n```typescript\nstoryStage(route: DeliveryRoute, evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[], issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined, unit: UnitHead | null): { stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `route: DeliveryRoute` — The story's route\n- `evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[]` — The story's records\n- `issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined` — The issue behind a fix story\n- `unit: UnitHead | null` — The STORY head\n\n**Returns:** `{ stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }` — 'complete' only when the STORY head is completed. An approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays 'build-recorded', and its text states the STORY head's status, that the head is not migrated, or that there is no STORY head.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- An approved BUILD alone no longer yields 'complete'\n\n## 3. Data model changes\n\n### 3.1 `CompletionEvidence` — field-add\n\nAdds storyBuildApproved(epicHash, storyId), true when the BUILD status is approved or later; storyApprovalOverride(epicHash, storyId), the explicit override reason on the BUILD's approval, or undefined; declaredStories(epicHash), the Story ids the DEF lists, empty when there is no DEF; and storyTasks(epicHash, storyId), answering { kind: 'listed'; taskIds: string[] } | { kind: 'not-created' } | { kind: 'none-required' }. listed holds the TASKS head's ids when it has at least one, else the Story's child TASK heads when there are any. Otherwise not-created when the Story's PLAN is approved or later, because Task creation did not finish, and none-required when it has no such PLAN, as on a small bugfix or trivial route. A clean review is not an override. The override extends k8 by the decision recorded in DECISIONS.md: on the BUILD approval it also waives failed or unfinished Tasks.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:48`\n- `src/workflow/tasks/types.ts:30`\n\n### 3.2 `Lifecycle operation record-override` — new\n\nA new lifecycle operation, valid on a BUILD whose status is approved, in-signoff or signed-off. It sets lifecycle.approval.override to the reason and leaves the status, the revision and the approval time unchanged. It appends one log entry with the actor, the time and outcome { result: 'override', summary: reason }, so the audit trail keeps each override even if a later one replaces it on the head. The reason is then found by storedOverride and storyApprovalOverride after the request is gone, including in deferred signoff completion and repair. The relationship is one BUILD approval to at most one current override and any number of logged ones.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/gates.ts:690`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:41`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts:20`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:41`\n\n### 3.3 `New and rewritten workflow heads` — invariant-change\n\nBoth sites that write a finished workflow artifact call one helper in src/workflow/storage.ts that settles meta.lifecycle before the write. No prior head, or a prior head with no lifecycle: a draft lifecycle. A prior head with a lifecycle and unchanged content: that lifecycle. A prior head with a lifecycle and changed content: a draft for the new revision, keeping its Signoff entries, because approval and review belong to the revision they were made at. Only these two sites change, so the writeArtifact behaviour that storage-signoff-history.test.ts pins stays as it is. Today such a head has no lifecycle until a lifecycle operation adds one, and a rewrite drops one that has no Signoff entries. A guard test fails if a production 'content' write of a delivery kind can create a head without a lifecycle.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93`\n- `src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349`\n- `src/workflow/storage.ts:178`\n- `src/workflow/storage.ts:224`\n\n### 3.4 `FollowOnOutcome` — field-modify\n\nAdds kind 'story-completion' and optional completed: string[]. Additive.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/gates.ts:854`\n- `src/workflow/gates.ts:881`\n- `src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts:58`\n- `src/cli/services/workflow.ts:152`\n\n### 3.5 `RepairReport` — new\n\n{ mode: 'repair-preview' | 'repair'; plan: ConversionPlan; result?: { applied: ConversionChange[]; remaining: ConversionChange[]; stoppedAt?: { step: RepairStep; reason: string }; held: UnitOutcome[]; failed: UnitOutcome[] } }, where UnitOutcome is { artifactId, reason, completedMembers: string[] } and RepairStep is every conversion step except the marker, plus 'settle'. After the run the plan is computed again from the files: remaining is what it still lists, and applied is every planned change it no longer lists. This covers every step without each one having to report its own writes. A step that throws stops the run, stoppedAt names it, and later steps do not run because each depends on the one before; nothing settles after a stop. Settling alone continues per unit: held units were left by the completion rule or a signoff hold, and failed ones hit a conflict or write error. completedMembers lists members already completed when a settlement failed. ConversionRule gains 'settle-unit'.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/convert/types.ts`\n- `src/daemon/repo-convert.ts:54`\n- `src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126`\n\n### 3.6 `Repair order, discovery and eligibility` — new\n\nRepair runs the conversion's own steps in their fixed order, each of which can be repeated: applyRenames, applyStamps, applyAmendments, applyFeedback, migrateHeads, applyUnits, applyTasks, applyStoryHistory, then settle. Renames come first because History refuses an uppercase Story id, and amendments before migration because migrateHeads skips a record with no meta. It does not use the progress file or write the schema marker. A plan with a problem writes nothing, as conversion does. This store has 152 uppercase heads, no collisions and no flat amendments. A Story is known from a DEF declaration or from any LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR head naming its hash and story id, with S001 read as s1 in the preview, before the rename has run; each known hash gets an EPIC head. An ISSUE with no such record creates nothing. A PLAN qualifies for Tasks at approved or any later status. A TASKS head listing a Task with no head is reported as failed and left unchanged, and the Story is not settled; this store has none. Settling: COMPLETION_RULE_FROM is a fixed UTC timestamp with a Z suffix, written into the code when this change is committed and never recomputed, so the attribution of old approvals cannot move between releases. A Story whose BUILD approval time is before it is settled with storyCodeReview answering overridden and storyApprovalOverride answering 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration, because that approval passed the gate of its time. A later approval, including one made before the new daemon is running, is settled only by the live rule, so repair cannot complete a Story the live rule holds and such a Story is reported in result.held.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126`\n- `src/workflow/convert/rename.ts:135`\n- `src/workflow/convert/amendments.ts`\n- `src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts`\n- `src/workflow/convert/units.ts`\n- `src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:92`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts:29`\n- `src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:154`\n\n### 3.7 `DeliveryArtifactKind` — field-modify\n\nAdds EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and DIAG. Relationship: one EPIC head has many STORY heads (by epicHash); one STORY has zero or one TASKS head, zero or more TASK heads and zero or more DIAG heads (by epicHash and storyId); a TASK references one plan row by planTaskId, and re-planning can change that row while the Task keeps its number. Each work item references at most one unit head of its own level, in the direction item to head. TESTS stays skipped by name.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/types.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts`\n- `src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:49`\n\n### 3.8 `WorkItemNode, DeliveryItem and TaskValidation` — field-add\n\nWorkItemNode and DeliveryItem add unit: { artifactId: string; status: UnitStatus } | null, where UnitStatus is Status | 'unmigrated'. unit is set for epics, stories and tasks, is null only when there is no head, and has status 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. They also add planRowId: string | null and taskOrder: number | null for tasks. TaskValidation adds taskOrder; a story's tasks array is sorted by taskOrder, then by task item id. A task's validation result stays the one in the BUILD record, and the Story roll-up uses the Task's latest round: the two can differ, in which case the row can show passed while its Story is held, and the reason is in the approval's story-completion note. board-details.ts joins PLAN rows and dependencies on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null, and the client renders the tasks array in the order it receives. The plugin shows an Epic as complete only when its unit status is completed, keeps the child count as progress, and carries a Task's unit status through TaskRowView to the webview beside its validation result.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/types.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts`\n\n### 3.9 `ApprovalState, NoticeCode and AttentionReason` — field-modify\n\nApprovalState adds 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. NoticeCode and AttentionReason add 'needs-migration', raised for an unmigrated record or a story, epic or active task with no head or an unmigrated head, so such a record never counts as pending-decision. The plugin gains labels for these and for the unmigrated unit status.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts`\n\n## 4. Error paths\n\n**Error cases**\n\n- **The completion walk fails after the BUILD approval is committed, for example a child head cannot be read or a write conflicts.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: completeThroughService catches the rejection from completeIfRolledUp or from ensuring the heads.\n  - Response: The approval stands. The answer carries a story-completion outcome with ok false and the failure as its note; handleWorkflowApprove merges it with the seam's outcomes so it reaches the caller.\n  - User impact: The build shows as approved and the caller is told the Story did not complete and why. A re-approval or a repair run finishes it.\n- **A listed Task's latest build round failed, a listed Task has no round or no head, or Task creation did not finish, and the BUILD approval carries no explicit override.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: rollUp for the STORY reads storyTasks, then statusOf and taskBuildPassed for each listed Task, then storyApprovalOverride.\n  - Response: rollUp returns undefined, so the Story and its Tasks are left unchanged. The outcome has ok true and a note naming the Tasks that hold it.\n  - User impact: The approval is recorded and the Story stays open on the board. Approving the BUILD again with an explicit override records the reason and completes the Story.\n- **An override is given for a BUILD whose status does not allow one to be recorded, for example it is completed.** (terminal)\n  - Detection: nextLifecycle refuses 'record-override' from that status with IllegalTransitionError.\n  - Response: The batch approval lists the path in skipped with the reason, and nothing changes.\n  - User impact: The caller is told the override was not recorded.\n- **A repair step throws part-way, for example a write fails during head migration.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The repair runner catches the throw around each step and computes the plan again from the files.\n  - Response: The run stops, later steps do not run and nothing settles. The answer is a RepairReport with stoppedAt, applied and remaining, not { error }.\n  - User impact: The report shows the step, why it stopped, what was written and what is left. Running repair again continues from the files, and a step's earlier writes are not repeated.\n- **The repair plan lists a problem, such as a renamed file colliding with a different existing one.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: planConversion lists it in plan.problems before any write.\n  - Response: It answers { error } naming the problems and writes nothing, as conversion does.\n  - User impact: The store is untouched and the conflicting files are named.\n- **A repair settlement fails after some of the unit's members were already completed, because members are written one at a time before the unit head.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The settle step catches the write failure for that unit and re-reads each member's status.\n  - Response: The unit is listed in result.failed with reason and completedMembers. Other units continue. A later repair run completes the rest, and completeMember skips the members already terminal.\n  - User impact: The report names the unit and the members already completed; running repair again finishes it.\n- **A TASKS head lists a Task id that has no TASK head during repair.** (terminal)\n  - Detection: The repair's Task step compares the TASKS listing against the store's TASK heads.\n  - Response: The Story is listed in result.failed, is left unchanged and is not settled; createFromPlan is not run over it.\n  - User impact: The report names the Story and the missing Task for manual attention. This store has none today.\n- **A store file is unreadable or is not a recognised artifact when the board loads.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: liftStoreFile returns a RecordLoadFailure for the file.\n  - Response: The failure is reported as a load notice, as today, and the rest of the board is built.\n  - User impact: The board still opens and shows a notice for that file.\n- **repo.convert receives an unknown mode, or a repository path that is not a directory.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: handleRepoConvert validates the mode against the accepted set and checks the path.\n  - Response: It answers { error } and writes nothing.\n  - User impact: The caller sees the reason and nothing changes.\n\n**Edge cases**\n\n| Input | Expected |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| A Story with an approved BUILD and clean review, no TASKS head, no child TASK heads and no PLAN at approved or later, such as a small bugfix or trivial route. | storyTasks answers none-required and it completes. |\n| A Story with an approved PLAN and no TASKS head or child TASK heads. | storyTasks answers not-created, and the Story is held unless the approval carries an override. |\n| A Story held by a failed Task, then the BUILD is approved again with an explicit override. | The override is saved on the approval and logged, the status, revision and approval time do not change, and the Story completes. |\n| A BUILD approved again with the override it already carries. | Nothing new is recorded; completion is attempted again. |\n| A held Story's override was recorded, and the Story is in signoff so it completes later. | The deferred completion reads the stored override and completes it. |\n| An Epic's signoff hold after its last Story completes. | The Story completes, the Epic stays open until its signoff finishes, and the outcome says so. |\n| A Task's earlier round passed and its latest round failed. | The latest round decides, so the Story is held back without an override. |\n| A listed Task is withdrawn or superseded. | It is not counted, and the cascade leaves it alone. |\n| An Epic whose DEF declares a Story that has no head. | completeThroughService creates the head first, and the Epic stays open until that Story is completed, withdrawn or superseded. |\n| An Epic with no DEF, such as a standalone ISSUE route. | declaredStories is empty and the Epic rolls up from its counted Stories only. |\n| A BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with Tasks whose latest round failed. | Repair settles it with the override 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration. |\n| A BUILD approved on or after COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with a failed latest round and no explicit override. | Repair does not complete it and lists it in result.held. |\n| Task t1 represents plan row t2 and Task t2 represents plan row t1. | A BUILD result for row t1 goes to Task t2 in repair, and the board joins each Task to its own row. |\n| A Task that already has a build round when repair back-fills. | Its rounds are left as they are. |\n| A head with an uppercase Story id and body.feedback. | Repair renames it first, then saves the feedback under the new id, then migrates it. |\n| An approved flat amendment. | Repair converts it to a head before migration, and it stays approved. |\n| Repair is run twice, or again after stopping part-way. | The second run after a complete one lists no changes, and a run after a stop lists only what remained, with no feedback line added twice. |\n| A repository with no artifact records. | Repair reports an empty plan and writes nothing. |\n| An ISSUE with no DEF, LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR naming its hash. | No EPIC or STORY head is created for it. |\n| A head with no lifecycle is loaded by the board, including an EPIC, STORY or TASK head. | Its approval state is 'unmigrated', a unit head has unit.status 'unmigrated', it raises needs-migration and it does not count as pending-decision. |\n| A DIAG head in the store. | It loads with no notice and is evidence of the Story its id names. |\n| A finished workflow artifact is written again over a head with a lifecycle and no Signoff entries, with changed content. | The head gets a draft lifecycle for the new revision, so it never has none. |\n| The same, with unchanged content. | The lifecycle is kept. |\n\n**Invariants to preserve**\n\n- An approval that was committed is never undone by a later completion failure. [[c1]]\n- A Task is completed only through its Story's cascade, so a held Story leaves its Tasks unchanged and an earlier status cannot hide a later failing round. A write failure part-way through a cascade can leave some members completed before the Story head; the next run finishes the unit. [[c2]]\n- Approved records stay approved through repair, and repair preview writes nothing. [[c3]]\n- Local feedback on a record is carried through head migration, and no line is added twice on a re-run. [[c4]]\n\n## 5. Test strategy\n\n**Test framework:** `node:test via tsx; vscode-plugin uses its own node:test run`\n\n**Test levels**\n\n- **unit** — The completion rule, evidence, cascade and board derivation, on in-memory fixtures.\n  - Subjects: `rollUp for STORY: approved BUILD with clean review and all listed Tasks' latest rounds passed completes`, `rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it`, `rollUp for STORY: a listed Task with no head holds back`, `rollUp for STORY: an approved PLAN with no Tasks holds back, and a Story with no PLAN and no Tasks completes`, `rollUp for STORY: a listed withdrawn or superseded Task is not counted; a clean review is not an override`, `rollUp for EPIC: a declared Story without a terminal head holds it; an Epic with no DEF rolls up from its counted Stories`, `unitMembers includes TASK heads, and a held Story leaves every Task unchanged`, `reopening a Story reopens only the Tasks it froze`, `record-override keeps status, revision and approval time, logs the actor and reason, and is refused from a completed BUILD`, `liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and a valid DIAG with no notice, gives a head with no lifecycle the state unmigrated, and TESTS stays skipped`, `buildWorkItemGraph: TASKS-listed membership, withdrawn and superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, unit, planRowId and taskOrder, and a Task whose number differs from its plan row has no number alias in sourceIds`, `buildWorkItemGraph: unit is null for a missing head and has status unmigrated for a head with no lifecycle`, `a missing or unmigrated unit raises needs-migration and not pending-decision`, `gate sorts tasks by taskOrder then id`, `storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head, and an approved BUILD otherwise stays build-recorded with text giving the head's status, that it is not migrated, or that there is no head`, `board-details joins on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null`, `board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status`, `TaskRowView carries a Task's unit status, including unmigrated`, `the storage helper: a first write gets a draft lifecycle; a rewrite with unchanged content keeps the lifecycle; a rewrite with changed content gets a draft and keeps Signoff entries, with no Signoff entries and with them`\n  - Fixtures: `src/workflow/__tests__/lifecycle-fixtures.ts`, `in-memory delivery records as in src/workflow/delivery/__tests__`\n- **integration** — Real store writes through approval, first write and repair.\n  - Subjects: `handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD: the outcome merges the approval's own followOn with the seam's, and the Story, its Tasks and its Epic complete`, `a walk failure leaves the approval standing and reports ok false`, `a live approval with a listed Task missing its head is held and named in the note`, `initial approval held, then re-approval with an override records it and completes the Story, then a failure injected in that completion is finished by a later re-approval using the stored override`, `a held Story in signoff completes later from the stored override`, `an Epic with a signoff hold stays open after its Story completes`, `the CLI adapter exposes the story-completion outcome`, `both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle`, `guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle`, `repair-preview writes nothing, and the changes 'repair' applies are the ones the preview listed, including proposed head creation and settlement`, `repair on a store with an uppercase head holding body.feedback and an approved flat amendment: the head is renamed, the feedback survives under the new id, and the amendment stays approved`, `repair on an already converted repository creates missing EPIC, STORY, TASKS and TASK heads, including from a PLAN at a status beyond approved`, `repair with crossed Task numbers and plan rows gives each BUILD result to the Task with that planTaskId and leaves existing rounds alone, before the live rule settles the Story`, `repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override`, `repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed and lists it in result.held`, `a failure injected in the head migration step answers a RepairReport with stoppedAt, applied and remaining and settles nothing, and the next run finishes with no feedback line added twice`, `a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit`, `a TASKS head listing a missing Task is reported failed and not settled`, `a plan with a rename collision answers an error and writes nothing`, `a second repair lists no changes`, `an unknown mode answers an error and writes nothing`, `verifyConversion keeps passing on a converted fixture with the changed loader, graph and gates`\n  - Fixtures: `a temporary repository with a seeded .insrc/artifacts store`\n- **contract** — The daemon and plugin agree on the new board fields and labels.\n  - Subjects: `src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts carries unit (including status unmigrated), planRowId, taskOrder, unmigrated and needs-migration through the snapshot`, `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/delivery-client.test.ts reads the same shape`\n- **smoke** — The Task status renders in the real board webview.\n  - Subjects: `Render the board webview during the build and confirm a Task row shows its unit status, including an unmigrated one`\n\n**Acceptance mapping**\n\n| Criterion | Proving tests |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `ac1` | `liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and a valid DIAG with no notice`, `buildWorkItemGraph: TASKS-listed membership, withdrawn and superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, unit, planRowId and taskOrder`, `the contract tests carry the new fields` |\n| `ac2` | `handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and its Epic`, `storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head`, `board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status` |\n| `ac3` | `rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it`, `a live approval with a listed Task missing its head is held and named in the note`, `initial approval held, then re-approval with an override records it and completes the Story`, `a held Story leaves every Task unchanged` |\n| `ac4` | `both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle`, `the storage helper: a rewrite never leaves a head with no lifecycle`, `guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle` |\n| `ac5` | `repair on an already converted repository creates missing heads`, `repair on a store with an uppercase head holding body.feedback and an approved flat amendment`, `repair with crossed Task numbers and plan rows`, `repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override`, `repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed`, `verifyConversion keeps passing on a converted fixture` |\n| `ac6` | `repair-preview writes nothing, and the changes 'repair' applies are the ones the preview listed`, `a second repair lists no changes`, `a failure injected in the head migration step answers a RepairReport, and the next run finishes`, `a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit` |\n\n## 6. Migration\n\n**State before:** No unit ever reaches completed: the walk in src/workflow/gates.ts:959 starts at the STORY, rollUp (src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336) needs every Task completed, and nothing completes a Task. The store has EPIC 53 draft, STORY 250 draft, TASK 1,972 approved and 42 draft, and 252 approved builds have no STORY head. A second approval of an approved BUILD records nothing (src/workflow/gates.ts:690). Two sources leave heads with no lifecycle. First, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93 and src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349 still write a new head without one, and src/workflow/storage.ts:178 only reconciles a lifecycle the next head carries; 4 records created on 2026-11-09 and awaiting approval have none (3 ISSUE, 1 LLD). Second, the installed daemon ran commit 5c5bc0cf1 from main, which has no lifecycle code, until 2026-11-07. In all, 273 records have no lifecycle, and 152 heads have an uppercase Story id. The board (src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35) admits neither EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS nor DIAG, and storyStage calls any approved BUILD complete. planConversion (src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121) does nothing at schema version 2, so a converted repository cannot be repaired.\n\n**State after:** Approving a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and, when every declared Story is done, its Epic, or reports why not. A Task whose latest round failed, or that is unfinished, holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override, which can be recorded after the first approval and is kept with an audit entry. Every workflow head has a lifecycle from its first write and through any rewrite. Repair brings existing records into the common model and settles units at any schema version, and is previewable, re-runnable and reports each step. The board reads the status of Epics, Stories and Tasks from their heads, labels anything not yet migrated, and no longer calls an approved BUILD complete on its own.\n\n**Zero downtime:** no — **Data rewrite:** yes\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Ship the code: the completion rule, the record-override operation, the first-write lifecycle, the follow-on merge, the board's new kinds and fields, and the repair modes. Write COMPLETION_RULE_FROM as a fixed UTC timestamp in that commit. — ↩ rollbackable\n2. Update and restart the daemon, and release the plugin with the new fields and labels. — ↩ rollbackable\n3. Run repair-preview on the repository and read the plan, including the renames and the Stories it would settle. — ↩ rollbackable\n4. Make sure no workflow is writing to the repository, then copy .insrc/artifacts and the docs folder aside. Repair renames files and rewrites references, so this copy is the way back. — ↩ rollbackable\n5. Run repair, with the steps in order: rename ids and files, stamp, convert flat amendments, save body.feedback, migrate heads, create missing EPIC and STORY heads, create missing TASKS and TASK heads, move Story history, settle units. — ✕ non-rollbackable\n6. Read result.applied, remaining, stoppedAt, held and failed. Re-run repair after a stop or a failed unit that can finish, and act by hand on those it cannot. — ✕ non-rollbackable\n7. Open the board and confirm that no record still raises needs-migration, then commit the changed store. — ↩ rollbackable\n\n**Backward compat:** New fields on the board's types, FollowOnOutcome, the new lifecycle operation and the repair modes are additive. The existing preview and apply modes of repo.convert and the schema marker are unchanged. handleWorkflowApprove now returns the approval's own outcomes and the seam's together instead of only the seam's. A second approval of an approved BUILD with a new override now records it, where before it did nothing. A consumer of the operation list sees one more operation. applyTasks no longer matches a BUILD result on a Task's number or id; every Task in this store has a planTaskId. An older plugin against the new daemon ignores the new fields but will see Stories it used to call complete shown as build-recorded until repair settles them. The STORY rule deliberately diverges from S007:FR001: a Task completes with its Story rather than before it, so a held Story cannot be hidden by an earlier Task status. Heads written by a daemon on main still have no lifecycle; the board labels them needs-migration and repair handles them. writeArtifact itself is unchanged. Steps 5 and 6 cannot be rolled back automatically; restoring the copy made in step 4 undoes them.\n\n## 7. Alternatives considered\n\n### 7.1 a1: Tasks complete with their Story at BUILD approval — **CHOSEN**\n\nAt BUILD approval a Story completes, with all its open Tasks, when every Task it lists has a latest round that passed or the approval carries an explicit override.\n\nThe Story roll-up reads the Tasks the TASKS head lists and each one's latest build round rather than its status. When the rule holds, completing the Story freezes its open Tasks through the cascade; when it does not, the Story and its Tasks stay as they are, and the outcome names the Tasks. A later explicit override is saved on the approved BUILD by its own audited operation. New records carry a draft lifecycle from their first write. A repair mode runs the conversion's ordered steps at any schema version, then settles units, applying the old approval rule only to approvals older than the new one. The board publishes unit status, a plan row key and an order.\n\n### 7.2 a2: Complete passing Tasks first, then roll up\n\nBUILD approval completes each passing Task, then rolls up the Story by Task status.\n\nWalk each counted Task so passing ones complete, then roll up the Story by Task status, reopening a completed Task when a later round fails. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\n\n**Rejected because:** Partial on status-is-reliable: a Task completed before its Story can be hidden by a later failing round, and it would need its own reopen path.\n\n### 7.3 a3: Any approved BUILD completes the Story\n\nA Story completes on an approved BUILD with a clean or overridden review, whatever its Tasks show.\n\nDrop the Task condition from the Story roll-up and cascade to all open Tasks. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\n\n**Rejected because:** Violates failed-task-holds-story: any approved BUILD would complete a Story with a failed Task.\n\n## 8. References\n\n- **[[c1]]** `code` `src/workflow/gates.ts:959`\n- **[[c2]]** `code` `src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336`\n- **[[c3]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts:29`\n- **[[c4]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts`\n- **[[c5]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121`\n- **[[c6]]** `code` `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35`\n- **[[c7]]** `doc` `docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md`\n- **[[c8]]** `prior-artifact` `docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md`\n- **[[c9]]** `doc` `docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md`\n- **[[c10]]** `doc` `/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon` — \"git reflog: 756d5adf4 HEAD@{2026-11-07 17:54:07 +0530} checkout: moving from main to v2\"\n- **[[c11]]** `code` `src/workflow/gates.ts:690`\n- **[[c12]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126`\n"},"capturedAt":"2026-11-09T13:17:25.557Z"},"inventory":{"units":[{"id":"/body/summary","selector":"/body/summary","title":"summary","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/hldContextSlice","selector":"/body/hldContextSlice","title":"hldContextSlice","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/contractDetails","selector":"/body/contractDetails","title":"contractDetails","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/dataModelChanges","selector":"/body/dataModelChanges","title":"dataModelChanges","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/interactionWithShared","selector":"/body/interactionWithShared","title":"interactionWithShared","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/errorPaths","selector":"/body/errorPaths","title":"errorPaths","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/testStrategy","selector":"/body/testStrategy","title":"testStrategy","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/migration","selector":"/body/migration","title":"migration","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered","title":"alternativesConsidered","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/chosenAlternative","selector":"/body/chosenAlternative","title":"chosenAlternative","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/openQuestions","selector":"/body/openQuestions","title":"openQuestions","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","title":"a1","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","title":"a2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","title":"a3","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/citations/0","selector":"/citations/0","title":"Citation 1","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/1","selector":"/citations/1","title":"Citation 2","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/2","selector":"/citations/2","title":"Citation 3","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/3","selector":"/citations/3","title":"Citation 4","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/4","selector":"/citations/4","title":"Citation 5","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/5","selector":"/citations/5","title":"Citation 6","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/6","selector":"/citations/6","title":"Citation 7","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/7","selector":"/citations/7","title":"Citation 8","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/8","selector":"/citations/8","title":"Citation 9","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/9","selector":"/citations/9","title":"Citation 10","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/10","selector":"/citations/10","title":"Citation 11","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/11","selector":"/citations/11","title":"Citation 12","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:24","selector":"document:line:24","title":"1. HLD context","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned scope sections align with the originating ISSUE and applicable common-model requirements. Recorded owner decisions support real unit status and explicit overrides for failed or unfinished Tasks. The design addresses lifecycle preservation, repeatable repair and reporting, preserves the issue’s exclusions, and correctly claims no parent HLD. No blocking scope or traceability defects were found.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","document:line:24","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-eedc4519199b24b4.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md — functional requirements, constraints k3/k8, acceptance ac7–ac10 and ac27–ac29","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — completion, revision and conversion requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:310","src/workflow/storage.ts:175","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:218","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:404","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:433"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"completion","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Reviewed all assigned selectors against the issue, owner decisions, applicable common-model requirements and current implementation. Two gaps remain in partial Task creation and durable-override retry behavior.","findings":[{"id":"completion-r4-001","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:218","message":"storyTasks treats existing child TASK heads as a complete listing whenever TASKS is absent, even with an approved PLAN. Task creation writes individual heads first and TASKS last, so an interrupted creation can leave only part of the planned set. If those existing Tasks have passing rounds, the proposed rule completes the Story without an override while uncreated plan Tasks disappear from the condition. Distinguish an incomplete set from a verified complete set before using this fallback, and cover partial creation with at least one existing Task.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §3.1 CompletionEvidence: child-head fallback precedes the approved-PLAN not-created condition","LLD.md §2.1 and §4: unfinished Task creation must hold completion without an override","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:148-183: createFromPlan writes TASK heads sequentially and the TASKS completion marker last","LLD.md §5: proposed incomplete-creation test covers zero Task heads but not a partial set","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md: unfinished Tasks require an explicit BUILD approval override"]},{"id":"completion-r4-002","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:227","message":"The durable-override design updates the approval writer and completion evidence, but leaves the preceding approveWorkflowTarget code-review gate without a stored-override contract. That gate passes only req.overrideReview and skips the artifact on a blocked review before reaching either approveArtifactByJsonPath or completeThroughService. Consequently, an approval made over review findings followed by interrupted completion cannot be retried through normal re-approval using only its stored override, as the design promises. Specify how this outer gate recognizes a current standing BUILD approval and its persisted override, and test the retry with an actually blocking task-based review and no override in the retry request.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §3.2: overrides must remain usable after request context is gone","LLD.md §4: re-approval finishes a failed completion without undoing the committed approval","LLD.md §5 integration: later re-approval must recover using the stored override","src/workflow/gates.ts:974-986: enforceCodeReviewGate receives only the request override and returns early on blocked","src/workflow/gates.ts:994-1010: approval and completion occur only after that outer gate","src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts:14-27: a blocking task-review gap is overridden only by the supplied option","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: storedOverride is consumed downstream of the rejecting gate"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/10","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: common-model constraints and S007 requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/approval-view.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts: operation validation","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: child discovery","src/workflow/gates.ts: approval gates and completion hook","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: Task creation and membership","src/workflow/storage.ts: lifecycle reconciliation and Signoff preservation","src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts: production content write","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts: production content write","src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts","src/cli/services/workflow.ts: approval outcome adapter","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: deferred completion","src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/storage-signoff-history.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/approve-build-freshness.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/completion-evidence.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-members.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"repair","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the issue, applicable common-model requirements and conversion code. Repair ordering, historical eligibility and Task identity handling are specified, but partial-write reporting and rollback remain defective.","findings":[{"id":"repair-r4-001","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:257","message":"Computing applied changes solely by subtracting the remaining plan cannot accurately report committed writes. applyFeedback appends sidecar records while leaving body.feedback intact; feedbackRule therefore reports exactly the same change after those writes. If feedback or subsequent head migration fails, the proposed report omits feedback already committed. Similarly, tasksRule stops listing a Story once TASKS exists, although applyTasks can still backfill missing rounds, including after an interrupted run. Specify sidecar-aware planning and granular write accounting, or collect actual phase results. Add failure tests asserting that committed feedback, migration log entries and Task rounds appear accurately in applied/remaining and retry previews.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §3.5: applied is every planned change absent from the recomputed plan","LLD.md §2.6 and §4: preview fidelity and reporting of writes before failure","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts:88 — feedbackRule examines body.feedback without checking existing sidecar records","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts:114 — applyFeedback appends records and strips nothing","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts: writeMigratedHead appends log entries before replacing the head","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:64 — tasksRule skips existing TASKS heads","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:82 — applyTasks backfills rounds even when TASKS already exists","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-feedback-rule.test.ts: interrupted append and head-replacement fixtures"]},{"id":"repair-r4-002","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:428","message":"The stated rollback restores only .insrc/artifacts and docs, but repair's unit creation and settlement also stage durable operations under .insrc/journal. A failed write can leave a pending operation outside that backup. After restoring the prescribed copy, the next lifecycle write can replay the repair operation when the restored head matches its prior hash, or encounter a persistent conflict when it does not. Thus restoring this copy does not reliably undo repair as §6 promises. Include journal state in the quiesced backup/restore procedure and define removal of repair-created pending operations before restarting writers. Cover rollback after a staged write fails before head replacement.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §6 steps 4–6 and Backward compat: restoring the step-4 copy is claimed to undo repair","src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts:32 — JOURNAL_DIR is .insrc/journal","src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-lifecycle.ts: createRepoLifecycle installs the durable file journal","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts:371 — staging precedes log append and head replacement","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts:410 — completePending replays staged operations or raises a head conflict","src/workflow/convert/units.ts: applyUnits creates heads through ArtifactStore.write"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9","/citations/11","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md: migration requirements and recorded conversion decisions","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts","src/workflow/convert/run.ts","src/workflow/convert/rename.ts","src/workflow/convert/stamps.ts","src/workflow/convert/amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/story-history.ts","src/workflow/convert/marker.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: readPlan and createFromPlan","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar-store.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: durable writes and pending-operation recovery","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts: rollUp and unitMembers","src/workflow/gates.ts: approved-or-beyond approval handling","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-feedback-rule.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: git reflog confirming the cited main-to-v2 checkout"],"limitations":[],"advice":["When implementing PLAN eligibility beyond approved, account for TaskSets.readPlan's current approved-only guard and test creation from signed-off and completed PLANs."]},{"chunkId":"board","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the originating ISSUE, applicable common-model and delivery requirements, and current daemon/client code. Unit status, migration labeling and Task identity contracts are substantially specified, but BUILD-only validation preservation and DIAG evidence reads have end-to-end gaps.","findings":[{"id":"board-r4-001","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:184","message":"The proposed task derivation uses TASKS membership, otherwise PLAN rows, without preserving BUILD-only validation entries. With no TASKS head, a PLAN containing t1 and a BUILD containing failed t3 would omit t3 entirely. The current gate computes validation and conflicts by walking graph task children, so this removes the unplanned result, failed count and potentially the validation-conflict signal. Preserve unmatched BUILD evidence independently of authoritative active-task membership, and test both PLAN-plus-extra-BUILD and BUILD-without-PLAN cases.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.9: tasks come from TASKS when present, otherwise PLAN","LLD §3.8: validation remains sourced from BUILD","LLD §5: membership tests omit BUILD-only validation regression cases","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts: addTasks currently collects PLAN and BUILD task ids","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts: storyValidation derives task results and conflicts through story.childIds","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts:284 — unmatched BUILD results remain visible as unplanned","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts:362 — BUILD tasks without PLAN remain visible","docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/DEF.md:156 — S003 ac4 requires unmatched BUILD results and unplanned marking"]},{"id":"board-r4-002","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:189","message":"DIAG is added as Story evidence, but the design does not extend the evidence-read handler's artifact-id validation. Its regex permits only one suffix after the hash, whereas valid DIAG ids contain both Story and sequence suffixes, such as DIAG-aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa-s1-2. Adding DIAG to the loader's kind list therefore displays an evidence row whose read action still returns 'invalid artifact id'. Specify kind-aware validation for this endpoint and add a client/handler test opening a valid sequenced DIAG while retaining invalid-id and containment checks.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.9 and §3.7: DIAG heads become Story evidence","LLD §5: DIAG coverage currently checks loader admission rather than evidence retrieval","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:85 — DIAG requires Story and sequence","src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-ids.test.ts:42 — valid DIAG id has two suffixes","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts: ARTIFACT_ID_RE allows only one suffix","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts:110 — handleDeliveryEvidence rejects ids before reading the record","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts:124 — evidence actions call workflow.deliveryEvidence"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/5","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json — inventory and completed dependency chunks","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md — common-model requirements and completion constraints","docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0df