cy and meaningful unit/integration coverage.","Freshly reassess completion-r4-001 and completion-r4-002 without presuming their resolution."],"dependsOn":["scope"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"repair","title":"Repair planning, committed-write accounting and recovery","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9","/citations/11"],"concerns":["Inspect repair-preview and repair at every schema version while preserving existing conversion modes, progress behavior and schema-marker semantics.","Check ordered prerequisites across renames, stamps, amendments, feedback, head migration, units, Tasks, Story history and settlement.","Inspect RepairRecorder propagation and commit boundaries for feedback lines, migration and batch log entries, heads and Task rounds; verify written remains accurate after failures and remaining accurately describes retry work.","Check planner visibility of backfill-round and settle-unit changes, including existing TASKS heads, proposed head creation and preview/write correspondence.","Inspect createFromPlan acceptLaterStatus, default approved-only behavior for live callers and reconcile, partial-set recovery, missing members, revision mismatches and per-Story failure isolation.","Verify planTaskId-only BUILD joins, preservation of existing rounds, fixed historical cutoff and attributed migration overrides versus the live completion rule.","Check idempotency, collisions, feedback preservation, stopped-step behavior, completedMembers, dependent-step stopping and conversion-verification regression coverage.","Assess deployment order and quiesced backup/restore of artifacts, journal and docs, including staged-write failure recovery and pending-operation replay.","Freshly reassess repair-r4-001 and repair-r4-002 without presuming their resolution."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"board","title":"Common-model board derivation, evidence access and client presentation","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/5"],"concerns":["Inspect loader coverage of common-model kinds, DIAG Story ownership, lifecycle-only approval and the explicit TESTS exclusion.","Check endpoints, direction, cardinality and ownership among EPIC, STORY, TASKS, TASK, DIAG and work items.","Inspect TASKS-authoritative active membership, PLAN fallback, withdrawn/superseded exclusion, planRowId joins, sourceIds collision avoidance and taskOrder propagation.","Verify unmatched BUILD results remain visible and contribute validation/conflict signals without becoming active Tasks or false migration notices; inspect PLAN-plus-extra-BUILD and BUILD-without-PLAN tests.","Trace TASK and sequenced DIAG evidence reads through kind-aware identifier validation, legacy uppercase compatibility, containment, handler contracts and client actions.","Trace UnitStatus including unmigrated, null-for-absent-head semantics, migration notices and pending-decision exclusion through graph, gates, snapshots and clients.","Check complete versus build-recorded derivation, Epic progress, Task lifecycle status beside BUILD validation and consistency with latest-round completion evidence.","Inspect daemon and current IDE consumer contracts, including VS Code details, labels and webview source; impose no deprecated insrc-ide requirements.","Assess necessary relationship and UX artifacts, inspect linked renderings if present, and distinguish available design evidence from the planned implementation smoke test.","Freshly reassess board-r4-001 and board-r4-002 and verify unchanged board and conversion-verification behavior."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Fresh whole-design consistency and finding reconciliation","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile every substantive assessment against the originating ISSUE, applicable upstream requirements and recorded owner decisions.","Check end-to-end agreement among membership completeness, persisted overrides, revision handling, repair reconstruction, committed-write reporting, rollback and board status.","Check acceptance mapping, contracts, errors, ownership, dependency order, deployment compatibility and citations across the live document and canonical artifact.","Reconcile all six carried findings only after fresh inspection, using their canonical provenance keys.","Check necessary visual inspection and coverage declarations; distinguish demonstrated defects, limitations and optional advice and enforce the required status precedence."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 28 current inventory units are assigned to substantive chunks, including the newly added /citations/12. The four implementation responsibilities and dependency order from attempt 4 remain intact. Broad contract, data-model, error and test selectors intentionally overlap so each responsibility retains its interfaces, logic, failure handling and verification. The originating ISSUE is the workflow ancestor; applicable common-model and delivery designs are supporting requirements, not invented Epic/HLD ancestry. All substantive chunks receive fresh review, followed by fresh final consistency. No prior chunk is retained or represented as newly reviewed. The current canonical body has no visual-definition fields, and the subject directory contains LLD.md and DECISIONS.md; the board chunk must independently assess visual sufficiency and inspect any linked artifacts it discovers.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","ch