d in the completion assessment.","Relationship prose adequately describes the proposed ownership and cardinality. No visual verification is claimed; the specified webview rendering check belongs to implementation validation. Proposed tests were assessed, not executed."],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":4,"chunkId":"completion","findingId":"completion-r4-001"},"rationale":"The current storyTasks contract treats an approved-or-later PLAN without a finished TASKS head as not-created even when partial TASK heads exist. Edge cases and tests explicitly cover a partial set whose existing Tasks passed. This resolves the original absent-TASKS defect; the distinct stale-listing defect remains recorded as completion-r5-001.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:276 — approved PLAN takes precedence over child-head fallback when TASKS is absent","LLD.md:424","LLD.md:469","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan publishes TASKS last","Checkpoint attempt 5 completedChunks: completion"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["completion","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":4,"chunkId":"completion","findingId":"completion-r4-002"},"rationale":"The design now supplies the persisted override to the outer code-review gate for a standing approved-or-later BUILD, excludes draft revisions and requires a retry test with an actually blocking review and no request override.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §2.3 — approveWorkflowTarget","LLD.md §3.2 — persisted override consumers","LLD.md:427–428","LLD.md:472","src/workflow/gates.ts:974–1010","Checkpoint attempt 5 completedChunks: completion"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["completion","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":4,"chunkId":"repair","findingId":"repair-r4-001"},"rationale":"RepairReport now records committed writes directly instead of inferring them by plan subtraction. Its recorder covers feedback lines, migration and batch entries, heads and rounds; remaining explicitly represents retry planning. Existing TAS