nflicting-status and re-plan fixtures requested by board-01 and board-02 as end-to-end acceptance evidence after repair.","Replace or define the ac1–ac7 labels in the acceptance mapping; neither the originating ISSUE nor the LLD provides their criterion text. Include explicit traceability for writer investigation and recurrence prevention.","No authored diagram definitions or rendered companions were supplied. The relationship prose can suffice; no visual verification is claimed. Live repair and implementation tests were appropriately left for implementation validation."]}],"progress":{"status":"incomplete","phase":"complete","completedChunks":5,"totalChunks":5,"lastMeaningfulActivityAt":null,"activeToolCount":0,"requiresUserInput":false,"checkpointPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","sequence":0,"reviewElapsedMs":0,"unitElapsedMs":null,"observedAt":"2026-11-09T10:03:07.127Z","freshness":"stored"},"startedAt":"2026-11-09T09:54:08.854Z","reviewer":"daemon","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","unit":{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","executionId":"95c7985b-feed-48c3-b698-89d72ce08a1d","dispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[]},"plan":{"chunks":[{"id":"scope","title":"Issue traceability, scope and chosen approach","selectors":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:24","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/5","/citations/6"],"concerns":["Read the originating ISSUE and compare reproduction, root cause, fix intent, requirements, acceptance criteria and non-goals with the current LLD and canonical artifact.","Assess the chosen completion model and rejected alternatives against the issue; resolve applicability of standalone context without inventing HLD ancestry.","Inspect stakeholder citation provenance and whether unresolved questions affect implementation feasibility."],"dependsOn":[],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"completion","title":"Live lifecycle completion and approval integration","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/3"],"concerns":["Inspect rollUp, CompletionEvidence, completeIfRolledUp and completeThroughService against current lifecycle, approval, evidence and cascade code.","Check current BUILD selection, review and override evidence, missing-head creation, signoff holds, reopened units, terminal child states and Epic aggregation.","Verify interface and error-result consistency, approval preservation, retry behavior, identity normalization and tests for the complete live approval path.","Assess shared contracts and necessary relationship or interaction artifacts, inspecting generated files and actual renderings where available."],"dependsOn":["scope"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"repair","title":"Repeatable repair, conversion compatibility and rollout","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/1","/citations/4"],"concerns":["Inspect handleRepoConvert, conversion planning, existing repair helpers and lifecycle settlement contracts.","Check lifecycle reconstruction, approval preservation, missing unit creation, historical review treatment, reopened work and identity normalization.","Assess preview purity, idempotence, interrupted-run recovery, unreadable heads, head/log conflicts, report contents and schema-version independence.","Verify ordering, rollback feasibility, unchanged preview/apply behavior and test coverage for repair and conversion verification."],"dependsOn":["completion"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"board","title":"Delivery loading, work-item graph and client contracts","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2"],"concerns":["Inspect loader, delivery types, graph construction, gate classification and daemon snapshot consumers against the proposed common artifact model.","Check Epic/Story/Task ownership and cardinality, TASKS handling, normalized identities, head status precedence, task ordering and exclusion of unit heads from evidence.","Verify unmigrated and missing-head behavior, needs-migration attention, lifecycle-only status reading and conversion parity.","Inspect applicable VS Code and JetBrains IPC contracts, labels and rendering behavior; assess necessary UX artifacts and actual renderings where available.","Check loader, graph, gate, client contract and live acceptance coverage."],"dependsOn":["completion","repair"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Whole-artifact consistency and upstream alignment","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile every originating ISSUE requirement and acceptance criterion with the assessed contracts, repair behavior, board behavior and proving tests.","Check cross-chunk contradictions, shared identities and statuses, error propagation, rollout dependencies and repository conventions.","Confirm citations and relevant authored/generated artifacts support the design, and distinguish demonstrated defects from mandatory inspection limitations and optional advice."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"Every inventory unit maps to at least one substantive chunk. Shared contract, model, error and test sections are assigned to each implementation responsibility that must inspect them. Migration is shared by repair and delivery rollout. The final consistency chunk reconciles these assessments without replacing substantive coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["completion","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["board"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"document:line:24","chunkIds":["scope"]}]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"planning","phase":"planning","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"completion","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"repair","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"board","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"delivery-board-lld-s1","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":3,"MED":5,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"incomplete","summary":"The LLD addresses the issue's main loading, migration and lifecycle-status goals, and correctly treats this as standalone issue work without requiring HLD ancestry. However, the chosen completion model changes an applicable Task completion rule without reconciling that change, and stakeholder provenance could not be independently verified.","findings":[{"id":"scope-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","message":"The chosen model completes every open Task when the Story BUILD is approved with a clean or overridden code review, even when a Task's latest build failed. The applicable common-model design requires each Task to pass its gate and says rejected or unfinished children count against Story completion. The originating ISSUE requests accurate lifecycle status and repair, but does not explicitly replace these completion requirements. Although the LLD acknowledges changing the roll-up rule, it does not reconcile the upstream requirement or distinguish an ordinary clean code review from explicit authorization to override failed Task evidence. Define that policy change and its recorded override requirements, or preserve Task completion gating.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:282-294",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json#/body/alternativesConsidered/0/cons","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:84-90","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:196","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md#Fix intent"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:24","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/5","/citations/6","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-eedc4519199b24b4.json","docs/plans/core-data-model.md","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/gates.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts"],"limitations":["Stakeholder provenance for /citations/6 could not be independently verified. It names a user decision dated 2026-11-09 but supplies no message identifier, transcript path, quotation or linked decision record. The supplied context and located issue/LLD records do not establish the decision's exact scope, particularly whether it authorized completing failed Tasks through ordinary BUILD approval."],"advice":["Retain the standalone context clarification; the generated HLD metadata and section heading do not establish actual HLD ancestry.","Add a source reference for the historical daemon attribution used to close the originating issue's writer-investigation requirement. The cited commit has no artifact-core directory, but that alone does not establish which deployed process produced every affected record."]},{"chunkId":"completion","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The live completion design has three implementation gaps: the existing cascade excludes Tasks, completion failures lack a return contract, and missing sibling Story heads can cause premature Epic completion.","findings":[{"id":"completion-01","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/1/postconditions","message":"The promised completion of open Tasks cannot use the existing cascade as specified. unitMembers includes Story records, TASKS and DIAG, but explicitly excludes TASK heads; existing tests confirm Tasks complete independently. Changing Story rollUp therefore allows the Story and Epic to complete while their Tasks remain open. Specify the Task cascade changes, including terminal-state exclusions, history attribution, reopen behavior and recovery after partial failure. The integration test should assert individual TASK lifecycles and logs.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:74","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts#unitMembers","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts#applyInQueue","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts#completeMember","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts:59","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts:109"]},{"id":"completion-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/0/response","message":"The error path promises that a completion failure is returned with the successful approval, but completeThroughService returns void and declares no errors or result data. Neither ApprovalResult nor WorkflowApproveResult currently has a completion outcome, and the current caller simply awaits the helper. Catching and logging would hide the failure; propagating it would prevent the caller receiving the successful approval result. Define an additive completion outcome and its propagation, and test that the caller receives both the standing approval and the failure details.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:79","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:187","src/workflow/gates.ts:545","src/workflow/gates.ts:881","src/workflow/gates.ts:956","src/workflow/gates.ts:1010"]},{"id":"completion-03","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/2/postconditions","message":"Ensuring only the approved BUILD's Story and Epic heads is insufficient before retaining the existing Epic roll-up. The originating issue documents missing STORY heads for Stories listed in DEF. Current Epic roll-up counts only existing heads discovered through parent links. If an Epic declares two Stories but only the approved Story has a head, this walk can complete the Epic and freeze DEF/HLD while the other Story remains unfinished. Before aggregation, establish all declared Story heads or explicitly block completion on missing declared members. Include this mixed existing/missing sibling case in the approval integration tests.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:44","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:93","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md#Root cause","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts#countedChildren","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts#rollUp","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts#scanChildren","src/workflow/convert/units.ts#applyUnits"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/3","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/HLD.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S003/LLD.md","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/approval-view.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts","src/workflow/gates.ts","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/completion.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/gates-lifecycle-service.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Expand the lifecycle test matrix to explicitly cover approval with a persisted review override followed by deferred signoff settlement, reopened BUILD records, normalized S001 identities, and withdrawn or superseded Tasks.","The relationship prose can suffice for these changes. No diagram definitions, companions or renderings were supplied in the canonical artifact or subject directory; no visual verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"repair","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The repair intent matches the issue, but the LLD leaves repair reporting and reconstruction rules insufficiently defined for the promised repeatability and coverage.","findings":[{"id":"repair-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/3","message":"The new modes return ConversionReport, but that contract currently permits only preview/apply. ConversionChange has no settlement rule, and ConversionResult has no runtime repair-problem collection. The LLD changes none of these types while promising previewed completion changes, per-unit conflict reporting and a second-run report with no changes. Define the additive report contracts and distinguish planned, successfully applied, held and failed changes; otherwise callers cannot reliably determine what repair actually accomplished.","evidenceReferences":["src/workflow/convert/types.ts#ConversionReport","src/workflow/convert/types.ts#ConversionRule","src/workflow/convert/types.ts#ConversionResult","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts#applyConversion","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts#handleRepoConvert","/body/errorPaths/errorCases/3","/body/migration/migrationSteps/4"]},{"id":"repair-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/migration/migrationSteps/3","message":"The reconstruction step promises missing units, including standalone work, without defining discovery and eligibility rules that cover them. Existing unitsRule/applyUnits discover Epics and Stories only from DEF, so they cannot reconstruct standalone work without DEF. Existing task reconstruction selects only PLAN status approved, excluding completed Plans, and createFromPlan returns immediately for an existing TASKS head at the same revision rather than restoring a missing TASK. Specify how repair discovers standalone ownership, handles completed Plans and reconciles incomplete existing task sets while preserving identities and terminal states. Add fixtures for these cases; the stated generic missing-TASKS test does not establish this coverage.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md#Fix intent","src/workflow/convert/units.ts#epicsOf","src/workflow/convert/units.ts#applyUnits","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts#plannedStories","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts#readPlan","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts#createFromPlan","/body/testStrategy/testLevels/1"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/1","/citations/4","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S009/LLD.md","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts","src/workflow/convert/run.ts","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/raw-heads.ts","src/workflow/convert/backfill.ts","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/rename.ts","src/workflow/convert/legacy-view.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-repeat.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-lifecycle-backfill.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Expand repair tests to cover unreadable heads, head/log conflicts, reopened work, normalized identities and interruption during settlement. The existing lifecycle service can complete earlier members before a later member fails, so recovery assertions should inspect individual heads and logs.","The assigned repair contracts can be explained adequately through prose and tables. No diagram definitions or rendered companions are supplied in the subject directory; no visual verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"board","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The loader extension addresses the reported unknown kinds, but the design does not define how lifecycle status reaches the published snapshot and UI, or how Task identities and ordering survive re-planning.","findings":[{"id":"board-01","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/5","message":"The graph promises to carry unit status, but no WorkItemNode or DeliveryItem field, snapshot propagation, stage precedence or client rendering contract is defined. Currently storyStage marks any approved BUILD complete, the plugin derives Epic completion from child stages, and Task rows display validation results. Consequently a held, reopened or missing STORY head can still appear complete, and Epic/Task lifecycle status cannot reach the UI through the specified changes. Define the published head/status representation, its precedence over BUILD-derived completion, missing-head behavior, and Epic/Task display behavior. Extend snapshot and client tests with deliberately conflicting BUILD and unit statuses; graph assertions and enum-label checks alone do not prove the originating issue's lifecycle-source requirement.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md#Fix intent","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:140","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:278","src/workflow/delivery/types.ts#WorkItemNode","src/workflow/delivery/types.ts#DeliveryItem","src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts#storyStage","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts#assembleSnapshot","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts#leastAdvancedStage","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts#taskRows"]},{"id":"board-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/5/postconditions","message":"Taking Task title and order from TASK heads is insufficient to join those heads to PLAN/BUILD evidence. Task artifact numbers differ from plan row ids after re-planning: the existing reconcile test maps row t9 to TASK t4 and later returning row t3 to TASK t5 while the old TASK t3 remains withdrawn. The current graph and gate join by numeric task id, and the client joins plan details through sourceIds; all would need explicit mapping through TaskPayload.planTaskId. Ordering also currently gets sorted by task number in the graph and gate, rather than TaskPayload.order. Specify TASKS membership, active versus withdrawn Task handling, row-to-artifact mapping, and preservation of execution order through snapshot and client rendering. Add a re-plan fixture proving correct status, validation, dependencies and order without duplicate synthetic tasks.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:144","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts#TaskPayload","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts#TasksPayload","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts#reconcile","src/workflow/tasks/__tests__/task-set-reconcile.test.ts","src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts#taskHeadIdOf","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts#addTasks","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts#freeze","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts#storyValidation","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts#taskRows","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:413"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S007/LLD.md","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts","src/workflow/delivery/types.ts","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts","src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts","src/workflow/delivery/notice.ts","src/workflow/delivery/read.ts","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/contract.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/identity-contract.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/graph.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts","src/workflow/tasks/__tests__/task-set-reconcile.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-model.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/labels.test.ts","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Explicitly classify TASKS as structural membership data rather than an approval decision; its draft lifecycle should not introduce pending-decision attention.","No diagram definitions, companions or renderings are supplied in the canonical artifact or subject directory; no visual verification is claimed. Relationship prose can suffice, but the revised status contract should explain the visible states.","No current JetBrains workflow.delivery consumer was found. Preserve the shared sample snapshot contract test without adding a new JetBrains delivery feature to this fix.","The live repair acceptance run belongs to implementation validation and was not executed during this read-only design review."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Inspected the current LLD, originating ISSUE, canonical records and all four completed chunk assessments. Both subject fingerprints match the checkpoint baseline. The earlier findings collectively cover the demonstrated completion, reconstruction, reporting and board-contract gaps; no additional distinct blocking defect was identified. Provenance verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-eedc4519199b24b4.json","checkpoint completedChunks: scope, completion, repair, board","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:84-90","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:196-207","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:300-390","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/gates.ts:950-1045","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/backfill.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts","git commit 5c5bc0cf189d2f4918411a9d6f6c1f8e7f6ce70d and its src/workflow/artifact-core tree entry","Subject S001 directory inventory: LLD.md only"],"limitations":["Citation c7's stakeholder decision could not be independently verified: no linked decision record or conversation evidence establishes whether the user authorized replacing individual Task completion gates. This preserves the provenance limitation reported by the scope chunk.","The originating ISSUE requires identifying the writer that omitted lifecycles and closing any surviving path. LLD.md:263 attributes the records to an installed daemon at commit 5c5bc0cf1, but supplies no deployment or writer evidence. That commit lacks artifact-core, which supports the explanation but does not establish which deployed process wrote the affected records or prove that recurrence paths are closed."],"advice":["Address scope-01 and completion-01 together: settle the Task completion policy before defining its cascade, history and recovery behavior.","Coordinate completion-03 with repair-02 so approval and repair use consistent Story membership and identity rules before Epic aggregation.","Resolve completion-02 and repair-01 through explicit result contracts that distinguish successful approval or repair from failed or held completion.","Use the conflicting-status and re-plan fixtures requested by board-01 and board-02 as end-to-end acceptance evidence after repair.","Replace or define the ac1–ac7 labels in the acceptance mapping; neither the originating ISSUE nor the LLD provides their criterion text. Include explicit traceability for writer investigation and recurrence prevention.","No authored diagram definitions or rendered companions were supplied. The relationship prose can suffice; no visual verification is claimed. Live repair and implementation tests were appropriately left for implementation validation."]}],"limitations":["Stakeholder provenance for /citations/6 could not be independently verified. It names a user decision dated 2026-11-09 but supplies no message identifier, transcript path, quotation or linked decision record. The supplied context and located issue/LLD records do not establish the decision's exact scope, particularly whether it authorized completing failed Tasks through ordinary BUILD approval.","Citation c7's stakeholder decision could not be independently verified: no linked decision record or conversation evidence establishes whether the user authorized replacing individual Task completion gates. This preserves the provenance limitation reported by the scope chunk.","The originating ISSUE requires identifying the writer that omitted lifecycles and closing any surviving path. LLD.md:263 attributes the records to an installed daemon at commit 5c5bc0cf1, but supplies no deployment or writer evidence. That commit lacks artifact-core, which supports the explanation but does not establish which deployed process wrote the affected records or prove that recurrence paths are closed."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"1c6308670f6b233a7745a95d4540dd26c2cdb4cddd46601c51619c779ddc35b2"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-09T10:03:07.127Z"},{"number":2,"status":"invalidated","preparationKind":"impact","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"1a688bd2ece3b5b7ddc2a2680530ebdd52eebcb630464d3633b165b50d27c0e0","document":"c82bd9a97becc223cc9619f7f583716ad1962dcdb4d2c6863f0d4aa1fdddfd9d"},"contentIdentity":"cfc97c117e676b2b0ccec199f96af87ffa4e0aa8999e5a1a78b3625b82097e12","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"design.story\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794219098430-hi9i5q\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-09T10:16:59.567Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-09T05:00:05.847Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-claude\",\n          \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 320894,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"eedc4519199b24b4\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact\",\n    \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n    \"hldBaseRunId\": \"wf-1794219098430-hi9i5q\",\n    \"hldEffectiveHash\": \"ee817330ed054e96f9e247f0eb148d270705dd334e94d67a21d7f43de8ee21a6\",\n    \"hldAmendmentsApplied\": [],\n    \"storyTitle\": \"Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\",\n    \"standalone\": true,\n    \"sizeClass\": \"bugfix\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"envelope\": {\n      \"attachments\": []\n    },\n    \"revision\": 2\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"audience\": \"product\",\n      \"prose\": \"Approving a build now really completes its Tasks and Story and, once every Story the Epic declares is done, the Epic, which never happened before. A Task whose build failed holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override. A repair run brings existing records up to date at any schema version and reports what it planned, did, held and could not do. The delivery board then shows Epic, Story and Task status from those records, and shows any record still in the old format as needing migration.\"\n    },\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\"\n      },\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {}\n    },\n    \"contractDetails\": {\n      \"surfaceLevel\": \"internal-shared\",\n      \"api\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"rollUp\",\n          \"signature\": \"rollUp(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader, evidence: CompletionEvidence): Promise<Status | undefined>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"id\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The TASK, STORY or EPIC head to evaluate\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reader\",\n              \"type\": \"ChildStatusReader\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Reads child listings and statuses\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"evidence\",\n              \"type\": \"CompletionEvidence\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Build, review, override and declared-Story facts\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<Status | undefined>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"'completed' when the condition holds. TASK: its latest build round passed (unchanged). STORY: its BUILD is approved, its review is clean or overridden, and every counted Task is completed, or the Story has no counted Tasks, or the approval carries an explicit override. EPIC: every counted Story is completed, and every Story its DEF declares has a head that is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"UnreadableChildError\",\n              \"condition\": \"A head of the counted child kind cannot be read\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"id parses as an artifact id\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Reads only\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"unitMembers\",\n          \"signature\": \"unitMembers(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader): Promise<string[]>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"id\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The unit\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reader\",\n              \"type\": \"ChildStatusReader\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Reads the unit's children\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<string[]>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"For a STORY, also its TASK children, so a Story completed by an override freezes its open Tasks\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"A member that is completed, withdrawn or superseded is left alone, as completeMember already does\",\n            \"Each frozen Task's log entry names the Story in frozenBy, and reopening the Story reopens the Tasks it froze\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"completeThroughService\",\n          \"signature\": \"completeThroughService(jsonPath: string): Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"jsonPath\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The approved record's path\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"For a BUILD, an outcome of kind 'story-completion' with ok, a note and the ids completed, added to WorkflowApproveResult.followOn. Undefined for other kinds. It never rejects.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"The record was just approved\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"The Story's and Epic's heads, and a head for every Story the DEF declares, exist before the walk\",\n            \"Each counted Task is walked first, then the Story\",\n            \"A failure leaves the approval standing and is reported with ok false\",\n            \"A Story held back is reported with ok true and a note naming the Tasks\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"handleRepoConvert\",\n          \"signature\": \"handleRepoConvert(params: unknown, repoEnv: string | undefined): Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"params\",\n              \"type\": \"RepoConvertParams\",\n              \"purpose\": \"repo and mode; mode gains 'repair-preview' and 'repair'\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"repoEnv\",\n              \"type\": \"string | undefined\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Fallback repository path\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Repair modes answer a RepairReport and work at any schema version.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"{ error: string }\",\n              \"condition\": \"Unknown mode, or a repository that is not a directory\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"'repair-preview' writes nothing\",\n            \"A second 'repair' lists no changes\",\n            \"The schema marker and the preview and apply modes are unchanged\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"liftStoreFile\",\n          \"signature\": \"liftStoreFile(fileName: string, parsed: unknown): ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"fileName\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The store file name\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"parsed\",\n              \"type\": \"unknown\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The parsed file\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\",\n            \"meaning\": \"A record for every kind of the common model; a head with no lifecycle has approval state 'unmigrated'\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"No legacy approval field is read\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"buildWorkItemGraph\",\n          \"signature\": \"buildWorkItemGraph(recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet): WorkItemGraph\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"recordSet\",\n              \"type\": \"ArtifactRecordSet\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The loaded records\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"WorkItemGraph\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Each epic, story and task node carries its unit head, or null. A story's tasks come from its TASKS head when it has one, else from its PLAN.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Unit records are not counted as evidence\",\n            \"Active Tasks are those the TASKS head lists and that are not withdrawn or superseded\",\n            \"A Task joins its PLAN row and BUILD result through planTaskId, not its own number, and that id comes first in sourceIds\",\n            \"Tasks are ordered by TaskPayload.order\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"storyStage\",\n          \"signature\": \"storyStage(route: DeliveryRoute, evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[], issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined, unit: UnitHead | null): { stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"route\",\n              \"type\": \"DeliveryRoute\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The story's route\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"evidence\",\n              \"type\": \"readonly ArtifactRecord[]\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The story's records\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"issue\",\n              \"type\": \"ArtifactRecord | undefined\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The issue behind a fix story\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"unit\",\n              \"type\": \"UnitHead | null\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The STORY head\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"{ stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\",\n            \"meaning\": \"'complete' only when the STORY head is completed. An approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays 'build-recorded', and its text says why: held, reopened, or no STORY head.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"An approved BUILD alone no longer yields 'complete'\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dataModelChanges\": [\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"CompletionEvidence\",\n        \"change\": \"field-add\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds storyBuildApproved(epicHash, storyId), true when the BUILD status is approved or later; storyApprovalOverride(epicHash, storyId), the explicit override reason on the approval, or undefined; and declaredStories(epicHash), the Story ids the DEF lists, empty when there is no DEF. A clean review is not an override. The repair supplies this interface with storyCodeReview answering overridden and storyApprovalOverride answering 'settled from an approved BUILD', because that approval already passed the gate of its time; every entry it writes is attributed to insrc:migration.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:48\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"FollowOnOutcome\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds kind 'story-completion' and optional completed: string[]. Additive; WorkflowApproveResult.followOn already carries outcomes to the caller.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/gates.ts:854\",\n          \"src/workflow/gates.ts:881\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"RepairReport\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"{ mode: 'repair-preview' | 'repair'; plan: ConversionPlan; result?: { applied: ConversionChange[]; held: UnitOutcome[]; failed: UnitOutcome[] } }, where UnitOutcome is { artifactId, reason }. Applied changes were written, held ones were left by a signoff hold, and failed ones hit a conflict or write error. ConversionRule gains 'settle-unit'.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/convert/types.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/repo-convert.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Repair discovery rules\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"A Story is known from a declaration in a DEF or from any LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR head naming its hash and story id, with S001 normalised to s1, so standalone work is found without a DEF; each known hash gets an EPIC head. An ISSUE with no such record creates nothing. A PLAN qualifies for Tasks at approved or any later status, after its lifecycle has been migrated. A PLAN with no TASKS head gets one from createFromPlan. A TASKS head that lists a Task with no head is reported as failed and left unchanged; this store has none. A Story is settled only when its BUILD is approved or later. Steps run in order: migrate heads, create units, create Tasks, settle.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/convert/units.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"DeliveryArtifactKind\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS. Relationship: one EPIC head has many STORY heads (by epicHash); one STORY has zero or one TASKS head and zero or more TASK heads (by epicHash and storyId); a TASK references one plan row by planTaskId, and re-planning can change that row while the Task keeps its number. Each work item references at most one unit head of its own level, in the direction item to head. TESTS stays skipped by name.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/types.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"WorkItemNode and DeliveryItem\",\n        \"change\": \"field-add\",\n        \"details\": \"Both add unit: { artifactId: string; status: Status } | null, set for epics, stories and tasks and null when the head is missing. The plugin shows an Epic as complete only when its unit status is completed, keeps the child count as progress, and shows a Task's unit status beside its validation result.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/types.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"ApprovalState, NoticeCode and AttentionReason\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"ApprovalState adds 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. NoticeCode and AttentionReason add 'needs-migration', raised for an unmigrated record or a story, epic or active task with no head, so such a record never counts as pending-decision. The plugin gains labels for these.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"interactionWithShared\": [],\n    \"errorPaths\": {\n      \"errorCases\": [\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The completion walk fails after a BUILD was approved\",\n          \"detection\": \"completeThroughService catches the rejection from completeIfRolledUp, for example a LifecycleConflictError\",\n          \"response\": \"The approval stands and a 'story-completion' outcome with ok false and the reason is added to followOn; a repair run or the next approval retries, and Tasks already completed are left alone\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The approval result says the build is approved and the Story could not be completed, and why\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A missing EPIC or STORY head cannot be created during approval\",\n          \"detection\": \"The store write rejects while the heads are being ensured\",\n          \"response\": \"The walk is skipped and a 'story-completion' outcome with ok false names the head\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The Story stays not complete until a repair run\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A head is unreadable during repair\",\n          \"detection\": \"readRawHeads reports it as a problem\",\n          \"response\": \"The plan lists it in problems and the other records are repaired\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The record is named in the report for the operator\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A head and its change log disagree while settling\",\n          \"detection\": \"LifecycleConflictError from the lifecycle service\",\n          \"response\": \"The unit is added to result.failed with the reason, left unchanged, and the run continues\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The unit is named in the report and stays unsettled\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A TASKS head lists a Task with no head during repair\",\n          \"detection\": \"The repair compares the listed ids against the Task heads found\",\n          \"response\": \"The Story is added to result.failed and its Task set is left unchanged\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The Story is named in the report for manual repair\",\n          \"recoverable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The repair stops part-way\",\n          \"detection\": \"The process ends before the run returns\",\n          \"response\": \"A later run finds each remaining change by what the records lack and finishes it\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"None once the repair is run again\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"edgeCases\": [\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Story with no Plan and no Tasks whose BUILD is approved with a clean review\",\n          \"expected\": \"The Story completes\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A clean approval of a BUILD where one Task's latest round failed\",\n          \"expected\": \"Passing Tasks complete, the Story stays open, and the outcome note names the failed Task\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"The same Story approved with an explicit override\",\n          \"expected\": \"The Story completes, the failed Task completes through the cascade with frozenBy naming the Story, and the override is recorded\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An approved BUILD whose code review is missing or blocked and no override\",\n          \"expected\": \"The Story stays open\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An Epic whose DEF declares two Stories, one with a head that completes and one with no head yet\",\n          \"expected\": \"The missing head is created as draft and the Epic stays open\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An Epic with no DEF\",\n          \"expected\": \"It counts the Stories that have heads\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A BUILD approved long ago with no code review record, during repair\",\n          \"expected\": \"The Story and its open Tasks complete, attributed to insrc:migration, with the reason saying it was settled from the approved BUILD\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A BUILD still pending, during repair\",\n          \"expected\": \"The Story stays open\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A unit whose signoff policy holds completion\",\n          \"expected\": \"It stays open; repair lists it in result.held\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A withdrawn or superseded Task under a Story\",\n          \"expected\": \"It keeps its status, does not count, and is not shown as an active Task\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Task whose number differs from its plan row after a re-plan\",\n          \"expected\": \"It joins its PLAN row and BUILD result by planTaskId and shows in TaskPayload.order\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Story reopened after completion\",\n          \"expected\": \"The Tasks it froze reopen, its stage is no longer complete, and repair does not complete it until its BUILD is approved again\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Story id stored as S001\",\n          \"expected\": \"Unit heads use s1, and the records resolve to one work item\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A repair run with nothing to change\",\n          \"expected\": \"No file is written and the plan lists no changes\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"invariantsToPreserve\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"An approval always stands, whatever happens in the completion walk that follows it.\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"A unit the signoff policy holds is not completed.\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"A completed status is recorded once, when a unit's children are complete and its review is clean or explicitly overridden.\",\n          \"source\": \"c4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The schema marker and the preview and apply modes of repo.convert keep their behaviour.\",\n          \"source\": \"c2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"conversion verification keeps reading the same loader and graph and reports no new differences.\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The delivery board reads only the lifecycle for approval and never a legacy approval field.\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"testStrategy\": {\n      \"testFramework\": \"node:test with node:assert/strict, run through tsx\",\n      \"testLevels\": [\n        {\n          \"level\": \"unit\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The roll-up rule and the board's reading of unit records\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"rollUp: a STORY with all Tasks complete, an approved BUILD and a clean review completes\",\n            \"rollUp: a STORY with no Tasks completes on an approved BUILD and a clean review\",\n            \"rollUp: a failed Task holds a STORY back on a clean review, and an explicit override releases it\",\n            \"rollUp: a pending BUILD, or a blocked or missing review, keeps a STORY open\",\n            \"rollUp: an EPIC stays open while a declared Story has no head\",\n            \"unitMembers: a STORY includes its TASK children\",\n            \"liftStoreFile: EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS records lift without a failure\",\n            \"liftStoreFile: a head with no lifecycle has approval state unmigrated\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: nodes carry their unit, and unit records are not evidence\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: a renumbered Task joins its plan row and BUILD result by planTaskId and sorts by order\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: withdrawn Tasks are not active\",\n            \"storyStage: an approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays build-recorded\",\n            \"gate: an unmigrated record raises needs-migration and never pending-decision\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"In-memory records built with src/workflow/__tests__/lifecycle-fixtures.ts\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Approval and repair against a real temporary artifact store\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"approving a BUILD completes passing Tasks, the Story and the Epic, asserting each TASK's lifecycle and log\",\n            \"a clean approval over a failed Task holds the Story and reports the Task\",\n            \"an approval with an override completes the failed Task with frozenBy naming the Story\",\n            \"reopening a Story reopens the Tasks it froze\",\n            \"approving a BUILD creates missing heads, and a declared sibling with no head keeps the Epic open\",\n            \"a failed walk leaves the approval standing and returns a story-completion outcome with ok false\",\n            \"a held signoff keeps the unit open\",\n            \"repair-preview writes nothing and lists settle-unit changes\",\n            \"repair at schema version 2 migrates heads with no lifecycle and keeps approved records approved\",\n            \"repair creates EPIC and STORY heads for standalone work with no DEF\",\n            \"repair creates Task sets for PLANs whose lifecycle it has just migrated and for completed PLANs\",\n            \"repair reports a TASKS head with a missing Task as failed and leaves it unchanged\",\n            \"repair completes units from approved BUILD records, leaves pending ones open and reports held and failed units\",\n            \"a second repair run lists no changes\",\n            \"a repair stopped part-way finishes when run again\",\n            \"repo.convert preview and apply keep their behaviour at schema version 2\",\n            \"conversion verification reports no new differences\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"A temporary repository with old-format and common-format records\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"contract\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The snapshot stays aligned with the VS Code plugin\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"the daemon delivery handler returns unit and the new notice and attention values\",\n            \"the plugin's delivery contract type-checks and labels every new value\",\n            \"the board shows an Epic complete only when its unit is completed\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"live\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The real repository after a repair\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"workflow.delivery on this repository reports no unknown-kind failures and no needs-migration notices, and approved work shows as complete\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac1\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"approving a BUILD completes passing Tasks, the Story and the Epic, asserting each TASK's lifecycle and log\",\n            \"rollUp: a STORY with no Tasks completes on an approved BUILD and a clean review\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac2\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"rollUp: a failed Task holds a STORY back on a clean review, and an explicit override releases it\",\n            \"an approval with an override completes the failed Task with frozenBy naming the Story\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac3\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"rollUp: an EPIC stays open while a declared Story has no head\",\n            \"approving a BUILD creates missing heads, and a declared sibling with no head keeps the Epic open\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac4\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"liftStoreFile: EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS records lift without a failure\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: nodes carry their unit, and unit records are not evidence\",\n            \"storyStage: an approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays build-recorded\",\n            \"the board shows an Epic complete only when its unit is completed\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac5\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: a renumbered Task joins its plan row and BUILD result by planTaskId and sorts by order\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac6\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"repair at schema version 2 migrates heads with no lifecycle and keeps approved records approved\",\n            \"repair creates EPIC and STORY heads for standalone work with no DEF\",\n            \"repair completes units from approved BUILD records, leaves pending ones open and reports held and failed units\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac7\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"repair-preview writes nothing and lists settle-unit changes\",\n            \"a second repair run lists no changes\",\n            \"a repair stopped part-way finishes when run again\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac8\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"gate: an unmigrated record raises needs-migration and never pending-decision\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac9\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"a failed walk leaves the approval standing and returns a story-completion outcome with ok false\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac10\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"the plugin's delivery contract type-checks and labels every new value\",\n            \"conversion verification reports no new differences\",\n            \"repo.convert preview and apply keep their behaviour at schema version 2\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac11\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"workflow.delivery on this repository reports no unknown-kind failures and no needs-migration notices, and approved work shows as complete\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"migration\": {\n      \"stateBefore\": \"The board rejects EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS records as unknown kinds and derives stories and tasks from DEF, PLAN and BUILD records. In this store 273 records have no lifecycle, every EPIC and STORY is draft, no Task is completed, and 252 approved builds have no STORY record. Conversion does nothing once the marker is at version 2. The records without a lifecycle were written by the installed daemon, which ran commit 5c5bc0cf1 from main, with no lifecycle code, until it moved to v2 on 2026-11-07; none has been created since. That path is closed on this machine by the move to v2. A daemon installed from a branch without the common model could write such records again, and the board's needs-migration notice and the repair cover that case.\",\n      \"stateAfter\": \"A BUILD approval completes its passing Tasks, its Story when the rule holds, and its Epic when every declared Story is done, and reports the outcome with the approval. Every record has a lifecycle, every known Story and Epic has a head, and approved work is marked completed. The board publishes unit status and shows complete only from it. Any record still without a lifecycle appears as needing migration.\",\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"action\": \"Ship the roll-up rule, the approval-time walk and head creation, the repair modes and the board change together, and update the daemon and the plugin.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"action\": \"Run repo.convert with mode repair-preview and read the listed changes and problems.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 3,\n          \"action\": \"Commit or set aside other work under the artifact store so that the repair's changes form their own commit.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 4,\n          \"action\": \"Run repo.convert with mode repair: migrate heads, create units, create Tasks, then settle units whose BUILD is approved. Read the applied, held and failed lists.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 5,\n          \"action\": \"Run the repair again to confirm it lists no changes, and check workflow.delivery shows no unknown-kind or needs-migration notices.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 6,\n          \"action\": \"Commit the repaired records.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"The repo.convert preview and apply modes and the schema marker are unchanged. The snapshot adds a unit field, one approval state, one notice code and one attention reason; an older plugin ignores the field and may show an unlabelled value until updated. Between the update and the repair, approved Stories without a completed STORY head show as build-recorded with a needs-migration notice, so the repair should run straight after the update. FollowOnOutcome gains one kind. Records are rolled back by reverting the repair's commit, since heads and logs both live under the artifact store. Other repositories are unaffected until repaired.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": true,\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": true\n    },\n    \"alternativesConsidered\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"name\": \"Wire the common model's rule at BUILD approval\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"BUILD approval completes each passing Task, then the Story when all counted Tasks are complete or the approval carries an explicit override; a repair run settles existing records.\",\n        \"approach\": \"On BUILD approval, walk each counted Task of the Story so those whose latest round passed complete, then roll up the Story. A Story needs an approved BUILD, a clean or overridden review, and every counted Task complete; an explicit override on the approval completes the remaining open Tasks through the cascade, and a Story with no Tasks needs only the first two. An Epic also requires a completed head for every Story its DEF declares. A repair mode of repo.convert, valid at any schema version, migrates records, creates missing units and settles status from approved builds. The board publishes unit status and gives it precedence over BUILD-derived completion.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Follows the common model's rule that a Story needs its Tasks complete\",\n          \"An override remains the one explicit way past a failed Task\",\n          \"Covers Stories with no Plan and reuses the walk, the cascade and repo.convert\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"A Task moves to complete at BUILD approval, not at the moment its round passes\",\n          \"Touches the lifecycle, the conversion and the board in one Story\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"L\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"name\": \"Any approved BUILD completes the Story\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"A Story completes on an approved BUILD with a clean or overridden review, and every open Task completes with it.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Replace the Task condition in the Story roll-up with an approved BUILD and a clean or overridden review, and cascade to all open Tasks. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"One rule with no Task condition\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Contradicts the common model's rule that a Story needs its Tasks complete\",\n          \"A clean approval would complete a Task whose build failed\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Violates k8-tasks-complete-before-story: a clean approval would complete a Story with a failed Task.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a3\",\n        \"name\": \"Complete each Task when its round passes\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Complete a Task at the moment recordBuildRound records a pass, and walk up from there.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Have the validate step run the completion walk after each passing round, so a Task completes as soon as its round passes. BUILD approval then only rolls up the Story. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Matches the wording of S007:FR001 most closely\",\n          \"A Task's status updates as soon as it passes\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"A later failing round on a completed Task leaves its status wrong, and completed is terminal without a reopen\",\n          \"Adds a lifecycle service dependency to the Task set and the validate path\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Violates status-is-reliable: a later failing round on a completed Task leaves its status wrong.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"chosenAlternative\": \"a1\",\n    \"openQuestions\": []\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/gates.ts:959\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:58\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts:29\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"git reflog: 756d5adf4 HEAD@{2026-11-07 17:54:07 +0530} checkout: moving from main to v2\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1 -->\n\n# LLD: STORY-eedc4519199b24b4-s1 — Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\n\n## Summary\n\n**Epic:** `make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact`\n**HLD base run:** `wf-1794219098430-hi9i5q`\n**HLD effective hash:** `ee817330ed05...`\n\nApproving a build now really completes its Tasks and Story and, once every Story the Epic declares is done, the Epic, which never happened before. A Task whose build failed holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override. A repair run brings existing records up to date at any schema version and reports what it planned, did, held and could not do. The delivery board then shows Epic, Story and Task status from those records, and shows any record still in the old format as needing migration.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [HLD context](#1-hld-context)\n2. [Contract details](#2-contract-details)\n3. [Data model changes](#3-data-model-changes)\n4. [Error paths](#4-error-paths)\n5. [Test strategy](#5-test-strategy)\n6. [Migration](#6-migration)\n7. [Alternatives considered](#7-alternatives-considered)\n8. [References](#8-references)\n\n## 1. HLD context\n\n**Framework:** Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\n**Rollout phase:** standalone\n\n## 2. Contract details\n\n**Surface level:** internal-shared\n\n### 2.1 `rollUp`\n\n```typescript\nrollUp(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader, evidence: CompletionEvidence): Promise<Status | undefined>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `id: string` — The TASK, STORY or EPIC head to evaluate\n- `reader: ChildStatusReader` — Reads child listings and statuses\n- `evidence: CompletionEvidence` — Build, review, override and declared-Story facts\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<Status | undefined>` — 'completed' when the condition holds. TASK: its latest build round passed (unchanged). STORY: its BUILD is approved, its review is clean or overridden, and every counted Task is completed, or the Story has no counted Tasks, or the approval carries an explicit override. EPIC: every counted Story is completed, and every Story its DEF declares has a head that is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `UnreadableChildError` when A head of the counted child kind cannot be read\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- id parses as an artifact id\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Reads only\n\n### 2.2 `unitMembers`\n\n```typescript\nunitMembers(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader): Promise<string[]>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `id: string` — The unit\n- `reader: ChildStatusReader` — Reads the unit's children\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<string[]>` — For a STORY, also its TASK children, so a Story completed by an override freezes its open Tasks\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A member that is completed, withdrawn or superseded is left alone, as completeMember already does\n- Each frozen Task's log entry names the Story in frozenBy, and reopening the Story reopens the Tasks it froze\n\n### 2.3 `completeThroughService`\n\n```typescript\ncompleteThroughService(jsonPath: string): Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `jsonPath: string` — The approved record's path\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>` — For a BUILD, an outcome of kind 'story-completion' with ok, a note and the ids completed, added to WorkflowApproveResult.followOn. Undefined for other kinds. It never rejects.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- The record was just approved\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The Story's and Epic's heads, and a head for every Story the DEF declares, exist before the walk\n- Each counted Task is walked first, then the Story\n- A failure leaves the approval standing and is reported with ok false\n- A Story held back is reported with ok true and a note naming the Tasks\n\n### 2.4 `handleRepoConvert`\n\n```typescript\nhandleRepoConvert(params: unknown, repoEnv: string | undefined): Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `params: RepoConvertParams` — repo and mode; mode gains 'repair-preview' and 'repair'\n- `repoEnv: string | undefined` — Fallback repository path\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>` — Repair modes answer a RepairReport and work at any schema version.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `{ error: string }` when Unknown mode, or a repository that is not a directory\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- 'repair-preview' writes nothing\n- A second 'repair' lists no changes\n- The schema marker and the preview and apply modes are unchanged\n\n### 2.5 `liftStoreFile`\n\n```typescript\nliftStoreFile(fileName: string, parsed: unknown): ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `fileName: string` — The store file name\n- `parsed: unknown` — The parsed file\n\n**Returns:** `ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure` — A record for every kind of the common model; a head with no lifecycle has approval state 'unmigrated'\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- No legacy approval field is read\n\n### 2.6 `buildWorkItemGraph`\n\n```typescript\nbuildWorkItemGraph(recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet): WorkItemGraph\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet` — The loaded records\n\n**Returns:** `WorkItemGraph` — Each epic, story and task node carries its unit head, or null. A story's tasks come from its TASKS head when it has one, else from its PLAN.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Unit records are not counted as evidence\n- Active Tasks are those the TASKS head lists and that are not withdrawn or superseded\n- A Task joins its PLAN row and BUILD result through planTaskId, not its own number, and that id comes first in sourceIds\n- Tasks are ordered by TaskPayload.order\n\n### 2.7 `storyStage`\n\n```typescript\nstoryStage(route: DeliveryRoute, evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[], issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined, unit: UnitHead | null): { stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `route: DeliveryRoute` — The story's route\n- `evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[]` — The story's records\n- `issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined` — The issue behind a fix story\n- `unit: UnitHead | null` — The STORY head\n\n**Returns:** `{ stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }` — 'complete' only when the STORY head is completed. An approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays 'build-recorded', and its text says why: held, reopened, or no STORY head.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- An approved BUILD alone no longer yields 'complete'\n\n## 3. Data model changes\n\n### 3.1 `CompletionEvidence` — field-add\n\nAdds storyBuildApproved(epicHash, storyId), true when the BUILD status is approved or later; storyApprovalOverride(epicHash, storyId), the explicit override reason on the approval, or undefined; and declaredStories(epicHash), the Story ids the DEF lists, empty when there is no DEF. A clean review is not an override. The repair supplies this interface with storyCodeReview answering overridden and storyApprovalOverride answering 'settled from an approved BUILD', because that approval already passed the gate of its time; every entry it writes is attributed to insrc:migration.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:48`\n\n### 3.2 `FollowOnOutcome` — field-modify\n\nAdds kind 'story-completion' and optional completed: string[]. Additive; WorkflowApproveResult.followOn already carries outcomes to the caller.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/gates.ts:854`\n- `src/workflow/gates.ts:881`\n\n### 3.3 `RepairReport` — new\n\n{ mode: 'repair-preview' | 'repair'; plan: ConversionPlan; result?: { applied: ConversionChange[]; held: UnitOutcome[]; failed: UnitOutcome[] } }, where UnitOutcome is { artifactId, reason }. Applied changes were written, held ones were left by a signoff hold, and failed ones hit a conflict or write error. ConversionRule gains 'settle-unit'.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/convert/types.ts`\n- `src/daemon/repo-convert.ts`\n\n### 3.4 `Repair discovery rules` — new\n\nA Story is known from a declaration in a DEF or from any LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR head naming its hash and story id, with S001 normalised to s1, so standalone work is found without a DEF; each known hash gets an EPIC head. An ISSUE with no such record creates nothing. A PLAN qualifies for Tasks at approved or any later status, after its lifecycle has been migrated. A PLAN with no TASKS head gets one from createFromPlan. A TASKS head that lists a Task with no head is reported as failed and left unchanged; this store has none. A Story is settled only when its BUILD is approved or later. Steps run in order: migrate heads, create units, create Tasks, settle.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/convert/units.ts`\n- `src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts`\n- `src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts`\n\n### 3.5 `DeliveryArtifactKind` — field-modify\n\nAdds EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS. Relationship: one EPIC head has many STORY heads (by epicHash); one STORY has zero or one TASKS head and zero or more TASK heads (by epicHash and storyId); a TASK references one plan row by planTaskId, and re-planning can change that row while the Task keeps its number. Each work item references at most one unit head of its own level, in the direction item to head. TESTS stays skipped by name.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/types.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts`\n- `src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts`\n\n### 3.6 `WorkItemNode and DeliveryItem` — field-add\n\nBoth add unit: { artifactId: string; status: Status } | null, set for epics, stories and tasks and null when the head is missing. The plugin shows an Epic as complete only when its unit status is completed, keeps the child count as progress, and shows a Task's unit status beside its validation result.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/types.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts`\n\n### 3.7 `ApprovalState, NoticeCode and AttentionReason` — field-modify\n\nApprovalState adds 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. NoticeCode and AttentionReason add 'needs-migration', raised for an unmigrated record or a story, epic or active task with no head, so such a record never counts as pending-decision. The plugin gains labels for these.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts`\n\n## 4. Error paths\n\n**Error cases**\n\n- **The completion walk fails after a BUILD was approved** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: completeThroughService catches the rejection from completeIfRolledUp, for example a LifecycleConflictError\n  - Response: The approval stands and a 'story-completion' outcome with ok false and the reason is added to followOn; a repair run or the next approval retries, and Tasks already completed are left alone\n  - User impact: The approval result says the build is approved and the Story could not be completed, and why\n- **A missing EPIC or STORY head cannot be created during approval** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The store write rejects while the heads are being ensured\n  - Response: The walk is skipped and a 'story-completion' outcome with ok false names the head\n  - User impact: The Story stays not complete until a repair run\n- **A head is unreadable during repair** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: readRawHeads reports it as a problem\n  - Response: The plan lists it in problems and the other records are repaired\n  - User impact: The record is named in the report for the operator\n- **A head and its change log disagree while settling** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: LifecycleConflictError from the lifecycle service\n  - Response: The unit is added to result.failed with the reason, left unchanged, and the run continues\n  - User impact: The unit is named in the report and stays unsettled\n- **A TASKS head lists a Task with no head during repair** (terminal)\n  - Detection: The repair compares the listed ids against the Task heads found\n  - Response: The Story is added to result.failed and its Task set is left unchanged\n  - User impact: The Story is named in the report for manual repair\n- **The repair stops part-way** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The process ends before the run returns\n  - Response: A later run finds each remaining change by what the records lack and finishes it\n  - User impact: None once the repair is run again\n\n**Edge cases**\n\n| Input | Expected |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| A Story with no Plan and no Tasks whose BUILD is approved with a clean review | The Story completes |\n| A clean approval of a BUILD where one Task's latest round failed | Passing Tasks complete, the Story stays open, and the outcome note names the failed Task |\n| The same Story approved with an explicit override | The Story completes, the failed Task completes through the cascade with frozenBy naming the Story, and the override is recorded |\n| An approved BUILD whose code review is missing or blocked and no override | The Story stays open |\n| An Epic whose DEF declares two Stories, one with a head that completes and one with no head yet | The missing head is created as draft and the Epic stays open |\n| An Epic with no DEF | It counts the Stories that have heads |\n| A BUILD approved long ago with no code review record, during repair | The Story and its open Tasks complete, attributed to insrc:migration, with the reason saying it was settled from the approved BUILD |\n| A BUILD still pending, during repair | The Story stays open |\n| A unit whose signoff policy holds completion | It stays open; repair lists it in result.held |\n| A withdrawn or superseded Task under a Story | It keeps its status, does not count, and is not shown as an active Task |\n| A Task whose number differs from its plan row after a re-plan | It joins its PLAN row and BUILD result by planTaskId and shows in TaskPayload.order |\n| A Story reopened after completion | The Tasks it froze reopen, its stage is no longer complete, and repair does not complete it until its BUILD is approved again |\n| A Story id stored as S001 | Unit heads use s1, and the records resolve to one work item |\n| A repair run with nothing to change | No file is written and the plan lists no changes |\n\n**Invariants to preserve**\n\n- An approval always stands, whatever happens in the completion walk that follows it. [[c1]]\n- A unit the signoff policy holds is not completed. [[c1]]\n- A completed status is recorded once, when a unit's children are complete and its review is clean or explicitly overridden. [[c4]]\n- The schema marker and the preview and apply modes of repo.convert keep their behaviour. [[c2]]\n- conversion verification keeps reading the same loader and graph and reports no new differences. [[c3]]\n- The delivery board reads only the lifecycle for approval and never a legacy approval field. [[c3]]\n\n## 5. Test strategy\n\n**Test framework:** `node:test with node:assert/strict, run through tsx`\n\n**Test levels**\n\n- **unit** — The roll-up rule and the board's reading of unit records\n  - Subjects: `rollUp: a STORY with all Tasks complete, an approved BUILD and a clean review completes`, `rollUp: a STORY with no Tasks completes on an approved BUILD and a clean review`, `rollUp: a failed Task holds a STORY back on a clean review, and an explicit override releases it`, `rollUp: a pending BUILD, or a blocked or missing review, keeps a STORY open`, `rollUp: an EPIC stays open while a declared Story has no head`, `unitMembers: a STORY includes its TASK children`, `liftStoreFile: EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS records lift without a failure`, `liftStoreFile: a head with no lifecycle has approval state unmigrated`, `buildWorkItemGraph: nodes carry their unit, and unit records are not evidence`, `buildWorkItemGraph: a renumbered Task joins its plan row and BUILD result by planTaskId and sorts by order`, `buildWorkItemGraph: withdrawn Tasks are not active`, `storyStage: an approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays build-recorded`, `gate: an unmigrated record raises needs-migration and never pending-decision`\n  - Fixtures: `In-memory records built with src/workflow/__tests__/lifecycle-fixtures.ts`\n- **integration** — Approval and repair against a real temporary artifact store\n  - Subjects: `approving a BUILD completes passing Tasks, the Story and the Epic, asserting each TASK's lifecycle and log`, `a clean approval over a failed Task holds the Story and reports the Task`, `an approval with an override completes the failed Task with frozenBy naming the Story`, `reopening a Story reopens the Tasks it froze`, `approving a BUILD creates missing heads, and a declared sibling with no head keeps the Epic open`, `a failed walk leaves the approval standing and returns a story-completion outcome with ok false`, `a held signoff keeps the unit open`, `repair-preview writes nothing and lists settle-unit changes`, `repair at schema version 2 migrates heads with no lifecycle and keeps approved records approved`, `repair creates EPIC and STORY heads for standalone work with no DEF`, `repair creates Task sets for PLANs whose lifecycle it has just migrated and for completed PLANs`, `repair reports a TASKS head with a missing Task as failed and leaves it unchanged`, `repair completes units from approved BUILD records, leaves pending ones open and reports held and failed units`, `a second repair run lists no changes`, `a repair stopped part-way finishes when run again`, `repo.convert preview and apply keep their behaviour at schema version 2`, `conversion verification reports no new differences`\n  - Fixtures: `A temporary repository with old-format and common-format records`\n- **contract** — The snapshot stays aligned with the VS Code plugin\n  - Subjects: `the daemon delivery handler returns unit and the new notice and attention values`, `the plugin's delivery contract type-checks and labels every new value`, `the board shows an Epic complete only when its unit is completed`\n- **live** — The real repository after a repair\n  - Subjects: `workflow.delivery on this repository reports no unknown-kind failures and no needs-migration notices, and approved work shows as complete`\n\n**Acceptance mapping**\n\n| Criterion | Proving tests |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `ac1` | `approving a BUILD completes passing Tasks, the Story and the Epic, asserting each TASK's lifecycle and log`, `rollUp: a STORY with no Tasks completes on an approved BUILD and a clean review` |\n| `ac2` | `rollUp: a failed Task holds a STORY back on a clean review, and an explicit override releases it`, `an approval with an override completes the failed Task with frozenBy naming the Story` |\n| `ac3` | `rollUp: an EPIC stays open while a declared Story has no head`, `approving a BUILD creates missing heads, and a declared sibling with no head keeps the Epic open` |\n| `ac4` | `liftStoreFile: EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS records lift without a failure`, `buildWorkItemGraph: nodes carry their unit, and unit records are not evidence`, `storyStage: an approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays build-recorded`, `the board shows an Epic complete only when its unit is completed` |\n| `ac5` | `buildWorkItemGraph: a renumbered Task joins its plan row and BUILD result by planTaskId and sorts by order` |\n| `ac6` | `repair at schema version 2 migrates heads with no lifecycle and keeps approved records approved`, `repair creates EPIC and STORY heads for standalone work with no DEF`, `repair completes units from approved BUILD records, leaves pending ones open and reports held and failed units` |\n| `ac7` | `repair-preview writes nothing and lists settle-unit changes`, `a second repair run lists no changes`, `a repair stopped part-way finishes when run again` |\n| `ac8` | `gate: an unmigrated record raises needs-migration and never pending-decision` |\n| `ac9` | `a failed walk leaves the approval standing and returns a story-completion outcome with ok false` |\n| `ac10` | `the plugin's delivery contract type-checks and labels every new value`, `conversion verification reports no new differences`, `repo.convert preview and apply keep their behaviour at schema version 2` |\n| `ac11` | `workflow.delivery on this repository reports no unknown-kind failures and no needs-migration notices, and approved work shows as complete` |\n\n## 6. Migration\n\n**State before:** The board rejects EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS records as unknown kinds and derives stories and tasks from DEF, PLAN and BUILD records. In this store 273 records have no lifecycle, every EPIC and STORY is draft, no Task is completed, and 252 approved builds have no STORY record. Conversion does nothing once the marker is at version 2. The records without a lifecycle were written by the installed daemon, which ran commit 5c5bc0cf1 from main, with no lifecycle code, until it moved to v2 on 2026-11-07; none has been created since. That path is closed on this machine by the move to v2. A daemon installed from a branch without the common model could write such records again, and the board's needs-migration notice and the repair cover that case.\n\n**State after:** A BUILD approval completes its passing Tasks, its Story when the rule holds, and its Epic when every declared Story is done, and reports the outcome with the approval. Every record has a lifecycle, every known Story and Epic has a head, and approved work is marked completed. The board publishes unit status and shows complete only from it. Any record still without a lifecycle appears as needing migration.\n\n**Zero downtime:** yes — **Data rewrite:** yes\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Ship the roll-up rule, the approval-time walk and head creation, the repair modes and the board change together, and update the daemon and the plugin. — ↩ rollbackable\n2. Run repo.convert with mode repair-preview and read the listed changes and problems. — ↩ rollbackable\n3. Commit or set aside other work under the artifact store so that the repair's changes form their own commit. — ↩ rollbackable\n4. Run repo.convert with mode repair: migrate heads, create units, create Tasks, then settle units whose BUILD is approved. Read the applied, held and failed lists. — ↩ rollbackable\n5. Run the repair again to confirm it lists no changes, and check workflow.delivery shows no unknown-kind or needs-migration notices. — ↩ rollbackable\n6. Commit the repaired records. — ↩ rollbackable\n\n**Backward compat:** The repo.convert preview and apply modes and the schema marker are unchanged. The snapshot adds a unit field, one approval state, one notice code and one attention reason; an older plugin ignores the field and may show an unlabelled value until updated. Between the update and the repair, approved Stories without a completed STORY head show as build-recorded with a needs-migration notice, so the repair should run straight after the update. FollowOnOutcome gains one kind. Records are rolled back by reverting the repair's commit, since heads and logs both live under the artifact store. Other repositories are unaffected until repaired.\n\n## 7. Alternatives considered\n\n### 7.1 a1: Wire the common model's rule at BUILD approval — **CHOSEN**\n\nBUILD approval completes each passing Task, then the Story when all counted Tasks are complete or the approval carries an explicit override; a repair run settles existing records.\n\nOn BUILD approval, walk each counted Task of the Story so those whose latest round passed complete, then roll up the Story. A Story needs an approved BUILD, a clean or overridden review, and every counted Task complete; an explicit override on the approval completes the remaining open Tasks through the cascade, and a Story with no Tasks needs only the first two. An Epic also requires a completed head for every Story its DEF declares. A repair mode of repo.convert, valid at any schema version, migrates records, creates missing units and settles status from approved builds. The board publishes unit status and gives it precedence over BUILD-derived completion.\n\n### 7.2 a2: Any approved BUILD completes the Story\n\nA Story completes on an approved BUILD with a clean or overridden review, and every open Task completes with it.\n\nReplace the Task condition in the Story roll-up with an approved BUILD and a clean or overridden review, and cascade to all open Tasks. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\n\n**Rejected because:** Violates k8-tasks-complete-before-story: a clean approval would complete a Story with a failed Task.\n\n### 7.3 a3: Complete each Task when its round passes\n\nComplete a Task at the moment recordBuildRound records a pass, and walk up from there.\n\nHave the validate step run the completion walk after each passing round, so a Task completes as soon as its round passes. BUILD approval then only rolls up the Story. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\n\n**Rejected because:** Violates status-is-reliable: a later failing round on a completed Task leaves its status wrong.\n\n## 8. References\n\n- **[[c1]]** `code` `src/workflow/gates.ts:959`\n- **[[c2]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121`\n- **[[c3]]** `code` `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:58`\n- **[[c4]]** `doc` `docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md`\n- **[[c5]]** `code` `src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336`\n- **[[c6]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts:29`\n- **[[c7]]** `prior-artifact` `docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md`\n- **[[c8]]** `doc` `/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon` — \"git reflog: 756d5adf4 HEAD@{2026-11-07 17:54:07 +0530} checkout: moving from main to v2\"\n"},"capturedAt":"2026-11-09T10:17:05.494Z"},"inventory":{"units":[{"id":"/body/summary","selector":"/body/summary","title":"summary","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/hldContextSlice","selector":"/body/hldContextSlice","title":"hldContextSlice","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/contractDetails","selector":"/body/contractDetails","title":"contractDetails","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/dataModelChanges","selector":"/body/dataModelChanges","title":"dataModelChanges","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/interactionWithShared","selector":"/body/interactionWithShared","title":"interactionWithShared","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/errorPaths","selector":"/body/errorPaths","title":"errorPaths","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/testStrategy","selector":"/body/testStrategy","title":"testStrategy","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/migration","selector":"/body/migration","title":"migration","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered","title":"alternativesConsidered","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/chosenAlternative","selector":"/body/chosenAlternative","title":"chosenAlternative","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/openQuestions","selector":"/body/openQuestions","title":"openQuestions","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","title":"a1","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","title":"a2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","title":"a3","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/citations/0","selector":"/citations/0","title":"Citation 1","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/1","selector":"/citations/1","title":"Citation 2","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/2","selector":"/citations/2","title":"Citation 3","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/3","selector":"/citations/3","title":"Citation 4","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/4","selector":"/citations/4","title":"Citation 5","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/5","selector":"/citations/5","title":"Citation 6","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/6","selector":"/citations/6","title":"Citation 7","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/7","selector":"/citations/7","title":"Citation 8","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:24","selector":"document:line:24","title":"1. HLD context","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"incomplete","summary":"The revised approach covers the issue's main reader, repair and lifecycle-status goals without requiring HLD ancestry. Two scope defects remain: failed Tasks can be completed through a review override without reconciling upstream requirements, and the design leaves a current lifecycle-less writer path open. Historical writer attribution remains only partially verified.","findings":[{"id":"scope-v2-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0/approach","message":"The chosen approach still permits an approval override to complete Tasks whose latest build failed. The cited DEF's k8 and ac9 require completed Tasks before Story completion; its explicit user override applies to the code review. The linked common-model design likewise requires each Task to pass its gate and says unfinished children count against completion. Distinguishing a clean review from an explicit review override improves the prior design, but does not establish authorization to waive failed Task gates. Reconcile this policy change with the upstream requirements, or preserve Task gating independently of the review override. Acceptance mapping ac2 currently tests the disputed behavior rather than establishing its requirement.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:340","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:260","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:304","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md — constraint k8, S003 ac9 and S007:FR001","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:84-90","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S003/LLD.md:115","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md — Fix intent"]},{"id":"scope-v2-02","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0 and /body/migration/stateBefore","message":"The design treats the lifecycle-less writer path as closed by the installed daemon's move to v2, but a current production path remains capable of writing that shape. The synthesize phase passes finalized JSON to writeArtifact; prepareArtifactWrite only reconciles a lifecycle when the input carries one (apart from preserving prior signoffs), otherwise it writes a revision without creating a lifecycle. The reviewed canonical LLD itself was created on 2026-11-09 and has no meta.lifecycle, directly contradicting the assertion that none has been created since the upgrade. The chosen repair-and-notice approach therefore does not satisfy the ISSUE's explicit requirement to close surviving writer paths. Include lifecycle initialization/preservation at these writes and a regression check covering newly synthesized artifacts and replacement drafts.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:317",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json#/meta — createdAt 2026-11-09T10:16:59.567Z; lifecycle absent","src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93","src/workflow/storage.ts:256-316","src/workflow/storage.ts:230-241","src/workflow/artifact-write-inventory.ts — synthesize and workflow-rpc content writer entries","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md — Fix intent, writer identification and closure"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:24","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/3","/citations/6","/citations/7","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-eedc4519199b24b4.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — completion, migration and subsequent binding requirements","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/HLD.md — architecture, lifecycle contract and story boundaries","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S003/LLD.md — roll-up and override contracts","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S007/LLD.md — Task completion and later failing rounds","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S009/LLD.md — migration lifecycle and history policy","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/gates.ts — approval override and completion hook","src/workflow/storage.ts — prepareArtifactWrite and lifecycleKeepingSignoffs","src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts","src/workflow/orchestrator.ts — finalization and author stamping","src/workflow/artifact-write-inventory.ts","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon — git reflog, current HEAD and historical commit 5c5bc0cf1"],"limitations":["Historical writer attribution in /citations/7 could not be fully verified. The installed checkout's reflog confirms the quoted move from main to v2 on 2026-11-07, and commit 5c5bc0cf1 lacks artifact-core. These facts establish checkout history, but do not establish which running process produced each of the 273 historical lifecycle-less records. The inspected evidence supplies no process-to-record provenance sufficient to verify that broader attribution."],"advice":["Give the local ac1–ac11 test mappings descriptive requirement text or explicit ISSUE paragraph links; the originating ISSUE does not define those criterion identifiers.","The linked common-model migration requirements support back-filling completion from historical approved BUILDs. Keep this migration policy explicitly distinct from the live approval override policy.","The relationship prose is adequate for this scope assessment. No authored diagram definitions or rendered companions are present in the subject directory; no visual verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"completion","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned sections cover Task traversal, declared Story discovery, completion cascades and approval preservation. Two gaps remain: completion outcomes can be discarded by existing callers, and previously completed Tasks can mask later failing build rounds.","findings":[{"id":"completion-v2-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/2 and /body/dataModelChanges/1","message":"Adding story-completion to WorkflowApproveResult.followOn does not ensure callers receive it. handleWorkflowApprove replaces result.followOn whenever the existing post-approval seam returns outcomes, discarding the proposed completion result. The CLI adapter also projects only the existing outcome kinds. Consequently an approval can succeed while its completion failure or held explanation disappears, contradicting the promised user-visible error contract. Specify merging both outcome collections, exposing completion in the CLI result, and tests through workflow.approve and workflow.approvePipeline with simultaneous completion and existing seam outcomes.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:80","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:172","src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts:56-58","src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts:84","src/cli/services/workflow.ts:151-162"]},{"id":"completion-v2-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/0, /body/errorPaths and /body/testStrategy","message":"The design completes passing Tasks while leaving their Story open, but does not handle a later failing round on one of those completed Tasks. For example, approval completes T1 while failed T2 holds the Story; subsequent rounds fail T1 and pass T2. recordBuildRound permits appending to a completed Task without changing its status. Walking T1 then returns no completion, but leaves its completed head intact; after T2 completes, the proposed Story rule sees every Task as completed and incorrectly completes the Story without an override. Specify how later rounds invalidate or reopen prior Task completion, or otherwise prevent stale completed status from satisfying Story aggregation. Add this multi-approval regression test, including individual Task heads and logs.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:44","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:231","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:259","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:383-391","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:50-58","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts:192-213","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:379-383","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S007/LLD.md:274"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/3","/citations/4","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — completion rules and lifecycle binding requirements","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S007/LLD.md — build-round and completion contracts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts — rollUp, countedChildren and unitMembers","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts — completion, frozenBy, reopening and partial recovery","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/approval-view.ts","src/workflow/gates.ts — approval contracts and completion hook","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts — completion holds and deferred settlement","src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts","src/cli/services/workflow.ts — approval outcome projection","src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/completion.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts — build-round recording","src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/completion-evidence.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Add explicit integration cases for deferred signoff using persisted approval overrides, mixed existing and missing declared sibling heads, and retry after some Task completions have already committed.","The relationship prose and ordered completion description adequately explain this chunk's interactions; no additional diagram is necessary. No rendered visual was supplied or visually verified."]},{"chunkId":"repair","status":"incomplete","summary":"Repair discovery and reporting are substantially clearer, but the specified migration order risks losing legacy feedback, repair can bypass the new live completion gate, and partial settlement reporting is incomplete. Historical writer attribution remains unverified.","findings":[{"id":"repair-v2-01","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/3 and /body/migration/migrationSteps/3","message":"The specified repair sequence starts with migrating heads but omits the feedback-conversion prerequisite. The existing migrateHeads helper calls backfillHead, which removes body.feedback; applyFeedback is the separate step that preserves those entries and review-decision batches in sidecars. Reusing head migration in the stated order therefore loses legacy feedback on a repository containing it. The applicable conversion requirements explicitly require appending feedback before the migration write. Include that prerequisite in repair planning/application and test interruption between feedback append and head replacement, preserving each entry exactly once.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:188","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts — migrateHeads and applyConversion","src/workflow/convert/backfill.ts:82-86","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts — applyFeedback","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:456 — s9 binding requirement 1"]},{"id":"repair-v2-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/0","message":"Repair manufactures an override for every approved BUILD without defining a historical eligibility boundary. Under this same LLD, a new ordinary BUILD approval can complete passing Tasks while deliberately holding its Story because another Task failed. Running repair then supplies an override for that still-approved BUILD and completes the failed Task and Story without a new explicit override. This makes repair undo the live completion policy. Define how grandfathered approvals are distinguished from current approvals and preserve current held work; test repair immediately after an ordinary approval held by a failed Task.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:164","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:188","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:259-260","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md — k8 and ac9"]},{"id":"repair-v2-03","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/2 and /body/errorPaths/errorCases/3","message":"The failed-settlement contract says the unit is left unchanged, but the reused lifecycle service writes members sequentially before committing the unit head. For example, completing LLD, PLAN and BUILD can succeed before a conflicting CR causes Story completion to reject. The Story remains open while those member heads and logs have changed. RepairReport does not define how these successful writes appear in applied when the settle-unit operation fails. Specify partial progress reporting and recovery, and inject a failure after earlier members have committed to verify that the report identifies both the applied changes and the failed settlement.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:180","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:241-244","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts:145-175","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts — completeMember","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts — unitMembers"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/1","/citations/5","/citations/7","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts","src/workflow/convert/run.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/raw-heads.ts","src/workflow/convert/backfill.ts","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts — completion holds and deferred settlement","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-units.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-repeat.test.ts","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md — lifecycle and conversion requirements","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S009/LLD.md — conversion contracts","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — s9 binding requirements and deployment handoff","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon — reflog, current HEAD and commit 5c5bc0cf1 tree inspection"],"limitations":["Historical writer attribution in /citations/7 could not be fully verified. The installed checkout's reflog confirms the quoted main-to-v2 transition on 2026-11-07, and commit 5c5bc0cf1 lacks artifact-core. These establish checkout history, but do not establish which running process wrote the historical lifecycle-less records or substantiate the claim that the deployed transition closed every relevant writer path."],"advice":["Make the migration-specific handling of completed PLANs explicit: TaskSets.readPlan currently accepts only approved status. Preserve the ordinary Task creation guard while implementing the repair's broader eligibility.","Strengthen preview tests to compare the entire planned change set against application, including settlement enabled by newly migrated heads and newly created units and Tasks. Assert byte-for-byte preview purity and second-run stability.","The ownership prose and ordered phases adequately explain repair without an additional diagram. No rendered visual was supplied or visually verified for this responsibility."]},{"chunkId":"board","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The revision defines common-kind loading, nullable unit status, lifecycle-based completion and migration attention. Two contract gaps remain: Task identity and ordering are not preserved explicitly through downstream consumers, and storyStage lacks the evidence needed for its promised explanations.","findings":[{"id":"board-r2-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/5/postconditions","message":"Putting planTaskId first in sourceIds does not make the existing client joins unambiguous. board-details.ts joins PLAN rows and dependencies using sourceIds.includes(), which ignores position. If a Task retains its own number as an alias, a re-plan can make that alias equal another active Task's plan row, selecting the wrong checks or dependency. Ordering also needs a downstream contract: graph.freeze sorts childIds, storyValidation sorts tasks by item id, and the client renders that task array directly. Specify a dedicated plan-row key or require consumers to use the designated first entry, and preserve TaskPayload.order through gate computation, snapshot and rendering. Extend the re-plan test beyond buildWorkItemGraph to prove validation, dependency joins and displayed order with colliding row and artifact numbers.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:140","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md#5-test-strategy","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts#freeze","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts#storyValidation","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts#assembleSnapshot","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts#taskRows","src/workflow/tasks/__tests__/task-set-reconcile.test.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts#TaskPayload"]},{"id":"board-r2-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/6","message":"storyStage promises to explain whether an uncompleted Story is held or reopened, but its proposed unit contains only artifactId and status. Reopening returns a unit to draft without adding a distinct lifecycle status; a signoff hold can leave the same draft status because the completion walk stops before applying completion. Unit records are excluded from evidence, and the loader does not expose Story reopen history or the completion hold result. The function therefore cannot reliably distinguish these cases from its declared inputs. Define how verified reopen and hold facts reach the stage pass, or narrow the explanation to facts it can establish. Add stage/snapshot tests for held and reopened units with otherwise equivalent BUILD evidence.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:146","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:155","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md#36-workitemnode-and-deliveryitem--field-add","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts#LIFECYCLE_TABLE","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts#nextLifecycle","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts#completeIfRolledUp","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts#withLogFacts","src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts#storyAnnotation"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/S007/LLD.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md","src/workflow/delivery/types.ts","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts","src/workflow/delivery/read.ts","src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts","src/workflow/delivery/notice.ts","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/contract.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/tasks/__tests__/task-set-reconcile.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/details-memory.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Preserve the existing JetBrains sample-snapshot contract test. No current JetBrains workflow.delivery consumer was found; a new delivery feature is unnecessary.","No diagram definitions, companions or renderings are supplied for this LLD. The relationship prose and status descriptions can support this change without a new mock; no visual verification is claimed.","The live repair and implementation tests were not executed during this read-only design review."]}],"progress":{"status":"invalidated","phase":"complete","completedChunks":4,"totalChunks":5,"lastMeaningfulActivityAt":null,"activeToolCount":0,"requiresUserInput":true,"checkpointPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","sequence":0,"reviewElapsedMs":0,"unitElapsedMs":null,"observedAt":"2026-11-09T12:57:54.181Z","freshness":"stored"},"startedAt":"2026-11-09T10:17:05.496Z","reviewer":"daemon","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","unit":{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","executionId":"b2dfa8f9-9247-4f7b-ac82-ec6a8617443f","dispatches":4,"retriesUsed":3,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"review_inactive","summary":"Review has no observed activity for 30 minutes"},{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Review activity CLI failed; NATIVE_CLI_FAILURE /: Resolve the reported native CLI output failure."},{"code":"review_inactive","summary":"Review has no observed activity for 30 minutes"},{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Review native session did not produce a successful final assessment; NATIVE_CLI_FAILURE /: Resolve the reported native CLI output failure."}]},"plan":{"chunks":[{"id":"scope","title":"Issue traceability, upstream requirements and chosen approach","selectors":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:24","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/3","/citations/6","/citations/7"],"concerns":["Compare the current live document and canonical artifact with the originating ISSUE's reproduction, root causes, fix intent, scope and exclusions; do not invent Epic or HLD ancestry.","Inspect applicable common-model requirements, including the cited DEF and relevant linked designs, for Task gates, Story completion, explicit overrides and reliable lifecycle status.","Assess the revised alternatives, historical approval policy and acceptance mapping against actual requirement text rather than assuming criterion identifiers establish traceability.","Verify the new deployment citation and writer attribution against available evidence, including whether any surviving writer path remains within the issue's fix intent.","Reassess prior scope findings and provenance limitations without assuming that citation replacement resolves them."],"dependsOn":[],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"completion","title":"Live approval, Task completion and Epic aggregation","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/citations/0","/citations/3","/citations/4"],"concerns":["Inspect rollUp, unitMembers, CompletionEvidence and completeThroughService against current lifecycle, lifecycle-service, evidence, approval and signoff code.","Check passing-Task traversal before Story completion, explicit approval override versus clean review, empty Task sets, terminal exclusions, frozenBy history and reopening semantics.","Verify declared Story discovery and head creation before Epic aggregation, including mixed existing and missing siblings and standalone work without DEF.","Trace story-completion outcomes through approval result contracts and callers; assess failure isolation, successful approval preservation, held outcomes, retry and partial-progress recovery.","Assess current BUILD and review selection, persisted override provenance, deferred signoff, normalized identities and tests asserting individual Task heads and logs.","Inspect necessary interaction or relationship artifacts and actual renderings where available; distinguish absent required evidence from optional diagrams."],"dependsOn":["scope"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"repair","title":"Repair discovery, reporting, repeatability and rollout","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/1","/citations/5","/citations/7"],"concerns":["Inspect RepairReport, ConversionPlan, ConversionChange, settle-unit and daemon routing against current conversion contracts and callers.","Verify migrate-heads, create-units, create-Tasks and settle ordering, including preview planning of changes enabled by earlier repair phases.","Check standalone Story discovery from LLD, PLAN, BUILD and CR, DEF declarations, normalized identities, approved or later PLAN eligibility and incomplete TASKS handling.","Assess historical BUILD approval as migration override evidence, attribution, signoff holds, reopened units, terminal states and compatibility with the live completion policy.","Verify planned versus applied, held, failed and unreadable outcomes, partial writes, interruption recovery, preview purity, second-run behavior and schema-version independence.","Inspect rollback feasibility, writer recurrence claims, unchanged preview/apply modes, shared conversion verification and focused repair test coverage."],"dependsOn":["completion"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"board","title":"Delivery graph, lifecycle status and IDE presentation","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2"],"concerns":["Inspect common-kind loading, lifecycle-only approval reading, unit representation, snapshot propagation and delivery handler contracts against current code.","Verify Epic, Story, TASKS and Task ownership, cardinality and membership, structural versus decision evidence, missing heads and unmigrated classification.","Trace planTaskId joins through PLAN content, BUILD validation, dependencies, sourceIds, graph freezing, gate computation, snapshot and client rendering; preserve TaskPayload.order and exclude withdrawn or superseded Tasks.","Assess storyStage precedence and Epic and Task display behavior for conflicting BUILD and unit status, held units, reopened units and missing heads.","Check needs-migration notices and attention without false pending decisions, and compatibility with conversion verification.","Inspect applicable VS Code and JetBrains consumers and contract tests without requiring an unrelated new client feature.","Assess necessary UX artifacts and inspect actual generated or authored renderings where available; verify proposed visible states through adequate design evidence."],"dependsOn":["completion","repair"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Fresh whole-artifact consistency and requirement coverage","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile all fresh substantive results with the originating ISSUE, applicable upstream common-model designs and current canonical and live documents.","Check end-to-end consistency between live completion, historical repair, published lifecycle status, Task identity, error outcomes and rollout order.","Confirm acceptance identifiers have meaningful requirement traceability and that tests cover the specified contracts and failure cases.","Reconcile all carried findings through fresh inspection, preserve unresolved mandatory verification limitations and apply the required status precedence.","Confirm citation mappings, linked evidence, necessary visual inspection and repository conventions without requiring future PLAN, TASKS, BUILD or CR artifacts."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 23 current inventory units are assigned to substantive chunks. Contracts, models, errors and tests remain grouped by implementation responsibility with deliberate overlap. Citation selectors are reassigned by their current targets because their indices changed. The added deployment citation is covered by scope and repair. Every substantive chunk requires fresh assessment; final consistency reconciles those assessments and does not replace inventory coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["completion","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["board"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["scope","completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["scope","repair"]},{"unitId":"document:line:24","chunkIds":["scope"]}]},"impact":{"baselineAttempt":1,"mode":"full","changes":["The chosen approach now completes passing Tasks before Story aggregation and requires an explicit approval override to bypass unfinished Tasks; all three alternatives and the summary were rewritten.","rollUp now specifies approved BUILD evidence and declared Story membership for Epic aggregation. CompletionEvidence gains explicit approval override and declaredStories facts.","The documented completeIfRolledUp contract was replaced by unitMembers changes that include Task cascade membership, frozenBy attribution and reopen behavior.","completeThroughService now returns a story-completion FollowOnOutcome, ensures declared sibling heads, walks Tasks first and preserves approval while reporting completion failures or held work.","RepairReport and settle-unit are introduced, with applied, held and failed outcomes. Discovery rules now cover standalone records, migrated and completed PLANs, normalized Story ids and missing listed Task heads.","Delivery graph contracts now specify TASKS membership, planTaskId joins, active Task filtering and TaskPayload.order.","storyStage is added, and WorkItemNode and DeliveryItem gain nullable unit status propagated to plugin presentation; needs-migration coverage expands to missing Epic and active Task heads.","Error cases, edge cases, integration tests, contract tests, acceptance mappings and rollout descriptions were revised across all implementation responsibilities.","The unsupported stakeholder citation was removed. The common-model DEF citation was added, existing citation indices shifted, and a deployment-directory reflog citation was added to support writer attribution."],"directChunkIds":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"indirectChunkIds":[],"rationale":"Attempt 1 is the immediately preceding completed publication, although its assessment status was incomplete. The current live and canonical documents revise every substantive responsibility, so none is eligible for unchanged coverage retention. Full mode selects all current substantive chunks and fresh consistency. Implicit effects also remain within this selected scope: stricter Task completion changes historical repair eligibility; Task cascade membership affects reopening and partial recovery; declared Story discovery affects both approval and repair aggregation; nullable unit status changes board stages and conversion parity; expanded outcomes affect caller contracts and tests. Unchanged preview/apply guarantees, signoff behavior, identity rules, issue exclusions and applicable common-model requirements therefore need reassessment alongside the direct edits. Prior provenance limitations require fresh verification rather than inheritance or assumed resolution. No new diagram definitions or companions appear in the current canonical body; substantive review must still determine visual necessity and inspect linked artifacts and renderings where available. All eight effective prior findings are carried without resolution.","uncertainReason":"No uncertainty requires selective retention: broad direct revisions and the preceding incomplete assessment justify full fresh coverage. The new writer-attribution evidence and revised override policy remain matters for substantive inspection.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["scope"],"currentIds":["scope"],"explanation":"Retains the scope responsibility and standalone issue ancestry checks, but revised alternatives and citation provenance require fresh review. Current citation 3 adds upstream DEF coverage, citation 6 now names the ISSUE, and citation 7 adds deployment evidence."},{"priorIds":["completion"],"currentIds":["completion"],"explanation":"Retains live lifecycle and approval responsibility. Contracts now add explicit Task traversal and cascade membership, declared sibling checks and returned outcomes. Lifecycle source coverage moves from citation 3 to citation 4; current citation 3 is the upstream DEF."},{"priorIds":["repair"],"currentIds":["repair"],"explanation":"Retains conversion and repair responsibility, with new report, discovery, eligibility and failure contracts. The repair helper citation moves from index 4 to 5; deployment citation 7 is additionally assigned for rollout and recurrence claims."},{"priorIds":["board"],"currentIds":["board"],"explanation":"Retains delivery and client responsibility, now covering explicit unit propagation, storyStage precedence, Task membership and re-plan joins. Shared contract, model, error, migration and test selectors remain assigned, but their content changed."},{"priorIds":["consistency"],"currentIds":["consistency"],"explanation":"Retains the final reconciliation role and dependencies on all substantive chunks; always runs fresh. No chunks are removed or split, and no prior assessment is retained."}],"retainedCoverage":[],"carriedFindingIds":["[1,\"scope\",\"scope-01\"]","[1,\"completion\",\"completion-01\"]","[1,\"completion\",\"completion-02\"]","[1,\"completion\",\"completion-03\"]","[1,\"repair\",\"repair-01\"]","[1,\"repair\",\"repair-02\"]","[1,\"board\",\"board-01\"]","[1,\"board\",\"board-02\"]"],"consistencyChunkIds":["consistency"]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"impact","phase":"impact","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"completion","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"repair","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"board","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"failure":{"code":"artifact_changed","summary":"Reviewed artifact changed; a user-approved full restart is required"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-09T12:57:54.181Z","recovery":{"attempt":2,"status":"invalidated","reason":"artifact_changed","completedChunkIds":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"requiresUserInput":true},"actions":[{"actionId":"delivery-board-round3-full-restart","signature":"f963562a51326a6bfe5bed8780a310dffa5bff2717468f2aa98c767e03f38ddc","operation":"restart_full","sourceAttempt":2,"resultAttempt":3,"userDecision":{"action":"restart_full","reason":"The owner said in chat on 2026-11-09: 'yeah, there was a network issue, fix the gaps already identified and then run another review'. Attempt 2 paused on a network failure and the LLD has since been revised to fix its findings.","recordedAt":"2026-11-09T13:05:00.000Z"},"acceptedAt":"2026-11-09T12:57:57.393Z"}]},{"number":3,"status":"changes_requested","preparationKind":"planning","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"4e5b1f12021d6cb9f27c9dfb6788f2dcad714a39328dbdf39d45860b40455187","document":"6e3dc78799e00102e03571f23b046a9183d1d69b9e581a90a0fa3462298d0b6d"},"contentIdentity":"fedc7d32a036c4fc9c9df730184ac4c886076fbf560c43e268adffe7e76108e6","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"design.story\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794228701499-fo6aur\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-09T12:57:14.854Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-09T05:00:05.847Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-claude\",\n          \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 332962,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"eedc4519199b24b4\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact\",\n    \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n    \"hldBaseRunId\": \"wf-1794228701499-fo6aur\",\n    \"hldEffectiveHash\": \"275251dd6eb3c46eb9d4eb18d0556942167ff3aaffb0e918e284e3b8be05fad2\",\n    \"hldAmendmentsApplied\": [],\n    \"storyTitle\": \"Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\",\n    \"standalone\": true,\n    \"sizeClass\": \"bugfix\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"envelope\": {\n      \"attachments\": []\n    },\n    \"revision\": 3\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"audience\": \"product\",\n      \"prose\": \"Approving a build now really completes its Story and Tasks and, once every Story the Epic declares is done, the Epic, which never happened before. A Task whose latest build failed holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override. New records have a lifecycle from the moment they are written. A repair run brings existing records up to date at any schema version and reports what it planned, did, held and could not do. The delivery board shows Epic, Story and Task status from those records.\"\n    },\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\"\n      },\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {}\n    },\n    \"contractDetails\": {\n      \"surfaceLevel\": \"internal-shared\",\n      \"api\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"rollUp\",\n          \"signature\": \"rollUp(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader, evidence: CompletionEvidence): Promise<Status | undefined>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"id\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The TASK, STORY or EPIC head to evaluate\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reader\",\n              \"type\": \"ChildStatusReader\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Reads child listings and statuses\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"evidence\",\n              \"type\": \"CompletionEvidence\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Build, review, override and declared-Story facts\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<Status | undefined>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"'completed' when the condition holds. TASK: its latest build round passed (unchanged). STORY: its BUILD is approved, its review is clean or overridden, and either it has no counted Tasks, or every counted Task's latest round passed, or the approval carries an explicit override. EPIC: every counted Story is completed, and every Story its DEF declares has a head that is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"UnreadableChildError\",\n              \"condition\": \"A head of the counted child kind cannot be read\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"id parses as an artifact id\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Reads only\",\n            \"A STORY's condition reads each Task's latest round, not its status, so a later failing round always counts\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"unitMembers\",\n          \"signature\": \"unitMembers(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader): Promise<string[]>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"id\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The unit\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reader\",\n              \"type\": \"ChildStatusReader\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Reads the unit's children\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<string[]>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"For a STORY, also its TASK children, so its open Tasks complete with it\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"A member that is completed, withdrawn or superseded is left alone, as completeMember already does\",\n            \"Each frozen Task's log entry names the Story in frozenBy, and reopening the Story reopens the Tasks it froze\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"completeThroughService\",\n          \"signature\": \"completeThroughService(jsonPath: string): Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"jsonPath\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The approved record's path\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"For a BUILD, an outcome of kind 'story-completion' with ok, a note and the ids completed. Undefined for other kinds. It never rejects.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"The record was just approved\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"The Story's and Epic's heads, and a head for every Story the DEF declares, exist before the walk\",\n            \"The walk starts at the STORY, and no Task is completed unless its Story is\",\n            \"A failure leaves the approval standing and is reported with ok false\",\n            \"A Story held back is reported with ok true and a note naming the Tasks\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"handleWorkflowApprove\",\n          \"signature\": \"handleWorkflowApprove(params: unknown, deps?: WorkflowApproveDeps): Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"params\",\n              \"type\": \"WorkflowApproveRequest\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The approval request\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"deps\",\n              \"type\": \"WorkflowApproveDeps\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The post-approval seam\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"followOn holds the approval's own outcomes followed by the seam's\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"A seam that returns outcomes no longer discards the story-completion outcome\",\n            \"src/cli/services/workflow.ts exposes the story-completion outcome in its result\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"handleRepoConvert\",\n          \"signature\": \"handleRepoConvert(params: unknown, repoEnv: string | undefined): Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"params\",\n              \"type\": \"RepoConvertParams\",\n              \"purpose\": \"repo and mode; mode gains 'repair-preview' and 'repair'\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"repoEnv\",\n              \"type\": \"string | undefined\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Fallback repository path\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Repair modes answer a RepairReport and work at any schema version.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"{ error: string }\",\n              \"condition\": \"Unknown mode, or a repository that is not a directory\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"'repair-preview' writes nothing\",\n            \"A second 'repair' lists no changes\",\n            \"The schema marker and the preview and apply modes are unchanged\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"liftStoreFile\",\n          \"signature\": \"liftStoreFile(fileName: string, parsed: unknown): ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"fileName\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The store file name\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"parsed\",\n              \"type\": \"unknown\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The parsed file\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\",\n            \"meaning\": \"A record for every kind of the common model; a head with no lifecycle has approval state 'unmigrated'\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"No legacy approval field is read\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"buildWorkItemGraph\",\n          \"signature\": \"buildWorkItemGraph(recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet): WorkItemGraph\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"recordSet\",\n              \"type\": \"ArtifactRecordSet\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The loaded records\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"WorkItemGraph\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Each epic, story and task node carries its unit head, or null. A story's tasks come from its TASKS head when it has one, else from its PLAN.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Unit records are not counted as evidence\",\n            \"Active Tasks are those the TASKS head lists and that are not withdrawn or superseded\",\n            \"A task node carries planRowId and taskOrder from its TASK head\",\n            \"For a task node with a head, sourceIds holds the plan row id and not the Task's own number, so no alias can collide with another Task's plan row\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"storyStage\",\n          \"signature\": \"storyStage(route: DeliveryRoute, evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[], issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined, unit: UnitHead | null): { stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"route\",\n              \"type\": \"DeliveryRoute\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The story's route\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"evidence\",\n              \"type\": \"readonly ArtifactRecord[]\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The story's records\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"issue\",\n              \"type\": \"ArtifactRecord | undefined\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The issue behind a fix story\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"unit\",\n              \"type\": \"UnitHead | null\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The STORY head\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"{ stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\",\n            \"meaning\": \"'complete' only when the STORY head is completed. An approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays 'build-recorded', and its text states the STORY head's status, or that there is no STORY head.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"An approved BUILD alone no longer yields 'complete'\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dataModelChanges\": [\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"CompletionEvidence\",\n        \"change\": \"field-add\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds storyBuildApproved(epicHash, storyId), true when the BUILD status is approved or later; storyApprovalOverride(epicHash, storyId), the explicit override reason on the approval, or undefined; and declaredStories(epicHash), the Story ids the DEF lists, empty when there is no DEF. A clean review is not an override. The override extends k8 by the decision recorded in DECISIONS.md: given on the BUILD approval, it also waives failed or unfinished Tasks.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:48\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"New workflow heads\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"The two sites that first write a finished workflow artifact give it a draft lifecycle, so a head is in the common model from its first write. Today such a head has none until a lifecycle operation adds one. A guard test fails if a production 'content' write of a delivery kind can create a head without a lifecycle.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93\",\n          \"src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349\",\n          \"src/workflow/storage.ts:178\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"FollowOnOutcome\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds kind 'story-completion' and optional completed: string[]. Additive.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/gates.ts:854\",\n          \"src/workflow/gates.ts:881\",\n          \"src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts:58\",\n          \"src/cli/services/workflow.ts:152\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"RepairReport\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"{ mode: 'repair-preview' | 'repair'; plan: ConversionPlan; result?: { applied: ConversionChange[]; held: UnitOutcome[]; failed: UnitOutcome[] } }, where UnitOutcome is { artifactId, reason, completedMembers: string[] }. Applied changes were written, held units were left by the completion rule or a signoff hold, and failed ones hit a conflict or write error. completedMembers lists members already completed when a settlement failed; the next run finishes the unit and leaves them alone. ConversionRule gains 'settle-unit'.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/convert/types.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/repo-convert.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Repair discovery, order and eligibility\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"Steps run in order: save feedback (applyFeedback), migrate heads, create units, create Tasks, settle. A Story is known from a DEF declaration or from any LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR head naming its hash and story id, with S001 normalised to s1; each known hash gets an EPIC head. An ISSUE with no such record creates nothing. A PLAN qualifies for Tasks at approved or any later status. A TASKS head listing a Task with no head is reported as failed and left unchanged; this store has none. Settling: a Story whose BUILD approval is dated before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM, a constant set to the date this change ships, is settled with storyCodeReview answering overridden and storyApprovalOverride answering 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration, because that approval passed the gate of its time. A later approval is settled only by the live rule, so repair cannot complete a Story the live rule holds.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/convert/apply.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/units.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"DeliveryArtifactKind\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS. Relationship: one EPIC head has many STORY heads (by epicHash); one STORY has zero or one TASKS head and zero or more TASK heads (by epicHash and storyId); a TASK references one plan row by planTaskId, and re-planning can change that row while the Task keeps its number. Each work item references at most one unit head of its own level, in the direction item to head. TESTS stays skipped by name.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/types.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"WorkItemNode, DeliveryItem and TaskValidation\",\n        \"change\": \"field-add\",\n        \"details\": \"WorkItemNode and DeliveryItem add unit: { artifactId: string; status: Status } | null, set for epics, stories and tasks and null when the head is missing, plus planRowId: string | null and taskOrder: number | null for tasks. TaskValidation adds taskOrder; a story's tasks array is sorted by taskOrder, then by task item id. board-details.ts joins PLAN rows and dependencies on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null, and the client renders the tasks array in the order it receives. The plugin shows an Epic as complete only when its unit status is completed, keeps the child count as progress, and shows a Task's unit status beside its validation result.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/types.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"ApprovalState, NoticeCode and AttentionReason\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"ApprovalState adds 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. NoticeCode and AttentionReason add 'needs-migration', raised for an unmigrated record or a story, epic or active task with no head, so such a record never counts as pending-decision. The plugin gains labels for these.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"interactionWithShared\": [],\n    \"errorPaths\": {\n      \"errorCases\": [\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The completion walk fails after the BUILD approval is committed, for example a child head cannot be read or a write conflicts.\",\n          \"detection\": \"completeThroughService catches the rejection from completeIfRolledUp or from ensuring the heads.\",\n          \"response\": \"The approval stands. The answer carries a story-completion outcome with ok false and the failure as its note; handleWorkflowApprove merges it with the seam's outcomes so it reaches the caller.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The build shows as approved and the caller is told the Story did not complete and why. A repair run or a re-approval attempt finishes it.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A counted Task's latest build round failed or the Task has no round, and the BUILD approval carries no explicit override.\",\n          \"detection\": \"rollUp for the STORY calls taskBuildPassed for each counted Task and storyApprovalOverride for the approval.\",\n          \"response\": \"rollUp returns undefined, so the Story and its Tasks are left unchanged. The outcome has ok true and a note naming the Tasks.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The approval is recorded and the Story stays open on the board, with the Tasks that hold it named. An approval with an explicit override completes it.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A repair settlement fails after some of the unit's members were already completed, because members are written one at a time before the unit head.\",\n          \"detection\": \"The settle step catches the write failure for that unit and re-reads each member's status.\",\n          \"response\": \"The unit is listed in result.failed with reason and completedMembers. Other units continue. A later repair run completes the rest, and completeMember skips the members already terminal.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The report names the unit and the members already completed; running repair again finishes it.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A TASKS head lists a Task id that has no TASK head.\",\n          \"detection\": \"The repair's Task step compares the TASKS listing against the store's TASK heads.\",\n          \"response\": \"The Story is listed in result.failed and is left unchanged; createFromPlan is not run over it.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The report names the Story and the missing Task for manual attention. This store has none today.\",\n          \"recoverable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A store file is unreadable or is not a recognised artifact when the board loads.\",\n          \"detection\": \"liftStoreFile returns a RecordLoadFailure for the file.\",\n          \"response\": \"The failure is reported as a load notice, as today, and the rest of the board is built.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The board still opens and shows a notice for that file.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"repo.convert receives an unknown mode, or a repository path that is not a directory.\",\n          \"detection\": \"handleRepoConvert validates the mode against the accepted set and checks the path.\",\n          \"response\": \"It answers { error } and writes nothing.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The caller sees the reason and nothing changes.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A head at a first-write site already exists with a lifecycle when a finished artifact is written again.\",\n          \"detection\": \"prepareArtifactWrite finds a lifecycle on the current head.\",\n          \"response\": \"The existing lifecycle is reconciled as it is today; the draft lifecycle is given only to a head that does not yet exist.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"None: approved and in-progress records keep their status.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"edgeCases\": [\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Story with an approved BUILD and clean review and no counted Tasks, such as a small bugfix or trivial route.\",\n          \"expected\": \"It completes; the Task check applies only when there are counted Tasks.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Task's earlier round passed and its latest round failed.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The latest round decides, so the Story is held back without an override.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Task is withdrawn or superseded.\",\n          \"expected\": \"It is not counted, and the cascade leaves it alone.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An Epic whose DEF declares a Story that has no head.\",\n          \"expected\": \"completeThroughService creates the head first, and the Epic stays open until that Story is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An Epic with no DEF, such as a standalone ISSUE route.\",\n          \"expected\": \"declaredStories is empty and the Epic rolls up from its counted Stories only.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with Tasks whose latest round failed.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair settles it with the override 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A BUILD approved on or after COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with a failed latest round and no explicit override.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair does not complete it and lists it in result.held.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Task's number differs from its plan row, as 20 Tasks in this store do.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The client joins on planRowId; the Task's number is not an alias in sourceIds, so it cannot match another Task's plan row.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Repair is run twice.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The second run's plan lists no changes.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A repository with no artifact records.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair reports an empty plan and writes nothing.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An old record still has body.feedback when repair runs.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The feedback is saved before heads are migrated, so it survives.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An ISSUE with no DEF, LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR naming its hash.\",\n          \"expected\": \"No EPIC or STORY head is created for it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A head with no lifecycle is loaded by the board.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Its approval state is 'unmigrated' and it raises needs-migration; it does not count as pending-decision.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"invariantsToPreserve\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"An approval that was committed is never undone by a later completion failure.\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"No Task is completed unless its Story is, so a held Story leaves its Tasks unchanged and an earlier status cannot hide a later failing round.\",\n          \"source\": \"c2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Approved records stay approved through repair, and repair preview writes nothing.\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Local feedback on a record is carried through head migration.\",\n          \"source\": \"c4\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"testStrategy\": {\n      \"testFramework\": \"node:test via tsx; vscode-plugin uses its own node:test run\",\n      \"testLevels\": [\n        {\n          \"level\": \"unit\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The completion rule, evidence, cascade and board derivation, on in-memory fixtures.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"rollUp for STORY: approved BUILD with clean review and all latest rounds passed completes\",\n            \"rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it\",\n            \"rollUp for STORY: no counted Tasks completes; a clean review is not an override\",\n            \"rollUp for EPIC: a declared Story without a terminal head holds it; an Epic with no DEF rolls up from its counted Stories\",\n            \"unitMembers includes TASK heads, and a held Story leaves every Task unchanged\",\n            \"reopening a Story reopens only the Tasks it froze\",\n            \"liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS and gives a head with no lifecycle the state unmigrated, and TESTS stays skipped\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph sets unit, planRowId and taskOrder, and a Task whose number differs from its plan row has no number alias in sourceIds\",\n            \"gate sorts tasks by taskOrder then id\",\n            \"storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head, and an approved BUILD otherwise stays build-recorded with text giving the head's status or that there is no head\",\n            \"board-details joins on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null\",\n            \"board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"src/workflow/__tests__/lifecycle-fixtures.ts\",\n            \"in-memory delivery records as in src/workflow/delivery/__tests__\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Real store writes through approval, first write and repair.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD: the outcome merges the approval's own followOn with the seam's, and the Story, its Tasks and its Epic complete\",\n            \"a walk failure leaves the approval standing and reports ok false\",\n            \"the CLI adapter exposes the story-completion outcome\",\n            \"both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle, and a rewrite of an existing head keeps its lifecycle\",\n            \"guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle\",\n            \"repair-preview writes nothing\",\n            \"repair in order: body.feedback survives on an old record\",\n            \"repair on an already converted repository creates missing EPIC, STORY, TASKS and TASK heads, with S001 normalised to s1\",\n            \"repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override\",\n            \"repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed and lists it in result.held\",\n            \"a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit\",\n            \"a TASKS head listing a missing Task is reported failed and left unchanged\",\n            \"a second repair lists no changes\",\n            \"an unknown mode answers an error and writes nothing\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"a temporary repository with a seeded .insrc/artifacts store\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"contract\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The daemon and plugin agree on the new board fields and labels.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts carries unit, planRowId, taskOrder, unmigrated and needs-migration\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/delivery-client.test.ts reads the same shape\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac1\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph sets unit, planRowId and taskOrder\",\n            \"the contract tests carry the new fields\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac2\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and its Epic\",\n            \"storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head\",\n            \"board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac3\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it\",\n            \"a held Story leaves every Task unchanged\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac4\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle\",\n            \"guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac5\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"repair on an already converted repository creates missing heads\",\n            \"repair in order: body.feedback survives on an old record\",\n            \"repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override\",\n            \"repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac6\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"repair-preview writes nothing\",\n            \"a second repair lists no changes\",\n            \"a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"migration\": {\n      \"stateBefore\": \"No unit ever reaches completed: the walk in src/workflow/gates.ts:959 starts at the STORY, rollUp (src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336) needs every Task completed, and nothing completes a Task. The store has EPIC 53 draft, STORY 250 draft, TASK 1,972 approved and 42 draft, and 252 approved builds have no STORY head. Two sources leave heads with no lifecycle. First, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93 and src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349 still write a new head without one, and src/workflow/storage.ts:178 only reconciles a lifecycle that exists; 4 records created on 2026-11-09 and awaiting approval have none (3 ISSUE, 1 LLD). Second, the installed daemon ran commit 5c5bc0cf1 from main, which has no lifecycle code, until 2026-11-07. In all, 273 records have no lifecycle. The board (src/workflow/delivery/load.ts) admits neither EPIC, STORY, TASK nor TASKS, and storyStage calls any approved BUILD complete. planConversion (src/workflow/convert/plan.ts) does nothing at schema version 2, so a converted repository cannot be repaired.\",\n      \"stateAfter\": \"Approving a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and, when every declared Story is done, its Epic, or reports why not. A Task whose latest round failed holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override. Every new head has a lifecycle from its first write. Repair brings existing records into the common model and settles units at any schema version, and is previewable and re-runnable. The board reads the status of Epics, Stories and Tasks from their heads, labels anything not yet migrated, and no longer calls an approved BUILD complete on its own.\",\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"action\": \"Ship the code: the completion rule, the first-write lifecycle, the follow-on merge, the board's new kinds and fields, and the repair modes. Set COMPLETION_RULE_FROM to the ship date.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"action\": \"Update and restart the daemon, and release the plugin with the new fields and labels.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 3,\n          \"action\": \"Run repair-preview on the repository and read the plan.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 4,\n          \"action\": \"Run repair, with the steps in order: save body.feedback, migrate heads, create missing EPIC and STORY heads, create missing TASKS and TASK heads, settle units.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 5,\n          \"action\": \"Read result.applied, result.held and result.failed. Re-run repair for failed units that can finish, and act by hand on those it cannot.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 6,\n          \"action\": \"Open the board and confirm that no record still raises needs-migration, then commit the changed store.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"New fields on the board's types, FollowOnOutcome and the repair modes are additive. The existing preview and apply modes of repo.convert and the schema marker are unchanged. handleWorkflowApprove now returns the approval's own outcomes and the seam's together instead of only the seam's. An older plugin against the new daemon ignores the new fields but will see Stories it used to call complete shown as build-recorded until repair settles them. The STORY rule deliberately diverges from S007:FR001: a Task completes with its Story rather than before it, so a held Story cannot be hidden by an earlier Task status. Heads written by a daemon on main still have no lifecycle; the board labels them needs-migration and repair handles them. Step 4 cannot be rolled back automatically, but its changes are confined to the store under version control, so restoring the store from git undoes them.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": true,\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": true\n    },\n    \"alternativesConsidered\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"name\": \"Tasks complete with their Story at BUILD approval\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"At BUILD approval a Story completes, with all its open Tasks, when every counted Task's latest round passed or the approval carries an explicit override.\",\n        \"approach\": \"The Story roll-up reads each counted Task's latest build round rather than its status. When the rule holds, completing the Story freezes its open Tasks through the cascade; when it does not, the Story and its Tasks stay as they are, and the outcome names the Tasks. A Story with no Tasks needs only an approved BUILD and a clean or overridden review. New records carry a draft lifecycle from their first write. A repair mode migrates records, saves feedback first, creates missing units and settles status, applying the old approval rule only to approvals older than the new one. The board publishes unit status, a plan row key and an order.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"A later failing round can never be hidden, because no Task is completed before its Story\",\n          \"One decision point, the existing walk and the existing cascade\",\n          \"Follows k8 for clean approvals, and DECISIONS.md for overrides\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"A Task's status changes only when its Story completes\",\n          \"Touches the lifecycle, the conversion and the board in one Story\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"L\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"name\": \"Complete passing Tasks first, then roll up\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"BUILD approval completes each passing Task, then rolls up the Story by Task status.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Walk each counted Task so passing ones complete, then roll up the Story by Task status, reopening a completed Task when a later round fails. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"A passing Task shows complete even while its Story is held\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Needs a reopen path on recordBuildRound so a later failing round cannot be hidden\",\n          \"Adds a lifecycle dependency to the validate path\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Partial on status-is-reliable: a Task completed before its Story can be hidden by a later failing round, and it would need its own reopen path.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a3\",\n        \"name\": \"Any approved BUILD completes the Story\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"A Story completes on an approved BUILD with a clean or overridden review, whatever its Tasks show.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Drop the Task condition from the Story roll-up and cascade to all open Tasks. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"One rule with no Task condition\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Contradicts k8 and the owner's decision: a clean approval would complete a Story with a failed Task\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Violates failed-task-holds-story: any approved BUILD would complete a Story with a failed Task.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"chosenAlternative\": \"a1\",\n    \"openQuestions\": []\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/gates.ts:959\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts:29\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:58\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c9\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c10\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"git reflog: 756d5adf4 HEAD@{2026-11-07 17:54:07 +0530} checkout: moving from main to v2\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1 -->\n\n# LLD: STORY-eedc4519199b24b4-s1 — Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\n\n## Summary\n\n**Epic:** `make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact`\n**HLD base run:** `wf-1794228701499-fo6aur`\n**HLD effective hash:** `275251dd6eb3...`\n\nApproving a build now really completes its Story and Tasks and, once every Story the Epic declares is done, the Epic, which never happened before. A Task whose latest build failed holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override. New records have a lifecycle from the moment they are written. A repair run brings existing records up to date at any schema version and reports what it planned, did, held and could not do. The delivery board shows Epic, Story and Task status from those records.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [HLD context](#1-hld-context)\n2. [Contract details](#2-contract-details)\n3. [Data model changes](#3-data-model-changes)\n4. [Error paths](#4-error-paths)\n5. [Test strategy](#5-test-strategy)\n6. [Migration](#6-migration)\n7. [Alternatives considered](#7-alternatives-considered)\n8. [References](#8-references)\n\n## 1. HLD context\n\n**Framework:** Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\n**Rollout phase:** standalone\n\n## 2. Contract details\n\n**Surface level:** internal-shared\n\n### 2.1 `rollUp`\n\n```typescript\nrollUp(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader, evidence: CompletionEvidence): Promise<Status | undefined>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `id: string` — The TASK, STORY or EPIC head to evaluate\n- `reader: ChildStatusReader` — Reads child listings and statuses\n- `evidence: CompletionEvidence` — Build, review, override and declared-Story facts\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<Status | undefined>` — 'completed' when the condition holds. TASK: its latest build round passed (unchanged). STORY: its BUILD is approved, its review is clean or overridden, and either it has no counted Tasks, or every counted Task's latest round passed, or the approval carries an explicit override. EPIC: every counted Story is completed, and every Story its DEF declares has a head that is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `UnreadableChildError` when A head of the counted child kind cannot be read\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- id parses as an artifact id\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Reads only\n- A STORY's condition reads each Task's latest round, not its status, so a later failing round always counts\n\n### 2.2 `unitMembers`\n\n```typescript\nunitMembers(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader): Promise<string[]>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `id: string` — The unit\n- `reader: ChildStatusReader` — Reads the unit's children\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<string[]>` — For a STORY, also its TASK children, so its open Tasks complete with it\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A member that is completed, withdrawn or superseded is left alone, as completeMember already does\n- Each frozen Task's log entry names the Story in frozenBy, and reopening the Story reopens the Tasks it froze\n\n### 2.3 `completeThroughService`\n\n```typescript\ncompleteThroughService(jsonPath: string): Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `jsonPath: string` — The approved record's path\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>` — For a BUILD, an outcome of kind 'story-completion' with ok, a note and the ids completed. Undefined for other kinds. It never rejects.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- The record was just approved\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The Story's and Epic's heads, and a head for every Story the DEF declares, exist before the walk\n- The walk starts at the STORY, and no Task is completed unless its Story is\n- A failure leaves the approval standing and is reported with ok false\n- A Story held back is reported with ok true and a note naming the Tasks\n\n### 2.4 `handleWorkflowApprove`\n\n```typescript\nhandleWorkflowApprove(params: unknown, deps?: WorkflowApproveDeps): Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `params: WorkflowApproveRequest` — The approval request\n- `deps: WorkflowApproveDeps` _(optional)_ — The post-approval seam\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>` — followOn holds the approval's own outcomes followed by the seam's\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A seam that returns outcomes no longer discards the story-completion outcome\n- src/cli/services/workflow.ts exposes the story-completion outcome in its result\n\n### 2.5 `handleRepoConvert`\n\n```typescript\nhandleRepoConvert(params: unknown, repoEnv: string | undefined): Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `params: RepoConvertParams` — repo and mode; mode gains 'repair-preview' and 'repair'\n- `repoEnv: string | undefined` — Fallback repository path\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>` — Repair modes answer a RepairReport and work at any schema version.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `{ error: string }` when Unknown mode, or a repository that is not a directory\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- 'repair-preview' writes nothing\n- A second 'repair' lists no changes\n- The schema marker and the preview and apply modes are unchanged\n\n### 2.6 `liftStoreFile`\n\n```typescript\nliftStoreFile(fileName: string, parsed: unknown): ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `fileName: string` — The store file name\n- `parsed: unknown` — The parsed file\n\n**Returns:** `ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure` — A record for every kind of the common model; a head with no lifecycle has approval state 'unmigrated'\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- No legacy approval field is read\n\n### 2.7 `buildWorkItemGraph`\n\n```typescript\nbuildWorkItemGraph(recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet): WorkItemGraph\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet` — The loaded records\n\n**Returns:** `WorkItemGraph` — Each epic, story and task node carries its unit head, or null. A story's tasks come from its TASKS head when it has one, else from its PLAN.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Unit records are not counted as evidence\n- Active Tasks are those the TASKS head lists and that are not withdrawn or superseded\n- A task node carries planRowId and taskOrder from its TASK head\n- For a task node with a head, sourceIds holds the plan row id and not the Task's own number, so no alias can collide with another Task's plan row\n\n### 2.8 `storyStage`\n\n```typescript\nstoryStage(route: DeliveryRoute, evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[], issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined, unit: UnitHead | null): { stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `route: DeliveryRoute` — The story's route\n- `evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[]` — The story's records\n- `issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined` — The issue behind a fix story\n- `unit: UnitHead | null` — The STORY head\n\n**Returns:** `{ stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }` — 'complete' only when the STORY head is completed. An approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays 'build-recorded', and its text states the STORY head's status, or that there is no STORY head.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- An approved BUILD alone no longer yields 'complete'\n\n## 3. Data model changes\n\n### 3.1 `CompletionEvidence` — field-add\n\nAdds storyBuildApproved(epicHash, storyId), true when the BUILD status is approved or later; storyApprovalOverride(epicHash, storyId), the explicit override reason on the approval, or undefined; and declaredStories(epicHash), the Story ids the DEF lists, empty when there is no DEF. A clean review is not an override. The override extends k8 by the decision recorded in DECISIONS.md: given on the BUILD approval, it also waives failed or unfinished Tasks.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:48`\n\n### 3.2 `New workflow heads` — invariant-change\n\nThe two sites that first write a finished workflow artifact give it a draft lifecycle, so a head is in the common model from its first write. Today such a head has none until a lifecycle operation adds one. A guard test fails if a production 'content' write of a delivery kind can create a head without a lifecycle.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93`\n- `src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349`\n- `src/workflow/storage.ts:178`\n\n### 3.3 `FollowOnOutcome` — field-modify\n\nAdds kind 'story-completion' and optional completed: string[]. Additive.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/gates.ts:854`\n- `src/workflow/gates.ts:881`\n- `src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts:58`\n- `src/cli/services/workflow.ts:152`\n\n### 3.4 `RepairReport` — new\n\n{ mode: 'repair-preview' | 'repair'; plan: ConversionPlan; result?: { applied: ConversionChange[]; held: UnitOutcome[]; failed: UnitOutcome[] } }, where UnitOutcome is { artifactId, reason, completedMembers: string[] }. Applied changes were written, held units were left by the completion rule or a signoff hold, and failed ones hit a conflict or write error. completedMembers lists members already completed when a settlement failed; the next run finishes the unit and leaves them alone. ConversionRule gains 'settle-unit'.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/convert/types.ts`\n- `src/daemon/repo-convert.ts`\n\n### 3.5 `Repair discovery, order and eligibility` — new\n\nSteps run in order: save feedback (applyFeedback), migrate heads, create units, create Tasks, settle. A Story is known from a DEF declaration or from any LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR head naming its hash and story id, with S001 normalised to s1; each known hash gets an EPIC head. An ISSUE with no such record creates nothing. A PLAN qualifies for Tasks at approved or any later status. A TASKS head listing a Task with no head is reported as failed and left unchanged; this store has none. Settling: a Story whose BUILD approval is dated before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM, a constant set to the date this change ships, is settled with storyCodeReview answering overridden and storyApprovalOverride answering 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration, because that approval passed the gate of its time. A later approval is settled only by the live rule, so repair cannot complete a Story the live rule holds.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/convert/apply.ts`\n- `src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts`\n- `src/workflow/convert/units.ts`\n- `src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts`\n- `src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts`\n\n### 3.6 `DeliveryArtifactKind` — field-modify\n\nAdds EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS. Relationship: one EPIC head has many STORY heads (by epicHash); one STORY has zero or one TASKS head and zero or more TASK heads (by epicHash and storyId); a TASK references one plan row by planTaskId, and re-planning can change that row while the Task keeps its number. Each work item references at most one unit head of its own level, in the direction item to head. TESTS stays skipped by name.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/types.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts`\n- `src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts`\n\n### 3.7 `WorkItemNode, DeliveryItem and TaskValidation` — field-add\n\nWorkItemNode and DeliveryItem add unit: { artifactId: string; status: Status } | null, set for epics, stories and tasks and null when the head is missing, plus planRowId: string | null and taskOrder: number | null for tasks. TaskValidation adds taskOrder; a story's tasks array is sorted by taskOrder, then by task item id. board-details.ts joins PLAN rows and dependencies on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null, and the client renders the tasks array in the order it receives. The plugin shows an Epic as complete only when its unit status is completed, keeps the child count as progress, and shows a Task's unit status beside its validation result.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/types.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts`\n\n### 3.8 `ApprovalState, NoticeCode and AttentionReason` — field-modify\n\nApprovalState adds 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. NoticeCode and AttentionReason add 'needs-migration', raised for an unmigrated record or a story, epic or active task with no head, so such a record never counts as pending-decision. The plugin gains labels for these.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts`\n\n## 4. Error paths\n\n**Error cases**\n\n- **The completion walk fails after the BUILD approval is committed, for example a child head cannot be read or a write conflicts.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: completeThroughService catches the rejection from completeIfRolledUp or from ensuring the heads.\n  - Response: The approval stands. The answer carries a story-completion outcome with ok false and the failure as its note; handleWorkflowApprove merges it with the seam's outcomes so it reaches the caller.\n  - User impact: The build shows as approved and the caller is told the Story did not complete and why. A repair run or a re-approval attempt finishes it.\n- **A counted Task's latest build round failed or the Task has no round, and the BUILD approval carries no explicit override.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: rollUp for the STORY calls taskBuildPassed for each counted Task and storyApprovalOverride for the approval.\n  - Response: rollUp returns undefined, so the Story and its Tasks are left unchanged. The outcome has ok true and a note naming the Tasks.\n  - User impact: The approval is recorded and the Story stays open on the board, with the Tasks that hold it named. An approval with an explicit override completes it.\n- **A repair settlement fails after some of the unit's members were already completed, because members are written one at a time before the unit head.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The settle step catches the write failure for that unit and re-reads each member's status.\n  - Response: The unit is listed in result.failed with reason and completedMembers. Other units continue. A later repair run completes the rest, and completeMember skips the members already terminal.\n  - User impact: The report names the unit and the members already completed; running repair again finishes it.\n- **A TASKS head lists a Task id that has no TASK head.** (terminal)\n  - Detection: The repair's Task step compares the TASKS listing against the store's TASK heads.\n  - Response: The Story is listed in result.failed and is left unchanged; createFromPlan is not run over it.\n  - User impact: The report names the Story and the missing Task for manual attention. This store has none today.\n- **A store file is unreadable or is not a recognised artifact when the board loads.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: liftStoreFile returns a RecordLoadFailure for the file.\n  - Response: The failure is reported as a load notice, as today, and the rest of the board is built.\n  - User impact: The board still opens and shows a notice for that file.\n- **repo.convert receives an unknown mode, or a repository path that is not a directory.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: handleRepoConvert validates the mode against the accepted set and checks the path.\n  - Response: It answers { error } and writes nothing.\n  - User impact: The caller sees the reason and nothing changes.\n- **A head at a first-write site already exists with a lifecycle when a finished artifact is written again.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: prepareArtifactWrite finds a lifecycle on the current head.\n  - Response: The existing lifecycle is reconciled as it is today; the draft lifecycle is given only to a head that does not yet exist.\n  - User impact: None: approved and in-progress records keep their status.\n\n**Edge cases**\n\n| Input | Expected |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| A Story with an approved BUILD and clean review and no counted Tasks, such as a small bugfix or trivial route. | It completes; the Task check applies only when there are counted Tasks. |\n| A Task's earlier round passed and its latest round failed. | The latest round decides, so the Story is held back without an override. |\n| A Task is withdrawn or superseded. | It is not counted, and the cascade leaves it alone. |\n| An Epic whose DEF declares a Story that has no head. | completeThroughService creates the head first, and the Epic stays open until that Story is completed, withdrawn or superseded. |\n| An Epic with no DEF, such as a standalone ISSUE route. | declaredStories is empty and the Epic rolls up from its counted Stories only. |\n| A BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with Tasks whose latest round failed. | Repair settles it with the override 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration. |\n| A BUILD approved on or after COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with a failed latest round and no explicit override. | Repair does not complete it and lists it in result.held. |\n| A Task's number differs from its plan row, as 20 Tasks in this store do. | The client joins on planRowId; the Task's number is not an alias in sourceIds, so it cannot match another Task's plan row. |\n| Repair is run twice. | The second run's plan lists no changes. |\n| A repository with no artifact records. | Repair reports an empty plan and writes nothing. |\n| An old record still has body.feedback when repair runs. | The feedback is saved before heads are migrated, so it survives. |\n| An ISSUE with no DEF, LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR naming its hash. | No EPIC or STORY head is created for it. |\n| A head with no lifecycle is loaded by the board. | Its approval state is 'unmigrated' and it raises needs-migration; it does not count as pending-decision. |\n\n**Invariants to preserve**\n\n- An approval that was committed is never undone by a later completion failure. [[c1]]\n- No Task is completed unless its Story is, so a held Story leaves its Tasks unchanged and an earlier status cannot hide a later failing round. [[c2]]\n- Approved records stay approved through repair, and repair preview writes nothing. [[c3]]\n- Local feedback on a record is carried through head migration. [[c4]]\n\n## 5. Test strategy\n\n**Test framework:** `node:test via tsx; vscode-plugin uses its own node:test run`\n\n**Test levels**\n\n- **unit** — The completion rule, evidence, cascade and board derivation, on in-memory fixtures.\n  - Subjects: `rollUp for STORY: approved BUILD with clean review and all latest rounds passed completes`, `rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it`, `rollUp for STORY: no counted Tasks completes; a clean review is not an override`, `rollUp for EPIC: a declared Story without a terminal head holds it; an Epic with no DEF rolls up from its counted Stories`, `unitMembers includes TASK heads, and a held Story leaves every Task unchanged`, `reopening a Story reopens only the Tasks it froze`, `liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS and gives a head with no lifecycle the state unmigrated, and TESTS stays skipped`, `buildWorkItemGraph sets unit, planRowId and taskOrder, and a Task whose number differs from its plan row has no number alias in sourceIds`, `gate sorts tasks by taskOrder then id`, `storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head, and an approved BUILD otherwise stays build-recorded with text giving the head's status or that there is no head`, `board-details joins on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null`, `board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status`\n  - Fixtures: `src/workflow/__tests__/lifecycle-fixtures.ts`, `in-memory delivery records as in src/workflow/delivery/__tests__`\n- **integration** — Real store writes through approval, first write and repair.\n  - Subjects: `handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD: the outcome merges the approval's own followOn with the seam's, and the Story, its Tasks and its Epic complete`, `a walk failure leaves the approval standing and reports ok false`, `the CLI adapter exposes the story-completion outcome`, `both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle, and a rewrite of an existing head keeps its lifecycle`, `guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle`, `repair-preview writes nothing`, `repair in order: body.feedback survives on an old record`, `repair on an already converted repository creates missing EPIC, STORY, TASKS and TASK heads, with S001 normalised to s1`, `repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override`, `repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed and lists it in result.held`, `a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit`, `a TASKS head listing a missing Task is reported failed and left unchanged`, `a second repair lists no changes`, `an unknown mode answers an error and writes nothing`\n  - Fixtures: `a temporary repository with a seeded .insrc/artifacts store`\n- **contract** — The daemon and plugin agree on the new board fields and labels.\n  - Subjects: `src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts carries unit, planRowId, taskOrder, unmigrated and needs-migration`, `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/delivery-client.test.ts reads the same shape`\n\n**Acceptance mapping**\n\n| Criterion | Proving tests |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `ac1` | `liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS`, `buildWorkItemGraph sets unit, planRowId and taskOrder`, `the contract tests carry the new fields` |\n| `ac2` | `handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and its Epic`, `storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head`, `board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status` |\n| `ac3` | `rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it`, `a held Story leaves every Task unchanged` |\n| `ac4` | `both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle`, `guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle` |\n| `ac5` | `repair on an already converted repository creates missing heads`, `repair in order: body.feedback survives on an old record`, `repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override`, `repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed` |\n| `ac6` | `repair-preview writes nothing`, `a second repair lists no changes`, `a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit` |\n\n## 6. Migration\n\n**State before:** No unit ever reaches completed: the walk in src/workflow/gates.ts:959 starts at the STORY, rollUp (src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336) needs every Task completed, and nothing completes a Task. The store has EPIC 53 draft, STORY 250 draft, TASK 1,972 approved and 42 draft, and 252 approved builds have no STORY head. Two sources leave heads with no lifecycle. First, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93 and src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349 still write a new head without one, and src/workflow/storage.ts:178 only reconciles a lifecycle that exists; 4 records created on 2026-11-09 and awaiting approval have none (3 ISSUE, 1 LLD). Second, the installed daemon ran commit 5c5bc0cf1 from main, which has no lifecycle code, until 2026-11-07. In all, 273 records have no lifecycle. The board (src/workflow/delivery/load.ts) admits neither EPIC, STORY, TASK nor TASKS, and storyStage calls any approved BUILD complete. planConversion (src/workflow/convert/plan.ts) does nothing at schema version 2, so a converted repository cannot be repaired.\n\n**State after:** Approving a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and, when every declared Story is done, its Epic, or reports why not. A Task whose latest round failed holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override. Every new head has a lifecycle from its first write. Repair brings existing records into the common model and settles units at any schema version, and is previewable and re-runnable. The board reads the status of Epics, Stories and Tasks from their heads, labels anything not yet migrated, and no longer calls an approved BUILD complete on its own.\n\n**Zero downtime:** yes — **Data rewrite:** yes\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Ship the code: the completion rule, the first-write lifecycle, the follow-on merge, the board's new kinds and fields, and the repair modes. Set COMPLETION_RULE_FROM to the ship date. — ↩ rollbackable\n2. Update and restart the daemon, and release the plugin with the new fields and labels. — ↩ rollbackable\n3. Run repair-preview on the repository and read the plan. — ↩ rollbackable\n4. Run repair, with the steps in order: save body.feedback, migrate heads, create missing EPIC and STORY heads, create missing TASKS and TASK heads, settle units. — ✕ non-rollbackable\n5. Read result.applied, result.held and result.failed. Re-run repair for failed units that can finish, and act by hand on those it cannot. — ✕ non-rollbackable\n6. Open the board and confirm that no record still raises needs-migration, then commit the changed store. — ↩ rollbackable\n\n**Backward compat:** New fields on the board's types, FollowOnOutcome and the repair modes are additive. The existing preview and apply modes of repo.convert and the schema marker are unchanged. handleWorkflowApprove now returns the approval's own outcomes and the seam's together instead of only the seam's. An older plugin against the new daemon ignores the new fields but will see Stories it used to call complete shown as build-recorded until repair settles them. The STORY rule deliberately diverges from S007:FR001: a Task completes with its Story rather than before it, so a held Story cannot be hidden by an earlier Task status. Heads written by a daemon on main still have no lifecycle; the board labels them needs-migration and repair handles them. Step 4 cannot be rolled back automatically, but its changes are confined to the store under version control, so restoring the store from git undoes them.\n\n## 7. Alternatives considered\n\n### 7.1 a1: Tasks complete with their Story at BUILD approval — **CHOSEN**\n\nAt BUILD approval a Story completes, with all its open Tasks, when every counted Task's latest round passed or the approval carries an explicit override.\n\nThe Story roll-up reads each counted Task's latest build round rather than its status. When the rule holds, completing the Story freezes its open Tasks through the cascade; when it does not, the Story and its Tasks stay as they are, and the outcome names the Tasks. A Story with no Tasks needs only an approved BUILD and a clean or overridden review. New records carry a draft lifecycle from their first write. A repair mode migrates records, saves feedback first, creates missing units and settles status, applying the old approval rule only to approvals older than the new one. The board publishes unit status, a plan row key and an order.\n\n### 7.2 a2: Complete passing Tasks first, then roll up\n\nBUILD approval completes each passing Task, then rolls up the Story by Task status.\n\nWalk each counted Task so passing ones complete, then roll up the Story by Task status, reopening a completed Task when a later round fails. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\n\n**Rejected because:** Partial on status-is-reliable: a Task completed before its Story can be hidden by a later failing round, and it would need its own reopen path.\n\n### 7.3 a3: Any approved BUILD completes the Story\n\nA Story completes on an approved BUILD with a clean or overridden review, whatever its Tasks show.\n\nDrop the Task condition from the Story roll-up and cascade to all open Tasks. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\n\n**Rejected because:** Violates failed-task-holds-story: any approved BUILD would complete a Story with a failed Task.\n\n## 8. References\n\n- **[[c1]]** `code` `src/workflow/gates.ts:959`\n- **[[c2]]** `code` `src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336`\n- **[[c3]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts:29`\n- **[[c4]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts`\n- **[[c5]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121`\n- **[[c6]]** `code` `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:58`\n- **[[c7]]** `doc` `docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md`\n- **[[c8]]** `prior-artifact` `docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md`\n- **[[c9]]** `doc` `docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md`\n- **[[c10]]** `doc` `/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon` — \"git reflog: 756d5adf4 HEAD@{2026-11-07 17:54:07 +0530} checkout: moving from main to v2\"\n"},"capturedAt":"2026-11-09T12:57:57.391Z"},"inventory":{"units":[{"id":"/body/summary","selector":"/body/summary","title":"summary","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/hldContextSlice","selector":"/body/hldContextSlice","title":"hldContextSlice","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/contractDetails","selector":"/body/contractDetails","title":"contractDetails","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/dataModelChanges","selector":"/body/dataModelChanges","title":"dataModelChanges","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/interactionWithShared","selector":"/body/interactionWithShared","title":"interactionWithShared","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/errorPaths","selector":"/body/errorPaths","title":"errorPaths","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/testStrategy","selector":"/body/testStrategy","title":"testStrategy","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/migration","selector":"/body/migration","title":"migration","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered","title":"alternativesConsidered","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/chosenAlternative","selector":"/body/chosenAlternative","title":"chosenAlternative","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/openQuestions","selector":"/body/openQuestions","title":"openQuestions","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","title":"a1","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","title":"a2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","title":"a3","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/citations/0","selector":"/citations/0","title":"Citation 1","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/1","selector":"/citations/1","title":"Citation 2","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/2","selector":"/citations/2","title":"Citation 3","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/3","selector":"/citations/3","title":"Citation 4","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/4","selector":"/citations/4","title":"Citation 5","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/5","selector":"/citations/5","title":"Citation 6","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/6","selector":"/citations/6","title":"Citation 7","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/7","selector":"/citations/7","title":"Citation 8","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/8","selector":"/citations/8","title":"Citation 9","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/9","selector":"/citations/9","title":"Citation 10","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:24","selector":"document:line:24","title":"1. HLD context","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned scope sections align with the originating ISSUE’s reader, lifecycle, repair and recurrence-prevention requirements. The common-model DEF and recorded owner decisions establish the applicable contracts without requiring HLD ancestry. The LLD explicitly describes its Task-completion divergence, preserves the explicit-override requirement for live approvals, and distinguishes historical migration settlement. No blocking scope defect was identified.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","document:line:24","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md:5-13","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:84-90","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:196","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — Gap 12 migration requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Label the context paragraph as standalone issue work rather than a standalone feature, and mention the applicable common-model contracts there so the empty HLD contract lists cannot suggest that no upstream requirements apply."]},{"chunkId":"completion","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The completion approach is coherent, but live completion can overlook missing declared Tasks, and the recovery path does not specify how a later approval override is durably recorded.","findings":[{"id":"completion-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/0","message":"Live Story completion needs to validate TASKS membership before evaluating counted Tasks. The proposed reader discovers existing child heads; a TASKS entry whose TASK head is absent never enters that listing. Consequently, an approved BUILD with clean review can complete the Story when the remaining Task heads pass, or when none exist. The design detects this condition only during repair, despite making TASKS authoritative for board membership. Specify live validation of listed Task heads, distinguish genuinely taskless routes from incomplete Task creation, and add approval-path tests for both cases.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.1, 2.3, 2.7 and 4","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts: countedChildren and ChildStatusReader","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: scanChildren","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts: TasksPayload.taskIds","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan and syncOnPlanApproval"]},{"id":"completion-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/1","message":"The promised recovery by approving again with an explicit override lacks a persistence contract. The first approval deliberately commits even when failed Tasks hold the Story. On the next approval, approveArtifactByJsonPath leaves an already-approved BUILD unchanged, so the new override is not recorded on its approval. The new storyApprovalOverride evidence is defined to read that recorded reason. It therefore either cannot release the hold, or relies on transient request context that disappears during deferred signoff completion or repair. Define an audited operation for recording the subsequent override without undoing the committed approval, and test initial hold → override retry → deferred completion/retry.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.1, 4 and 5","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md: explicit override is recorded on the BUILD approval","src/workflow/gates.ts: approveArtifactByJsonPath, approved-or-beyond branch at lines 690–699","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: CompletionEvidenceOptions.overrideReview and storedOverride","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: deferred completeIfRolledUp call"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: scanChildren","src/workflow/gates.ts: approval and completion paths","src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts","src/cli/services/workflow.ts: approveOutcomeOf","src/workflow/storage.ts: prepareArtifactWrite and lifecycleKeepingSignoffs","src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts: artifact persistence","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tracker/unit-head.ts","src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts: persistBuildRecord","src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts","src/workflow/resolve-comment.ts: resolveTargetQuestion","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: completion holds and deferred settlement","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-rollup.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-members.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/storage-signoff-history.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/gates-lifecycle-service.test.ts: override coverage","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/completion-evidence.test.ts: override coverage"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make the existing-lifecycle preservation change explicit in section 3.2. prepareArtifactWrite currently preserves an omitted incoming lifecycle only when prior signoff history exists; storage-signoff-history.test.ts explicitly expects lifecycle loss without that history. The proposed rewrite-preservation tests should cover identical and changed content without signoffs and replace that obsolete expectation.","Retain signoff holds in the completion integration tests, including a held Epic after its Story completes. The current service supports these holds, but the proposed test list does not explicitly exercise them."]},{"chunkId":"repair","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Repair discovery and historical settlement are defined, but the execution sequence omits legacy normalization prerequisites, partial-write reporting covers only settlement, and Task round backfill can confuse Task numbers with plan-row identities.","findings":[{"id":"repair-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/4","message":"The advertised repair-at-any-schema contract is incompatible with the specified execution order. Repair starts with applyFeedback and migrateHeads, but both use History with the stored artifact id; History rejects uppercase S001 ids. Normalizing Story discovery does not rename those files or references. Flat amendments also require conversion before migrateHeads, which skips records without meta. Specify the prerequisite normalization/conversion sequence, or explicitly route unconverted repositories through conversion first. Add repair fixtures containing uppercase heads with feedback and approved flat amendments.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.5, 3.5 and 6","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts: requireId, feedback and appendLog","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: STORY_RE and ArtifactIds.parse","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts: migrateHeads and applyConversion prerequisite ordering","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts: repairFlatAmendments","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts: uppercase heads with feedback and approved flat amendment fixture"]},{"id":"repair-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths","message":"Partial-write reporting is specified only for settlement failures, although feedback migration, head migration and unit/Task creation also perform multiple independent writes. For example, feedback and several migrated heads can commit before a later migration write fails. The existing handler catches such failures as { error }, losing the list of committed changes; the proposed design supplies no replacement reporting or continuation contract for these phases. Extend RepairReport handling across every mutating phase, define which dependent operations stop after a failure, and test a failure before settlement followed by a safe retry.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.4, 3.5, 4 and migration steps 4–5","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts: handleRepoConvert catch","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts: applyFeedback","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts: migrateHeads","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts: writeMigratedHead","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan"]},{"id":"repair-003","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/4","message":"Repair must use the plan-row identity when backfilling Task build rounds. The referenced applyTasks currently selects the first Task matching either planTaskId or its own Task number. When Task t1 represents plan row t2 and Task t2 represents row t1, a passing BUILD result for row t1 can therefore be written onto Task t1, which represents the wrong row. The design explicitly recognizes differing Task numbers and plan rows but corrects only the board join. Specify an unambiguous backfill join, preserve existing rounds, and test crossed identities before live-rule settlement.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.5–3.7 and differing Task-number edge case","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts: applyTasks set.tasks.find predicate","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan number allocation and existingTasks mapping","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts: existing fixtures use matching Task numbers and plan-row ids"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: S009 acceptance and lifecycle/identity constraints","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts","src/workflow/convert/run.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/rename.ts","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/backfill.ts","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts","src/workflow/convert/raw-heads.ts","src/workflow/convert/legacy-view.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar-store.ts","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts: approved lifecycle status mapping","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-preview.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-repeat.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: git reflog confirming main-to-v2 checkout on 2026-11-07","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: commit 5c5bc0cf1 src/workflow/storage.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Explicitly retain conversion verification regression coverage in the test strategy. The ISSUE names it as required behavior, and verifyConversion shares the loader, graph and gates changed here.","Add preview/apply parity checks covering proposed head creation and settlement, and PLAN eligibility tests for statuses beyond approved.","Define COMPLETION_RULE_FROM as an immutable timestamp with a timezone and document how it relates to daemon activation, so historical attribution remains stable across releases."]},{"chunkId":"board","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The board design addresses unit association, active Task membership, plan-row identity, ordering and lifecycle-based completion. Two contract gaps remain: DIAG records are omitted despite the all-common-kinds contract, and existing unit heads without lifecycles cannot be represented by the proposed unit field.","findings":[{"id":"board-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/5","message":"The proposed kind expansion still excludes DIAG, contradicting liftStoreFile's promise to accept every common-model kind and the ISSUE's expected behavior. DIAG is a registered common-model artifact with supported storage codecs and Story ownership. Adding only EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS leaves a valid DIAG head classified as unknown-kind, producing the same false unreadable notices this fix targets. Include DIAG in the loader/type contract and define its evidence association, with a valid DIAG fixture that loads without notices. Retain the explicitly intended TESTS exclusion.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.6, 3.6 and 5","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md: Expected behavior and Fix intent","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: ArtifactIdKind and SHAPES.DIAG","src/workflow/artifact-core/codecs.ts: CODECS registration for DIAG","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/pass-through-codecs.test.ts: supported DIAG heads","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts: kindOfFile and unknown-kind handling","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: S002 acceptance criteria ac4–ac6"]},{"id":"board-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/6","message":"The published unit shape cannot represent an existing EPIC, STORY or TASK head without a lifecycle. Section 3.7 requires status: Status and reserves unit: null for a missing head, while sections 2.6 and 3.8 explicitly admit heads without lifecycles as unmigrated. Status contains no unmigrated or unknown value. Consequently, this supported input requires inventing a lifecycle status, violating the null contract, or emitting an invalid snapshot. Define an explicit representation for an existing unmigrated unit, propagate it through stage derivation and client labels, and test it through the daemon snapshot and plugin details.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:237","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:249","src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts:105 — Status union","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts: assembleSnapshot and itemOf","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts: DeliveryItemView","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md: unmigrated records must be reported as needing migration"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/5","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts","src/workflow/delivery/types.ts","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts","src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts","src/workflow/delivery/currency.ts","src/workflow/delivery/notice.ts","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/tasks/__tests__/task-build-rounds.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts: Status","src/workflow/artifact-core/codecs.ts: registered kinds","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: taskBuildPassed","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: common-model kind definitions","src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts: recordTaskRound","src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/load.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/contract.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts: TaskRowView","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts: Task and Epic rendering source","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/delivery-client.test.ts","jetbrains-plugin: delivery-consumer search"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Define whether Task validation intentionally remains the BUILD record's result or follows the latest Task history round used by completion. These sources can differ; add coverage showing how the board explains a completion hold when its displayed BUILD result passed.","Add explicit tests for TASKS-authoritative membership, withdrawn/superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, missing unit migration notices and Task status presentation. Retain conversion-verification regression coverage alongside the new loader and graph tests.","Carry Task status through TaskRowView and the actual webview renderer, and verify the rendered result during implementation. No authored/generated visual artifacts or renderings accompany this LLD; the relationship prose adequately describes the model, and no visual verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"passed","summary":"Completed whole-design consistency review against the originating ISSUE, applicable common-model requirements, recorded decisions and all four current completed assessments. The live document matches the checkpoint baseline. No additional distinct defect was identified; the substantive chunks retain seven MED findings that require changes.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md: lifecycle completion, Task ownership and migration requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts: applyInQueue, completeIfRolledUp, completeMember and reopenMember","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json: attempt 3 completedChunks scope, completion, repair and board",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json: empty attachments and absence of visual definitions","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001: artifact inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Coordinate completion-001 with repair-001 and board-002: live completion, repair and board derivation need consistent handling of missing or unmigrated unit heads and authoritative TASKS membership.","Resolve completion-002 before relying on repair's live-rule settlement: a later explicit override must remain auditable and available after request context disappears.","Resolve repair-003 across migration and board fixtures so plan-row identity consistently determines Task evidence, completion eligibility and displayed validation.","Retain conversion-verification regression coverage explicitly. The originating ISSUE requires it, and verifyConversion consumes the loader, graph and gates changed here.","Define or replace acceptance labels ac1–ac6 with identifiable requirement text; the originating ISSUE supplies narrative requirements rather than those numbered criteria.","Qualify the invariant that no Task completes unless its Story does: the documented partial-write recovery deliberately permits completed members before the Story head commits.","No authored or generated diagrams or renderings accompany this LLD. Relationship prose adequately describes the model; no visual verification is claimed. Verify the Task status rendering through the actual webview during implementation."]}],"progress":{"status":"changes_requested","phase":"complete","completedChunks":5,"totalChunks":5,"lastMeaningfulActivityAt":null,"activeToolCount":0,"requiresUserInput":false,"checkpointPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","sequence":0,"reviewElapsedMs":0,"unitElapsedMs":null,"observedAt":"2026-11-09T13:07:48.472Z","freshness":"stored"},"startedAt":"2026-11-09T12:57:57.393Z","reviewer":"daemon","unit":{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","executionId":"775579da-579b-4af3-99fe-de9fc4970470","dispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[]},"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","plan":{"chunks":[{"id":"scope","title":"Issue scope, upstream requirements and design decisions","selectors":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","document:line:24","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8"],"concerns":["Trace the design to the originating ISSUE reproduction, root causes, fix intent and explicit exclusions.","Read the common-model DEF and DECISIONS.md; establish applicable lifecycle requirements and authorized divergences without inventing HLD ancestry.","Assess ownership boundaries, shared contracts, scope completeness and unresolved decisions."],"dependsOn":[],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"completion","title":"Lifecycle completion, approval propagation and first-write integrity","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/citations/0","/citations/1"],"concerns":["Inspect rollUp, unitMembers, CompletionEvidence and completeThroughService against actual lifecycle, task-round and review contracts.","Check declared-Story completeness, counted-child eligibility, cascade ownership, frozenBy attribution and reopening behavior.","Inspect approval follow-on merging through daemon and CLI, committed-approval failure handling and retry feasibility.","Verify first-write lifecycle coverage and preservation of existing lifecycles against production write paths.","Assess completion alternatives, relevant error paths and unit/integration test coverage."],"dependsOn":["scope"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"repair","title":"Repair planning, migration execution and recovery","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9"],"concerns":["Inspect repair modes, report types and conversion integration at every schema version while preserving existing conversion behavior.","Check discovery, identity normalization, head creation, PLAN eligibility, TASKS integrity and feedback preservation in execution order.","Assess historical approval cutoff, migration attribution and live-rule settlement against owner decisions and lifecycle contracts.","Check preview fidelity, idempotency, partial-write reporting, held versus failed classification and retry behavior.","Verify migration evidence and citations, release ordering, compatibility, rollback claims and relevant tests, including conversion verification."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"board","title":"Common-model board derivation and client contracts","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/5"],"concerns":["Inspect loader acceptance of common-model kinds, lifecycle-only approval, unmigrated notices and retained TESTS exclusion.","Check graph ownership/cardinality, unit-head association, active Task membership, PLAN fallback, plan-row identity and ordering.","Trace lifecycle status through snapshot, gate, daemon contract, VS Code details, views and labels; assess applicable current-client IPC compatibility.","Check completed versus build-recorded behavior, Epic progress and Task validation/status presentation against originating requirements.","Inspect necessary relationship and UX artifacts and actual renderings where available; assess board, contract and conversion-verification test coverage."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Whole-design requirement and contract consistency","selectors":[],"concerns":["Check missing ISSUE requirements and acceptance traceability across all substantive assessments.","Reconcile completion, repair and board contracts, failure semantics, lifecycle ownership, ordering and compatibility claims.","Check actual upstream alignment, citation support, necessary artifact verification and cross-chunk contradictions.","Ensure demonstrated findings, advice and inspection limitations remain distinct and the final status follows the required precedence."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 25 inventory units map to substantive chunks. Broad contract, model, error and test selectors intentionally recur so each implementation responsibility is reviewed with its interfaces, logic, failures and verification together. Citation ownership follows the behavior it supports. Scope establishes upstream applicability, completion defines lifecycle behavior, repair applies it to stored records, and the board consumes the resulting model. The final consistency chunk depends on every substantive chunk and does not substitute for unit coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["board"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/8","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/9","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"document:line:24","chunkIds":["scope"]}]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"planning","phase":"planning","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"completion","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"repair","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"board","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"delivery-board-lld-s1","attempt":3,"artifactId":"LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1","status":"changes_requested","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":7,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned scope sections align with the originating ISSUE’s reader, lifecycle, repair and recurrence-prevention requirements. The common-model DEF and recorded owner decisions establish the applicable contracts without requiring HLD ancestry. The LLD explicitly describes its Task-completion divergence, preserves the explicit-override requirement for live approvals, and distinguishes historical migration settlement. No blocking scope defect was identified.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","document:line:24","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md:5-13","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:84-90","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:196","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — Gap 12 migration requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Label the context paragraph as standalone issue work rather than a standalone feature, and mention the applicable common-model contracts there so the empty HLD contract lists cannot suggest that no upstream requirements apply."]},{"chunkId":"completion","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The completion approach is coherent, but live completion can overlook missing declared Tasks, and the recovery path does not specify how a later approval override is durably recorded.","findings":[{"id":"completion-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/0","message":"Live Story completion needs to validate TASKS membership before evaluating counted Tasks. The proposed reader discovers existing child heads; a TASKS entry whose TASK head is absent never enters that listing. Consequently, an approved BUILD with clean review can complete the Story when the remaining Task heads pass, or when none exist. The design detects this condition only during repair, despite making TASKS authoritative for board membership. Specify live validation of listed Task heads, distinguish genuinely taskless routes from incomplete Task creation, and add approval-path tests for both cases.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.1, 2.3, 2.7 and 4","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts: countedChildren and ChildStatusReader","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: scanChildren","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts: TasksPayload.taskIds","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan and syncOnPlanApproval"]},{"id":"completion-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/1","message":"The promised recovery by approving again with an explicit override lacks a persistence contract. The first approval deliberately commits even when failed Tasks hold the Story. On the next approval, approveArtifactByJsonPath leaves an already-approved BUILD unchanged, so the new override is not recorded on its approval. The new storyApprovalOverride evidence is defined to read that recorded reason. It therefore either cannot release the hold, or relies on transient request context that disappears during deferred signoff completion or repair. Define an audited operation for recording the subsequent override without undoing the committed approval, and test initial hold → override retry → deferred completion/retry.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.1, 4 and 5","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md: explicit override is recorded on the BUILD approval","src/workflow/gates.ts: approveArtifactByJsonPath, approved-or-beyond branch at lines 690–699","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: CompletionEvidenceOptions.overrideReview and storedOverride","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: deferred completeIfRolledUp call"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: scanChildren","src/workflow/gates.ts: approval and completion paths","src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts","src/cli/services/workflow.ts: approveOutcomeOf","src/workflow/storage.ts: prepareArtifactWrite and lifecycleKeepingSignoffs","src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts: artifact persistence","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tracker/unit-head.ts","src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts: persistBuildRecord","src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts","src/workflow/resolve-comment.ts: resolveTargetQuestion","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: completion holds and deferred settlement","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-rollup.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-members.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/storage-signoff-history.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/gates-lifecycle-service.test.ts: override coverage","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/completion-evidence.test.ts: override coverage"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make the existing-lifecycle preservation change explicit in section 3.2. prepareArtifactWrite currently preserves an omitted incoming lifecycle only when prior signoff history exists; storage-signoff-history.test.ts explicitly expects lifecycle loss without that history. The proposed rewrite-preservation tests should cover identical and changed content without signoffs and replace that obsolete expectation.","Retain signoff holds in the completion integration tests, including a held Epic after its Story completes. The current service supports these holds, but the proposed test list does not explicitly exercise them."]},{"chunkId":"repair","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Repair discovery and historical settlement are defined, but the execution sequence omits legacy normalization prerequisites, partial-write reporting covers only settlement, and Task round backfill can confuse Task numbers with plan-row identities.","findings":[{"id":"repair-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/4","message":"The advertised repair-at-any-schema contract is incompatible with the specified execution order. Repair starts with applyFeedback and migrateHeads, but both use History with the stored artifact id; History rejects uppercase S001 ids. Normalizing Story discovery does not rename those files or references. Flat amendments also require conversion before migrateHeads, which skips records without meta. Specify the prerequisite normalization/conversion sequence, or explicitly route unconverted repositories through conversion first. Add repair fixtures containing uppercase heads with feedback and approved flat amendments.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.5, 3.5 and 6","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts: requireId, feedback and appendLog","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: STORY_RE and ArtifactIds.parse","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts: migrateHeads and applyConversion prerequisite ordering","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts: repairFlatAmendments","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts: uppercase heads with feedback and approved flat amendment fixture"]},{"id":"repair-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths","message":"Partial-write reporting is specified only for settlement failures, although feedback migration, head migration and unit/Task creation also perform multiple independent writes. For example, feedback and several migrated heads can commit before a later migration write fails. The existing handler catches such failures as { error }, losing the list of committed changes; the proposed design supplies no replacement reporting or continuation contract for these phases. Extend RepairReport handling across every mutating phase, define which dependent operations stop after a failure, and test a failure before settlement followed by a safe retry.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.4, 3.5, 4 and migration steps 4–5","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts: handleRepoConvert catch","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts: applyFeedback","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts: migrateHeads","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts: writeMigratedHead","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan"]},{"id":"repair-003","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/4","message":"Repair must use the plan-row identity when backfilling Task build rounds. The referenced applyTasks currently selects the first Task matching either planTaskId or its own Task number. When Task t1 represents plan row t2 and Task t2 represents row t1, a passing BUILD result for row t1 can therefore be written onto Task t1, which represents the wrong row. The design explicitly recognizes differing Task numbers and plan rows but corrects only the board join. Specify an unambiguous backfill join, preserve existing rounds, and test crossed identities before live-rule settlement.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.5–3.7 and differing Task-number edge case","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts: applyTasks set.tasks.find predicate","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan number allocation and existingTasks mapping","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts: existing fixtures use matching Task numbers and plan-row ids"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: S009 acceptance and lifecycle/identity constraints","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts","src/workflow/convert/run.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/rename.ts","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/backfill.ts","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts","src/workflow/convert/raw-heads.ts","src/workflow/convert/legacy-view.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar-store.ts","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts: approved lifecycle status mapping","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-preview.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-repeat.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: git reflog confirming main-to-v2 checkout on 2026-11-07","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: commit 5c5bc0cf1 src/workflow/storage.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Explicitly retain conversion verification regression coverage in the test strategy. The ISSUE names it as required behavior, and verifyConversion shares the loader, graph and gates changed here.","Add preview/apply parity checks covering proposed head creation and settlement, and PLAN eligibility tests for statuses beyond approved.","Define COMPLETION_RULE_FROM as an immutable timestamp with a timezone and document how it relates to daemon activation, so historical attribution remains stable across releases."]},{"chunkId":"board","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The board design addresses unit association, active Task membership, plan-row identity, ordering and lifecycle-based completion. Two contract gaps remain: DIAG records are omitted despite the all-common-kinds contract, and existing unit heads without lifecycles cannot be represented by the proposed unit field.","findings":[{"id":"board-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/5","message":"The proposed kind expansion still excludes DIAG, contradicting liftStoreFile's promise to accept every common-model kind and the ISSUE's expected behavior. DIAG is a registered common-model artifact with supported storage codecs and Story ownership. Adding only EPIC, STORY, TASK and TASKS leaves a valid DIAG head classified as unknown-kind, producing the same false unreadable notices this fix targets. Include DIAG in the loader/type contract and define its evidence association, with a valid DIAG fixture that loads without notices. Retain the explicitly intended TESTS exclusion.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.6, 3.6 and 5","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md: Expected behavior and Fix intent","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: ArtifactIdKind and SHAPES.DIAG","src/workflow/artifact-core/codecs.ts: CODECS registration for DIAG","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/pass-through-codecs.test.ts: supported DIAG heads","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts: kindOfFile and unknown-kind handling","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: S002 acceptance criteria ac4–ac6"]},{"id":"board-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/6","message":"The published unit shape cannot represent an existing EPIC, STORY or TASK head without a lifecycle. Section 3.7 requires status: Status and reserves unit: null for a missing head, while sections 2.6 and 3.8 explicitly admit heads without lifecycles as unmigrated. Status contains no unmigrated or unknown value. Consequently, this supported input requires inventing a lifecycle status, violating the null contract, or emitting an invalid snapshot. Define an explicit representation for an existing unmigrated unit, propagate it through stage derivation and client labels, and test it through the daemon snapshot and plugin details.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:237","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:249","src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts:105 — Status union","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts: assembleSnapshot and itemOf","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts: DeliveryItemView","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md: unmigrated records must be reported as needing migration"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/5","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts","src/workflow/delivery/types.ts","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts","src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts","src/workflow/delivery/currency.ts","src/workflow/delivery/notice.ts","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/tasks/__tests__/task-build-rounds.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts: Status","src/workflow/artifact-core/codecs.ts: registered kinds","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: taskBuildPassed","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts: common-model kind definitions","src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts: recordTaskRound","src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/load.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/contract.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts: TaskRowView","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts: Task and Epic rendering source","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/delivery-client.test.ts","jetbrains-plugin: delivery-consumer search"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Define whether Task validation intentionally remains the BUILD record's result or follows the latest Task history round used by completion. These sources can differ; add coverage showing how the board explains a completion hold when its displayed BUILD result passed.","Add explicit tests for TASKS-authoritative membership, withdrawn/superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, missing unit migration notices and Task status presentation. Retain conversion-verification regression coverage alongside the new loader and graph tests.","Carry Task status through TaskRowView and the actual webview renderer, and verify the rendered result during implementation. No authored/generated visual artifacts or renderings accompany this LLD; the relationship prose adequately describes the model, and no visual verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"passed","summary":"Completed whole-design consistency review against the originating ISSUE, applicable common-model requirements, recorded decisions and all four current completed assessments. The live document matches the checkpoint baseline. No additional distinct defect was identified; the substantive chunks retain seven MED findings that require changes.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md: lifecycle completion, Task ownership and migration requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts: applyInQueue, completeIfRolledUp, completeMember and reopenMember","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json: attempt 3 completedChunks scope, completion, repair and board",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json: empty attachments and absence of visual definitions","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001: artifact inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Coordinate completion-001 with repair-001 and board-002: live completion, repair and board derivation need consistent handling of missing or unmigrated unit heads and authoritative TASKS membership.","Resolve completion-002 before relying on repair's live-rule settlement: a later explicit override must remain auditable and available after request context disappears.","Resolve repair-003 across migration and board fixtures so plan-row identity consistently determines Task evidence, completion eligibility and displayed validation.","Retain conversion-verification regression coverage explicitly. The originating ISSUE requires it, and verifyConversion consumes the loader, graph and gates changed here.","Define or replace acceptance labels ac1–ac6 with identifiable requirement text; the originating ISSUE supplies narrative requirements rather than those numbered criteria.","Qualify the invariant that no Task completes unless its Story does: the documented partial-write recovery deliberately permits completed members before the Story head commits.","No authored or generated diagrams or renderings accompany this LLD. Relationship prose adequately describes the model; no visual verification is claimed. Verify the Task status rendering through the actual webview during implementation."]}],"limitations":[],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"fedc7d32a036c4fc9c9df730184ac4c886076fbf560c43e268adffe7e76108e6"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-09T13:07:48.472Z"},{"number":4,"status":"changes_requested","preparationKind":"impact","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"30aaeaf6469ee60cac028004f7f0083e95e604d5da034c5a13408994286b28e5","document":"27a86da5b3a8d09df803de2ac001e66264f636c7b049398ccb2f831c63a52030"},"contentIdentity":"3cb9ac15ef2beee2cf8dcaa44bc61971868b9552c76c7c6fa4c3395db91d3b02","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"design.story\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794229933602-ie4di8\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-09T13:17:16.709Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-09T05:00:05.847Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-claude\",\n          \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 302735,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"eedc4519199b24b4\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact\",\n    \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n    \"hldBaseRunId\": \"wf-1794229933602-ie4di8\",\n    \"hldEffectiveHash\": \"1d17e3d5a79a2451328357e8be478671c72e4fd4fffad3a446232ea754fa0073\",\n    \"hldAmendmentsApplied\": [],\n    \"storyTitle\": \"Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\",\n    \"standalone\": true,\n    \"sizeClass\": \"bugfix\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"envelope\": {\n      \"attachments\": []\n    },\n    \"revision\": 4\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"audience\": \"product\",\n      \"prose\": \"Approving a build now really completes its Story and Tasks and, once every Story the Epic declares is done, the Epic, which never happened before. A Task that failed its latest build, or was never finished, holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override, which can also be given after the first approval. New records have a lifecycle from the moment they are written. A repair run brings existing records up to date at any schema version and reports, step by step, what it planned, did, held and could not do. The delivery board shows Epic, Story and Task status from those records.\"\n    },\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\"\n      },\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {}\n    },\n    \"contractDetails\": {\n      \"surfaceLevel\": \"internal-shared\",\n      \"api\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"rollUp\",\n          \"signature\": \"rollUp(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader, evidence: CompletionEvidence): Promise<Status | undefined>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"id\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The TASK, STORY or EPIC head to evaluate\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reader\",\n              \"type\": \"ChildStatusReader\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Reads child listings and statuses\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"evidence\",\n              \"type\": \"CompletionEvidence\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Build, review, Task-list, override and declared-Story facts\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<Status | undefined>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"'completed' when the condition holds. TASK: its latest build round passed (unchanged). STORY: its BUILD is approved, its review is clean or overridden, and either storyTasks answers none-required, or storyTasks answers listed and every listed Task that is not withdrawn or superseded has a head whose latest round passed, or the BUILD's approval carries an explicit override. A listed Task with no head, and an answer of not-created, count as unfinished. EPIC: every counted Story is completed, and every Story its DEF declares has a head that is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"UnreadableChildError\",\n              \"condition\": \"A head of the counted child kind cannot be read\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"id parses as an artifact id\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Reads only\",\n            \"A STORY's condition reads each Task's latest round, not its status, so a later failing round always counts\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"unitMembers\",\n          \"signature\": \"unitMembers(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader): Promise<string[]>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"id\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The unit\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reader\",\n              \"type\": \"ChildStatusReader\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Reads the unit's children\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<string[]>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"For a STORY, also its TASK children, so its open Tasks complete with it\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"A member that is completed, withdrawn or superseded is left alone, as completeMember already does\",\n            \"Each frozen Task's log entry names the Story in frozenBy, and reopening the Story reopens the Tasks it froze\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"approveArtifactByJsonPath\",\n          \"signature\": \"approveArtifactByJsonPath(jsonPath: string, opts: ApproveOptions): Promise<ApprovalResult>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"jsonPath\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The record being approved\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"opts\",\n              \"type\": \"ApproveOptions\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The lifecycle service, actor and any override reason\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<ApprovalResult>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"As today. For a BUILD already approved or in signoff that is given an explicit override different from the one it carries, the override is first saved by the 'record-override' operation.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"IllegalTransitionError\",\n              \"condition\": \"The BUILD's status does not allow an override to be recorded, for example it is completed\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"The BUILD's status, revision and approval time do not change when an override is recorded\",\n            \"Other kinds, and a repeat of the same reason, record nothing\",\n            \"The batch approval then runs completeThroughService, so the held Story completes when the rule now holds\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"completeThroughService\",\n          \"signature\": \"completeThroughService(jsonPath: string): Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"jsonPath\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The approved record's path\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"For a BUILD, an outcome of kind 'story-completion' with ok, a note and the ids completed. Undefined for other kinds. It never rejects.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"The record was just approved or re-approved\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"The Story's and Epic's heads, and a head for every Story the DEF declares, exist before the walk\",\n            \"The walk starts at the STORY, and the only path that completes a Task is its Story's cascade\",\n            \"A failure leaves the approval standing and is reported with ok false\",\n            \"A Story held back is reported with ok true and a note naming the Tasks that hold it, including listed Tasks with no head\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"handleWorkflowApprove\",\n          \"signature\": \"handleWorkflowApprove(params: unknown, deps?: WorkflowApproveDeps): Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"params\",\n              \"type\": \"WorkflowApproveRequest\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The approval request\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"deps\",\n              \"type\": \"WorkflowApproveDeps\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The post-approval seam\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"followOn holds the approval's own outcomes followed by the seam's\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"A seam that returns outcomes no longer discards the story-completion outcome\",\n            \"src/cli/services/workflow.ts exposes the story-completion outcome in its result\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"handleRepoConvert\",\n          \"signature\": \"handleRepoConvert(params: unknown, repoEnv: string | undefined): Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"params\",\n              \"type\": \"RepoConvertParams\",\n              \"purpose\": \"repo and mode; mode gains 'repair-preview' and 'repair'\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"repoEnv\",\n              \"type\": \"string | undefined\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Fallback repository path\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Repair modes answer a RepairReport and work at any schema version. Once a repair has begun writing it always answers a RepairReport; { error } means nothing was written.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"{ error: string }\",\n              \"condition\": \"Unknown mode, or a repository that is not a directory, or the plan lists a problem such as a rename collision, in which case nothing is written\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"'repair-preview' writes nothing and lists the same changes 'repair' then applies\",\n            \"A second 'repair' lists no changes\",\n            \"The schema marker and the preview and apply modes are unchanged\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"applyTasks\",\n          \"signature\": \"applyTasks(repo: string, deps: ConversionDeps): Promise<TasksResult>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"repo\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The repository\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"deps\",\n              \"type\": \"ConversionDeps\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Store, history and Task sets\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<TasksResult>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"The Task sets created and the Tasks given a back-filled round\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"A BUILD result is matched to a Task by planTaskId alone, so a Task whose number equals another Task's plan row cannot receive it\",\n            \"A Task that already has a build round is left as it is\",\n            \"A PLAN at approved or any later status qualifies, as the units step does for repair\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"liftStoreFile\",\n          \"signature\": \"liftStoreFile(fileName: string, parsed: unknown): ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"fileName\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The store file name\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"parsed\",\n              \"type\": \"unknown\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The parsed file\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\",\n            \"meaning\": \"A record for every kind of the common model, including DIAG; TESTS stays deliberately skipped. A head with no lifecycle has approval state 'unmigrated'.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"No legacy approval field is read\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"buildWorkItemGraph\",\n          \"signature\": \"buildWorkItemGraph(recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet): WorkItemGraph\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"recordSet\",\n              \"type\": \"ArtifactRecordSet\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The loaded records\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"WorkItemGraph\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Each epic, story and task node carries its unit head, or null. A story's tasks come from its TASKS head when it has one, else from its PLAN.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Unit records are not counted as evidence; a DIAG head is evidence of the Story its id names\",\n            \"Active Tasks are those the TASKS head lists and that are not withdrawn or superseded\",\n            \"A task node carries planRowId and taskOrder from its TASK head\",\n            \"For a task node with a head, sourceIds holds the plan row id and not the Task's own number, so no alias can collide with another Task's plan row\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"storyStage\",\n          \"signature\": \"storyStage(route: DeliveryRoute, evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[], issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined, unit: UnitHead | null): { stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"route\",\n              \"type\": \"DeliveryRoute\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The story's route\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"evidence\",\n              \"type\": \"readonly ArtifactRecord[]\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The story's records\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"issue\",\n              \"type\": \"ArtifactRecord | undefined\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The issue behind a fix story\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"unit\",\n              \"type\": \"UnitHead | null\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The STORY head\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"{ stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\",\n            \"meaning\": \"'complete' only when the STORY head is completed. An approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays 'build-recorded', and its text states the STORY head's status, that the head is not migrated, or that there is no STORY head.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [],\n          \"preconditions\": [],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"An approved BUILD alone no longer yields 'complete'\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dataModelChanges\": [\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"CompletionEvidence\",\n        \"change\": \"field-add\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds storyBuildApproved(epicHash, storyId), true when the BUILD status is approved or later; storyApprovalOverride(epicHash, storyId), the explicit override reason on the BUILD's approval, or undefined; declaredStories(epicHash), the Story ids the DEF lists, empty when there is no DEF; and storyTasks(epicHash, storyId), answering { kind: 'listed'; taskIds: string[] } | { kind: 'not-created' } | { kind: 'none-required' }. listed holds the TASKS head's ids when it has at least one, else the Story's child TASK heads when there are any. Otherwise not-created when the Story's PLAN is approved or later, because Task creation did not finish, and none-required when it has no such PLAN, as on a small bugfix or trivial route. A clean review is not an override. The override extends k8 by the decision recorded in DECISIONS.md: on the BUILD approval it also waives failed or unfinished Tasks.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:48\",\n          \"src/workflow/tasks/types.ts:30\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Lifecycle operation record-override\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"A new lifecycle operation, valid on a BUILD whose status is approved, in-signoff or signed-off. It sets lifecycle.approval.override to the reason and leaves the status, the revision and the approval time unchanged. It appends one log entry with the actor, the time and outcome { result: 'override', summary: reason }, so the audit trail keeps each override even if a later one replaces it on the head. The reason is then found by storedOverride and storyApprovalOverride after the request is gone, including in deferred signoff completion and repair. The relationship is one BUILD approval to at most one current override and any number of logged ones.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/gates.ts:690\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:41\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts:20\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:41\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"New and rewritten workflow heads\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"Both sites that write a finished workflow artifact call one helper in src/workflow/storage.ts that settles meta.lifecycle before the write. No prior head, or a prior head with no lifecycle: a draft lifecycle. A prior head with a lifecycle and unchanged content: that lifecycle. A prior head with a lifecycle and changed content: a draft for the new revision, keeping its Signoff entries, because approval and review belong to the revision they were made at. Only these two sites change, so the writeArtifact behaviour that storage-signoff-history.test.ts pins stays as it is. Today such a head has no lifecycle until a lifecycle operation adds one, and a rewrite drops one that has no Signoff entries. A guard test fails if a production 'content' write of a delivery kind can create a head without a lifecycle.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93\",\n          \"src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349\",\n          \"src/workflow/storage.ts:178\",\n          \"src/workflow/storage.ts:224\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"FollowOnOutcome\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds kind 'story-completion' and optional completed: string[]. Additive.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/gates.ts:854\",\n          \"src/workflow/gates.ts:881\",\n          \"src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts:58\",\n          \"src/cli/services/workflow.ts:152\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"RepairReport\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"{ mode: 'repair-preview' | 'repair'; plan: ConversionPlan; result?: { applied: ConversionChange[]; remaining: ConversionChange[]; stoppedAt?: { step: RepairStep; reason: string }; held: UnitOutcome[]; failed: UnitOutcome[] } }, where UnitOutcome is { artifactId, reason, completedMembers: string[] } and RepairStep is every conversion step except the marker, plus 'settle'. After the run the plan is computed again from the files: remaining is what it still lists, and applied is every planned change it no longer lists. This covers every step without each one having to report its own writes. A step that throws stops the run, stoppedAt names it, and later steps do not run because each depends on the one before; nothing settles after a stop. Settling alone continues per unit: held units were left by the completion rule or a signoff hold, and failed ones hit a conflict or write error. completedMembers lists members already completed when a settlement failed. ConversionRule gains 'settle-unit'.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/convert/types.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/repo-convert.ts:54\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Repair order, discovery and eligibility\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"Repair runs the conversion's own steps in their fixed order, each of which can be repeated: applyRenames, applyStamps, applyAmendments, applyFeedback, migrateHeads, applyUnits, applyTasks, applyStoryHistory, then settle. Renames come first because History refuses an uppercase Story id, and amendments before migration because migrateHeads skips a record with no meta. It does not use the progress file or write the schema marker. A plan with a problem writes nothing, as conversion does. This store has 152 uppercase heads, no collisions and no flat amendments. A Story is known from a DEF declaration or from any LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR head naming its hash and story id, with S001 read as s1 in the preview, before the rename has run; each known hash gets an EPIC head. An ISSUE with no such record creates nothing. A PLAN qualifies for Tasks at approved or any later status. A TASKS head listing a Task with no head is reported as failed and left unchanged, and the Story is not settled; this store has none. Settling: COMPLETION_RULE_FROM is a fixed UTC timestamp with a Z suffix, written into the code when this change is committed and never recomputed, so the attribution of old approvals cannot move between releases. A Story whose BUILD approval time is before it is settled with storyCodeReview answering overridden and storyApprovalOverride answering 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration, because that approval passed the gate of its time. A later approval, including one made before the new daemon is running, is settled only by the live rule, so repair cannot complete a Story the live rule holds and such a Story is reported in result.held.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/rename.ts:135\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/amendments.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/units.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:92\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts:29\",\n          \"src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:154\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"DeliveryArtifactKind\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"Adds EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and DIAG. Relationship: one EPIC head has many STORY heads (by epicHash); one STORY has zero or one TASKS head, zero or more TASK heads and zero or more DIAG heads (by epicHash and storyId); a TASK references one plan row by planTaskId, and re-planning can change that row while the Task keeps its number. Each work item references at most one unit head of its own level, in the direction item to head. TESTS stays skipped by name.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/types.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:49\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"WorkItemNode, DeliveryItem and TaskValidation\",\n        \"change\": \"field-add\",\n        \"details\": \"WorkItemNode and DeliveryItem add unit: { artifactId: string; status: UnitStatus } | null, where UnitStatus is Status | 'unmigrated'. unit is set for epics, stories and tasks, is null only when there is no head, and has status 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. They also add planRowId: string | null and taskOrder: number | null for tasks. TaskValidation adds taskOrder; a story's tasks array is sorted by taskOrder, then by task item id. A task's validation result stays the one in the BUILD record, and the Story roll-up uses the Task's latest round: the two can differ, in which case the row can show passed while its Story is held, and the reason is in the approval's story-completion note. board-details.ts joins PLAN rows and dependencies on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null, and the client renders the tasks array in the order it receives. The plugin shows an Epic as complete only when its unit status is completed, keeps the child count as progress, and carries a Task's unit status through TaskRowView to the webview beside its validation result.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/types.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"ApprovalState, NoticeCode and AttentionReason\",\n        \"change\": \"field-modify\",\n        \"details\": \"ApprovalState adds 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. NoticeCode and AttentionReason add 'needs-migration', raised for an unmigrated record or a story, epic or active task with no head or an unmigrated head, so such a record never counts as pending-decision. The plugin gains labels for these and for the unmigrated unit status.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35\",\n          \"src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"interactionWithShared\": [],\n    \"errorPaths\": {\n      \"errorCases\": [\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The completion walk fails after the BUILD approval is committed, for example a child head cannot be read or a write conflicts.\",\n          \"detection\": \"completeThroughService catches the rejection from completeIfRolledUp or from ensuring the heads.\",\n          \"response\": \"The approval stands. The answer carries a story-completion outcome with ok false and the failure as its note; handleWorkflowApprove merges it with the seam's outcomes so it reaches the caller.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The build shows as approved and the caller is told the Story did not complete and why. A re-approval or a repair run finishes it.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A listed Task's latest build round failed, a listed Task has no round or no head, or Task creation did not finish, and the BUILD approval carries no explicit override.\",\n          \"detection\": \"rollUp for the STORY reads storyTasks, then statusOf and taskBuildPassed for each listed Task, then storyApprovalOverride.\",\n          \"response\": \"rollUp returns undefined, so the Story and its Tasks are left unchanged. The outcome has ok true and a note naming the Tasks that hold it.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The approval is recorded and the Story stays open on the board. Approving the BUILD again with an explicit override records the reason and completes the Story.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"An override is given for a BUILD whose status does not allow one to be recorded, for example it is completed.\",\n          \"detection\": \"nextLifecycle refuses 'record-override' from that status with IllegalTransitionError.\",\n          \"response\": \"The batch approval lists the path in skipped with the reason, and nothing changes.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The caller is told the override was not recorded.\",\n          \"recoverable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A repair step throws part-way, for example a write fails during head migration.\",\n          \"detection\": \"The repair runner catches the throw around each step and computes the plan again from the files.\",\n          \"response\": \"The run stops, later steps do not run and nothing settles. The answer is a RepairReport with stoppedAt, applied and remaining, not { error }.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The report shows the step, why it stopped, what was written and what is left. Running repair again continues from the files, and a step's earlier writes are not repeated.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"The repair plan lists a problem, such as a renamed file colliding with a different existing one.\",\n          \"detection\": \"planConversion lists it in plan.problems before any write.\",\n          \"response\": \"It answers { error } naming the problems and writes nothing, as conversion does.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The store is untouched and the conflicting files are named.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A repair settlement fails after some of the unit's members were already completed, because members are written one at a time before the unit head.\",\n          \"detection\": \"The settle step catches the write failure for that unit and re-reads each member's status.\",\n          \"response\": \"The unit is listed in result.failed with reason and completedMembers. Other units continue. A later repair run completes the rest, and completeMember skips the members already terminal.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The report names the unit and the members already completed; running repair again finishes it.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A TASKS head lists a Task id that has no TASK head during repair.\",\n          \"detection\": \"The repair's Task step compares the TASKS listing against the store's TASK heads.\",\n          \"response\": \"The Story is listed in result.failed, is left unchanged and is not settled; createFromPlan is not run over it.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The report names the Story and the missing Task for manual attention. This store has none today.\",\n          \"recoverable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"A store file is unreadable or is not a recognised artifact when the board loads.\",\n          \"detection\": \"liftStoreFile returns a RecordLoadFailure for the file.\",\n          \"response\": \"The failure is reported as a load notice, as today, and the rest of the board is built.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The board still opens and shows a notice for that file.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"repo.convert receives an unknown mode, or a repository path that is not a directory.\",\n          \"detection\": \"handleRepoConvert validates the mode against the accepted set and checks the path.\",\n          \"response\": \"It answers { error } and writes nothing.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The caller sees the reason and nothing changes.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"edgeCases\": [\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Story with an approved BUILD and clean review, no TASKS head, no child TASK heads and no PLAN at approved or later, such as a small bugfix or trivial route.\",\n          \"expected\": \"storyTasks answers none-required and it completes.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Story with an approved PLAN and no TASKS head or child TASK heads.\",\n          \"expected\": \"storyTasks answers not-created, and the Story is held unless the approval carries an override.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Story held by a failed Task, then the BUILD is approved again with an explicit override.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The override is saved on the approval and logged, the status, revision and approval time do not change, and the Story completes.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A BUILD approved again with the override it already carries.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Nothing new is recorded; completion is attempted again.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A held Story's override was recorded, and the Story is in signoff so it completes later.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The deferred completion reads the stored override and completes it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An Epic's signoff hold after its last Story completes.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The Story completes, the Epic stays open until its signoff finishes, and the outcome says so.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Task's earlier round passed and its latest round failed.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The latest round decides, so the Story is held back without an override.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A listed Task is withdrawn or superseded.\",\n          \"expected\": \"It is not counted, and the cascade leaves it alone.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An Epic whose DEF declares a Story that has no head.\",\n          \"expected\": \"completeThroughService creates the head first, and the Epic stays open until that Story is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An Epic with no DEF, such as a standalone ISSUE route.\",\n          \"expected\": \"declaredStories is empty and the Epic rolls up from its counted Stories only.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with Tasks whose latest round failed.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair settles it with the override 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A BUILD approved on or after COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with a failed latest round and no explicit override.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair does not complete it and lists it in result.held.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Task t1 represents plan row t2 and Task t2 represents plan row t1.\",\n          \"expected\": \"A BUILD result for row t1 goes to Task t2 in repair, and the board joins each Task to its own row.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A Task that already has a build round when repair back-fills.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Its rounds are left as they are.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A head with an uppercase Story id and body.feedback.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair renames it first, then saves the feedback under the new id, then migrates it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An approved flat amendment.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair converts it to a head before migration, and it stays approved.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Repair is run twice, or again after stopping part-way.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The second run after a complete one lists no changes, and a run after a stop lists only what remained, with no feedback line added twice.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A repository with no artifact records.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Repair reports an empty plan and writes nothing.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"An ISSUE with no DEF, LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR naming its hash.\",\n          \"expected\": \"No EPIC or STORY head is created for it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A head with no lifecycle is loaded by the board, including an EPIC, STORY or TASK head.\",\n          \"expected\": \"Its approval state is 'unmigrated', a unit head has unit.status 'unmigrated', it raises needs-migration and it does not count as pending-decision.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A DIAG head in the store.\",\n          \"expected\": \"It loads with no notice and is evidence of the Story its id names.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A finished workflow artifact is written again over a head with a lifecycle and no Signoff entries, with changed content.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The head gets a draft lifecycle for the new revision, so it never has none.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"The same, with unchanged content.\",\n          \"expected\": \"The lifecycle is kept.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"invariantsToPreserve\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"An approval that was committed is never undone by a later completion failure.\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"A Task is completed only through its Story's cascade, so a held Story leaves its Tasks unchanged and an earlier status cannot hide a later failing round. A write failure part-way through a cascade can leave some members completed before the Story head; the next run finishes the unit.\",\n          \"source\": \"c2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Approved records stay approved through repair, and repair preview writes nothing.\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Local feedback on a record is carried through head migration, and no line is added twice on a re-run.\",\n          \"source\": \"c4\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"testStrategy\": {\n      \"testFramework\": \"node:test via tsx; vscode-plugin uses its own node:test run\",\n      \"testLevels\": [\n        {\n          \"level\": \"unit\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The completion rule, evidence, cascade and board derivation, on in-memory fixtures.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"rollUp for STORY: approved BUILD with clean review and all listed Tasks' latest rounds passed completes\",\n            \"rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it\",\n            \"rollUp for STORY: a listed Task with no head holds back\",\n            \"rollUp for STORY: an approved PLAN with no Tasks holds back, and a Story with no PLAN and no Tasks completes\",\n            \"rollUp for STORY: a listed withdrawn or superseded Task is not counted; a clean review is not an override\",\n            \"rollUp for EPIC: a declared Story without a terminal head holds it; an Epic with no DEF rolls up from its counted Stories\",\n            \"unitMembers includes TASK heads, and a held Story leaves every Task unchanged\",\n            \"reopening a Story reopens only the Tasks it froze\",\n            \"record-override keeps status, revision and approval time, logs the actor and reason, and is refused from a completed BUILD\",\n            \"liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and a valid DIAG with no notice, gives a head with no lifecycle the state unmigrated, and TESTS stays skipped\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: TASKS-listed membership, withdrawn and superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, unit, planRowId and taskOrder, and a Task whose number differs from its plan row has no number alias in sourceIds\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: unit is null for a missing head and has status unmigrated for a head with no lifecycle\",\n            \"a missing or unmigrated unit raises needs-migration and not pending-decision\",\n            \"gate sorts tasks by taskOrder then id\",\n            \"storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head, and an approved BUILD otherwise stays build-recorded with text giving the head's status, that it is not migrated, or that there is no head\",\n            \"board-details joins on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null\",\n            \"board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status\",\n            \"TaskRowView carries a Task's unit status, including unmigrated\",\n            \"the storage helper: a first write gets a draft lifecycle; a rewrite with unchanged content keeps the lifecycle; a rewrite with changed content gets a draft and keeps Signoff entries, with no Signoff entries and with them\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"src/workflow/__tests__/lifecycle-fixtures.ts\",\n            \"in-memory delivery records as in src/workflow/delivery/__tests__\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Real store writes through approval, first write and repair.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD: the outcome merges the approval's own followOn with the seam's, and the Story, its Tasks and its Epic complete\",\n            \"a walk failure leaves the approval standing and reports ok false\",\n            \"a live approval with a listed Task missing its head is held and named in the note\",\n            \"initial approval held, then re-approval with an override records it and completes the Story, then a failure injected in that completion is finished by a later re-approval using the stored override\",\n            \"a held Story in signoff completes later from the stored override\",\n            \"an Epic with a signoff hold stays open after its Story completes\",\n            \"the CLI adapter exposes the story-completion outcome\",\n            \"both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle\",\n            \"guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle\",\n            \"repair-preview writes nothing, and the changes 'repair' applies are the ones the preview listed, including proposed head creation and settlement\",\n            \"repair on a store with an uppercase head holding body.feedback and an approved flat amendment: the head is renamed, the feedback survives under the new id, and the amendment stays approved\",\n            \"repair on an already converted repository creates missing EPIC, STORY, TASKS and TASK heads, including from a PLAN at a status beyond approved\",\n            \"repair with crossed Task numbers and plan rows gives each BUILD result to the Task with that planTaskId and leaves existing rounds alone, before the live rule settles the Story\",\n            \"repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override\",\n            \"repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed and lists it in result.held\",\n            \"a failure injected in the head migration step answers a RepairReport with stoppedAt, applied and remaining and settles nothing, and the next run finishes with no feedback line added twice\",\n            \"a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit\",\n            \"a TASKS head listing a missing Task is reported failed and not settled\",\n            \"a plan with a rename collision answers an error and writes nothing\",\n            \"a second repair lists no changes\",\n            \"an unknown mode answers an error and writes nothing\",\n            \"verifyConversion keeps passing on a converted fixture with the changed loader, graph and gates\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"a temporary repository with a seeded .insrc/artifacts store\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"contract\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The daemon and plugin agree on the new board fields and labels.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts carries unit (including status unmigrated), planRowId, taskOrder, unmigrated and needs-migration through the snapshot\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/delivery-client.test.ts reads the same shape\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"smoke\",\n          \"purpose\": \"The Task status renders in the real board webview.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"Render the board webview during the build and confirm a Task row shows its unit status, including an unmigrated one\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac1\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and a valid DIAG with no notice\",\n            \"buildWorkItemGraph: TASKS-listed membership, withdrawn and superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, unit, planRowId and taskOrder\",\n            \"the contract tests carry the new fields\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac2\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and its Epic\",\n            \"storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head\",\n            \"board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac3\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it\",\n            \"a live approval with a listed Task missing its head is held and named in the note\",\n            \"initial approval held, then re-approval with an override records it and completes the Story\",\n            \"a held Story leaves every Task unchanged\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac4\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle\",\n            \"the storage helper: a rewrite never leaves a head with no lifecycle\",\n            \"guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac5\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"repair on an already converted repository creates missing heads\",\n            \"repair on a store with an uppercase head holding body.feedback and an approved flat amendment\",\n            \"repair with crossed Task numbers and plan rows\",\n            \"repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override\",\n            \"repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed\",\n            \"verifyConversion keeps passing on a converted fixture\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac6\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"repair-preview writes nothing, and the changes 'repair' applies are the ones the preview listed\",\n            \"a second repair lists no changes\",\n            \"a failure injected in the head migration step answers a RepairReport, and the next run finishes\",\n            \"a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"migration\": {\n      \"stateBefore\": \"No unit ever reaches completed: the walk in src/workflow/gates.ts:959 starts at the STORY, rollUp (src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336) needs every Task completed, and nothing completes a Task. The store has EPIC 53 draft, STORY 250 draft, TASK 1,972 approved and 42 draft, and 252 approved builds have no STORY head. A second approval of an approved BUILD records nothing (src/workflow/gates.ts:690). Two sources leave heads with no lifecycle. First, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93 and src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349 still write a new head without one, and src/workflow/storage.ts:178 only reconciles a lifecycle the next head carries; 4 records created on 2026-11-09 and awaiting approval have none (3 ISSUE, 1 LLD). Second, the installed daemon ran commit 5c5bc0cf1 from main, which has no lifecycle code, until 2026-11-07. In all, 273 records have no lifecycle, and 152 heads have an uppercase Story id. The board (src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35) admits neither EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS nor DIAG, and storyStage calls any approved BUILD complete. planConversion (src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121) does nothing at schema version 2, so a converted repository cannot be repaired.\",\n      \"stateAfter\": \"Approving a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and, when every declared Story is done, its Epic, or reports why not. A Task whose latest round failed, or that is unfinished, holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override, which can be recorded after the first approval and is kept with an audit entry. Every workflow head has a lifecycle from its first write and through any rewrite. Repair brings existing records into the common model and settles units at any schema version, and is previewable, re-runnable and reports each step. The board reads the status of Epics, Stories and Tasks from their heads, labels anything not yet migrated, and no longer calls an approved BUILD complete on its own.\",\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"action\": \"Ship the code: the completion rule, the record-override operation, the first-write lifecycle, the follow-on merge, the board's new kinds and fields, and the repair modes. Write COMPLETION_RULE_FROM as a fixed UTC timestamp in that commit.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"action\": \"Update and restart the daemon, and release the plugin with the new fields and labels.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 3,\n          \"action\": \"Run repair-preview on the repository and read the plan, including the renames and the Stories it would settle.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 4,\n          \"action\": \"Make sure no workflow is writing to the repository, then copy .insrc/artifacts and the docs folder aside. Repair renames files and rewrites references, so this copy is the way back.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 5,\n          \"action\": \"Run repair, with the steps in order: rename ids and files, stamp, convert flat amendments, save body.feedback, migrate heads, create missing EPIC and STORY heads, create missing TASKS and TASK heads, move Story history, settle units.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 6,\n          \"action\": \"Read result.applied, remaining, stoppedAt, held and failed. Re-run repair after a stop or a failed unit that can finish, and act by hand on those it cannot.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 7,\n          \"action\": \"Open the board and confirm that no record still raises needs-migration, then commit the changed store.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"New fields on the board's types, FollowOnOutcome, the new lifecycle operation and the repair modes are additive. The existing preview and apply modes of repo.convert and the schema marker are unchanged. handleWorkflowApprove now returns the approval's own outcomes and the seam's together instead of only the seam's. A second approval of an approved BUILD with a new override now records it, where before it did nothing. A consumer of the operation list sees one more operation. applyTasks no longer matches a BUILD result on a Task's number or id; every Task in this store has a planTaskId. An older plugin against the new daemon ignores the new fields but will see Stories it used to call complete shown as build-recorded until repair settles them. The STORY rule deliberately diverges from S007:FR001: a Task completes with its Story rather than before it, so a held Story cannot be hidden by an earlier Task status. Heads written by a daemon on main still have no lifecycle; the board labels them needs-migration and repair handles them. writeArtifact itself is unchanged. Steps 5 and 6 cannot be rolled back automatically; restoring the copy made in step 4 undoes them.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": false,\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": true\n    },\n    \"alternativesConsidered\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"name\": \"Tasks complete with their Story at BUILD approval\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"At BUILD approval a Story completes, with all its open Tasks, when every Task it lists has a latest round that passed or the approval carries an explicit override.\",\n        \"approach\": \"The Story roll-up reads the Tasks the TASKS head lists and each one's latest build round rather than its status. When the rule holds, completing the Story freezes its open Tasks through the cascade; when it does not, the Story and its Tasks stay as they are, and the outcome names the Tasks. A later explicit override is saved on the approved BUILD by its own audited operation. New records carry a draft lifecycle from their first write. A repair mode runs the conversion's ordered steps at any schema version, then settles units, applying the old approval rule only to approvals older than the new one. The board publishes unit status, a plan row key and an order.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"A later failing round can never be hidden, because no Task is completed before its Story\",\n          \"One decision point, the existing walk and the existing cascade\",\n          \"Repair reuses steps that are already repeatable\",\n          \"Follows k8 for clean approvals, and DECISIONS.md for overrides\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"A Task's status changes only when its Story completes\",\n          \"Touches the lifecycle, the conversion and the board in one Story\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"L\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"name\": \"Complete passing Tasks first, then roll up\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"BUILD approval completes each passing Task, then rolls up the Story by Task status.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Walk each counted Task so passing ones complete, then roll up the Story by Task status, reopening a completed Task when a later round fails. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"A passing Task shows complete even while its Story is held\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Needs a reopen path on recordBuildRound so a later failing round cannot be hidden\",\n          \"Adds a lifecycle dependency to the validate path\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Partial on status-is-reliable: a Task completed before its Story can be hidden by a later failing round, and it would need its own reopen path.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a3\",\n        \"name\": \"Any approved BUILD completes the Story\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"A Story completes on an approved BUILD with a clean or overridden review, whatever its Tasks show.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Drop the Task condition from the Story roll-up and cascade to all open Tasks. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"One rule with no Task condition\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Contradicts k8 and the owner's decision: a clean approval would complete a Story with a failed Task\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Violates failed-task-holds-story: any approved BUILD would complete a Story with a failed Task.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"chosenAlternative\": \"a1\",\n    \"openQuestions\": []\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/gates.ts:959\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts:29\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c9\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c10\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"git reflog: 756d5adf4 HEAD@{2026-11-07 17:54:07 +0530} checkout: moving from main to v2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c11\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/gates.ts:690\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c12\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1 -->\n\n# LLD: STORY-eedc4519199b24b4-s1 — Make the delivery board read the common artifact model and migrate old records\n\n## Summary\n\n**Epic:** `make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact`\n**HLD base run:** `wf-1794229933602-ie4di8`\n**HLD effective hash:** `1d17e3d5a79a...`\n\nApproving a build now really completes its Story and Tasks and, once every Story the Epic declares is done, the Epic, which never happened before. A Task that failed its latest build, or was never finished, holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override, which can also be given after the first approval. New records have a lifecycle from the moment they are written. A repair run brings existing records up to date at any schema version and reports, step by step, what it planned, did, held and could not do. The delivery board shows Epic, Story and Task status from those records.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [HLD context](#1-hld-context)\n2. [Contract details](#2-contract-details)\n3. [Data model changes](#3-data-model-changes)\n4. [Error paths](#4-error-paths)\n5. [Test strategy](#5-test-strategy)\n6. [Migration](#6-migration)\n7. [Alternatives considered](#7-alternatives-considered)\n8. [References](#8-references)\n\n## 1. HLD context\n\n**Framework:** Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\n**Rollout phase:** standalone\n\n## 2. Contract details\n\n**Surface level:** internal-shared\n\n### 2.1 `rollUp`\n\n```typescript\nrollUp(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader, evidence: CompletionEvidence): Promise<Status | undefined>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `id: string` — The TASK, STORY or EPIC head to evaluate\n- `reader: ChildStatusReader` — Reads child listings and statuses\n- `evidence: CompletionEvidence` — Build, review, Task-list, override and declared-Story facts\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<Status | undefined>` — 'completed' when the condition holds. TASK: its latest build round passed (unchanged). STORY: its BUILD is approved, its review is clean or overridden, and either storyTasks answers none-required, or storyTasks answers listed and every listed Task that is not withdrawn or superseded has a head whose latest round passed, or the BUILD's approval carries an explicit override. A listed Task with no head, and an answer of not-created, count as unfinished. EPIC: every counted Story is completed, and every Story its DEF declares has a head that is completed, withdrawn or superseded.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `UnreadableChildError` when A head of the counted child kind cannot be read\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- id parses as an artifact id\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Reads only\n- A STORY's condition reads each Task's latest round, not its status, so a later failing round always counts\n\n### 2.2 `unitMembers`\n\n```typescript\nunitMembers(id: string, reader: ChildStatusReader): Promise<string[]>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `id: string` — The unit\n- `reader: ChildStatusReader` — Reads the unit's children\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<string[]>` — For a STORY, also its TASK children, so its open Tasks complete with it\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A member that is completed, withdrawn or superseded is left alone, as completeMember already does\n- Each frozen Task's log entry names the Story in frozenBy, and reopening the Story reopens the Tasks it froze\n\n### 2.3 `approveArtifactByJsonPath`\n\n```typescript\napproveArtifactByJsonPath(jsonPath: string, opts: ApproveOptions): Promise<ApprovalResult>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `jsonPath: string` — The record being approved\n- `opts: ApproveOptions` — The lifecycle service, actor and any override reason\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<ApprovalResult>` — As today. For a BUILD already approved or in signoff that is given an explicit override different from the one it carries, the override is first saved by the 'record-override' operation.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `IllegalTransitionError` when The BUILD's status does not allow an override to be recorded, for example it is completed\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The BUILD's status, revision and approval time do not change when an override is recorded\n- Other kinds, and a repeat of the same reason, record nothing\n- The batch approval then runs completeThroughService, so the held Story completes when the rule now holds\n\n### 2.4 `completeThroughService`\n\n```typescript\ncompleteThroughService(jsonPath: string): Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `jsonPath: string` — The approved record's path\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<FollowOnOutcome | undefined>` — For a BUILD, an outcome of kind 'story-completion' with ok, a note and the ids completed. Undefined for other kinds. It never rejects.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- The record was just approved or re-approved\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- The Story's and Epic's heads, and a head for every Story the DEF declares, exist before the walk\n- The walk starts at the STORY, and the only path that completes a Task is its Story's cascade\n- A failure leaves the approval standing and is reported with ok false\n- A Story held back is reported with ok true and a note naming the Tasks that hold it, including listed Tasks with no head\n\n### 2.5 `handleWorkflowApprove`\n\n```typescript\nhandleWorkflowApprove(params: unknown, deps?: WorkflowApproveDeps): Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `params: WorkflowApproveRequest` — The approval request\n- `deps: WorkflowApproveDeps` _(optional)_ — The post-approval seam\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<WorkflowApproveResult>` — followOn holds the approval's own outcomes followed by the seam's\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A seam that returns outcomes no longer discards the story-completion outcome\n- src/cli/services/workflow.ts exposes the story-completion outcome in its result\n\n### 2.6 `handleRepoConvert`\n\n```typescript\nhandleRepoConvert(params: unknown, repoEnv: string | undefined): Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `params: RepoConvertParams` — repo and mode; mode gains 'repair-preview' and 'repair'\n- `repoEnv: string | undefined` — Fallback repository path\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<ConversionReport | RepairReport | { error: string }>` — Repair modes answer a RepairReport and work at any schema version. Once a repair has begun writing it always answers a RepairReport; { error } means nothing was written.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `{ error: string }` when Unknown mode, or a repository that is not a directory, or the plan lists a problem such as a rename collision, in which case nothing is written\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- 'repair-preview' writes nothing and lists the same changes 'repair' then applies\n- A second 'repair' lists no changes\n- The schema marker and the preview and apply modes are unchanged\n\n### 2.7 `applyTasks`\n\n```typescript\napplyTasks(repo: string, deps: ConversionDeps): Promise<TasksResult>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `repo: string` — The repository\n- `deps: ConversionDeps` — Store, history and Task sets\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<TasksResult>` — The Task sets created and the Tasks given a back-filled round\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- A BUILD result is matched to a Task by planTaskId alone, so a Task whose number equals another Task's plan row cannot receive it\n- A Task that already has a build round is left as it is\n- A PLAN at approved or any later status qualifies, as the units step does for repair\n\n### 2.8 `liftStoreFile`\n\n```typescript\nliftStoreFile(fileName: string, parsed: unknown): ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `fileName: string` — The store file name\n- `parsed: unknown` — The parsed file\n\n**Returns:** `ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure` — A record for every kind of the common model, including DIAG; TESTS stays deliberately skipped. A head with no lifecycle has approval state 'unmigrated'.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- No legacy approval field is read\n\n### 2.9 `buildWorkItemGraph`\n\n```typescript\nbuildWorkItemGraph(recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet): WorkItemGraph\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `recordSet: ArtifactRecordSet` — The loaded records\n\n**Returns:** `WorkItemGraph` — Each epic, story and task node carries its unit head, or null. A story's tasks come from its TASKS head when it has one, else from its PLAN.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Unit records are not counted as evidence; a DIAG head is evidence of the Story its id names\n- Active Tasks are those the TASKS head lists and that are not withdrawn or superseded\n- A task node carries planRowId and taskOrder from its TASK head\n- For a task node with a head, sourceIds holds the plan row id and not the Task's own number, so no alias can collide with another Task's plan row\n\n### 2.10 `storyStage`\n\n```typescript\nstoryStage(route: DeliveryRoute, evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[], issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined, unit: UnitHead | null): { stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `route: DeliveryRoute` — The story's route\n- `evidence: readonly ArtifactRecord[]` — The story's records\n- `issue: ArtifactRecord | undefined` — The issue behind a fix story\n- `unit: UnitHead | null` — The STORY head\n\n**Returns:** `{ stage: DeliveryStage; text: string; artifactIds: string[] }` — 'complete' only when the STORY head is completed. An approved BUILD on a Story not completed stays 'build-recorded', and its text states the STORY head's status, that the head is not migrated, or that there is no STORY head.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- An approved BUILD alone no longer yields 'complete'\n\n## 3. Data model changes\n\n### 3.1 `CompletionEvidence` — field-add\n\nAdds storyBuildApproved(epicHash, storyId), true when the BUILD status is approved or later; storyApprovalOverride(epicHash, storyId), the explicit override reason on the BUILD's approval, or undefined; declaredStories(epicHash), the Story ids the DEF lists, empty when there is no DEF; and storyTasks(epicHash, storyId), answering { kind: 'listed'; taskIds: string[] } | { kind: 'not-created' } | { kind: 'none-required' }. listed holds the TASKS head's ids when it has at least one, else the Story's child TASK heads when there are any. Otherwise not-created when the Story's PLAN is approved or later, because Task creation did not finish, and none-required when it has no such PLAN, as on a small bugfix or trivial route. A clean review is not an override. The override extends k8 by the decision recorded in DECISIONS.md: on the BUILD approval it also waives failed or unfinished Tasks.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:48`\n- `src/workflow/tasks/types.ts:30`\n\n### 3.2 `Lifecycle operation record-override` — new\n\nA new lifecycle operation, valid on a BUILD whose status is approved, in-signoff or signed-off. It sets lifecycle.approval.override to the reason and leaves the status, the revision and the approval time unchanged. It appends one log entry with the actor, the time and outcome { result: 'override', summary: reason }, so the audit trail keeps each override even if a later one replaces it on the head. The reason is then found by storedOverride and storyApprovalOverride after the request is gone, including in deferred signoff completion and repair. The relationship is one BUILD approval to at most one current override and any number of logged ones.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/gates.ts:690`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:41`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts:20`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:41`\n\n### 3.3 `New and rewritten workflow heads` — invariant-change\n\nBoth sites that write a finished workflow artifact call one helper in src/workflow/storage.ts that settles meta.lifecycle before the write. No prior head, or a prior head with no lifecycle: a draft lifecycle. A prior head with a lifecycle and unchanged content: that lifecycle. A prior head with a lifecycle and changed content: a draft for the new revision, keeping its Signoff entries, because approval and review belong to the revision they were made at. Only these two sites change, so the writeArtifact behaviour that storage-signoff-history.test.ts pins stays as it is. Today such a head has no lifecycle until a lifecycle operation adds one, and a rewrite drops one that has no Signoff entries. A guard test fails if a production 'content' write of a delivery kind can create a head without a lifecycle.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93`\n- `src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349`\n- `src/workflow/storage.ts:178`\n- `src/workflow/storage.ts:224`\n\n### 3.4 `FollowOnOutcome` — field-modify\n\nAdds kind 'story-completion' and optional completed: string[]. Additive.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/gates.ts:854`\n- `src/workflow/gates.ts:881`\n- `src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts:58`\n- `src/cli/services/workflow.ts:152`\n\n### 3.5 `RepairReport` — new\n\n{ mode: 'repair-preview' | 'repair'; plan: ConversionPlan; result?: { applied: ConversionChange[]; remaining: ConversionChange[]; stoppedAt?: { step: RepairStep; reason: string }; held: UnitOutcome[]; failed: UnitOutcome[] } }, where UnitOutcome is { artifactId, reason, completedMembers: string[] } and RepairStep is every conversion step except the marker, plus 'settle'. After the run the plan is computed again from the files: remaining is what it still lists, and applied is every planned change it no longer lists. This covers every step without each one having to report its own writes. A step that throws stops the run, stoppedAt names it, and later steps do not run because each depends on the one before; nothing settles after a stop. Settling alone continues per unit: held units were left by the completion rule or a signoff hold, and failed ones hit a conflict or write error. completedMembers lists members already completed when a settlement failed. ConversionRule gains 'settle-unit'.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/convert/types.ts`\n- `src/daemon/repo-convert.ts:54`\n- `src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126`\n\n### 3.6 `Repair order, discovery and eligibility` — new\n\nRepair runs the conversion's own steps in their fixed order, each of which can be repeated: applyRenames, applyStamps, applyAmendments, applyFeedback, migrateHeads, applyUnits, applyTasks, applyStoryHistory, then settle. Renames come first because History refuses an uppercase Story id, and amendments before migration because migrateHeads skips a record with no meta. It does not use the progress file or write the schema marker. A plan with a problem writes nothing, as conversion does. This store has 152 uppercase heads, no collisions and no flat amendments. A Story is known from a DEF declaration or from any LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR head naming its hash and story id, with S001 read as s1 in the preview, before the rename has run; each known hash gets an EPIC head. An ISSUE with no such record creates nothing. A PLAN qualifies for Tasks at approved or any later status. A TASKS head listing a Task with no head is reported as failed and left unchanged, and the Story is not settled; this store has none. Settling: COMPLETION_RULE_FROM is a fixed UTC timestamp with a Z suffix, written into the code when this change is committed and never recomputed, so the attribution of old approvals cannot move between releases. A Story whose BUILD approval time is before it is settled with storyCodeReview answering overridden and storyApprovalOverride answering 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration, because that approval passed the gate of its time. A later approval, including one made before the new daemon is running, is settled only by the live rule, so repair cannot complete a Story the live rule holds and such a Story is reported in result.held.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126`\n- `src/workflow/convert/rename.ts:135`\n- `src/workflow/convert/amendments.ts`\n- `src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts`\n- `src/workflow/convert/units.ts`\n- `src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:92`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts:29`\n- `src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:154`\n\n### 3.7 `DeliveryArtifactKind` — field-modify\n\nAdds EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and DIAG. Relationship: one EPIC head has many STORY heads (by epicHash); one STORY has zero or one TASKS head, zero or more TASK heads and zero or more DIAG heads (by epicHash and storyId); a TASK references one plan row by planTaskId, and re-planning can change that row while the Task keeps its number. Each work item references at most one unit head of its own level, in the direction item to head. TESTS stays skipped by name.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/types.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts`\n- `src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts`\n- `src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:49`\n\n### 3.8 `WorkItemNode, DeliveryItem and TaskValidation` — field-add\n\nWorkItemNode and DeliveryItem add unit: { artifactId: string; status: UnitStatus } | null, where UnitStatus is Status | 'unmigrated'. unit is set for epics, stories and tasks, is null only when there is no head, and has status 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. They also add planRowId: string | null and taskOrder: number | null for tasks. TaskValidation adds taskOrder; a story's tasks array is sorted by taskOrder, then by task item id. A task's validation result stays the one in the BUILD record, and the Story roll-up uses the Task's latest round: the two can differ, in which case the row can show passed while its Story is held, and the reason is in the approval's story-completion note. board-details.ts joins PLAN rows and dependencies on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null, and the client renders the tasks array in the order it receives. The plugin shows an Epic as complete only when its unit status is completed, keeps the child count as progress, and carries a Task's unit status through TaskRowView to the webview beside its validation result.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/types.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts`\n\n### 3.9 `ApprovalState, NoticeCode and AttentionReason` — field-modify\n\nApprovalState adds 'unmigrated' for a head with no lifecycle. NoticeCode and AttentionReason add 'needs-migration', raised for an unmigrated record or a story, epic or active task with no head or an unmigrated head, so such a record never counts as pending-decision. The plugin gains labels for these and for the unmigrated unit status.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35`\n- `src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts`\n\n## 4. Error paths\n\n**Error cases**\n\n- **The completion walk fails after the BUILD approval is committed, for example a child head cannot be read or a write conflicts.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: completeThroughService catches the rejection from completeIfRolledUp or from ensuring the heads.\n  - Response: The approval stands. The answer carries a story-completion outcome with ok false and the failure as its note; handleWorkflowApprove merges it with the seam's outcomes so it reaches the caller.\n  - User impact: The build shows as approved and the caller is told the Story did not complete and why. A re-approval or a repair run finishes it.\n- **A listed Task's latest build round failed, a listed Task has no round or no head, or Task creation did not finish, and the BUILD approval carries no explicit override.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: rollUp for the STORY reads storyTasks, then statusOf and taskBuildPassed for each listed Task, then storyApprovalOverride.\n  - Response: rollUp returns undefined, so the Story and its Tasks are left unchanged. The outcome has ok true and a note naming the Tasks that hold it.\n  - User impact: The approval is recorded and the Story stays open on the board. Approving the BUILD again with an explicit override records the reason and completes the Story.\n- **An override is given for a BUILD whose status does not allow one to be recorded, for example it is completed.** (terminal)\n  - Detection: nextLifecycle refuses 'record-override' from that status with IllegalTransitionError.\n  - Response: The batch approval lists the path in skipped with the reason, and nothing changes.\n  - User impact: The caller is told the override was not recorded.\n- **A repair step throws part-way, for example a write fails during head migration.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The repair runner catches the throw around each step and computes the plan again from the files.\n  - Response: The run stops, later steps do not run and nothing settles. The answer is a RepairReport with stoppedAt, applied and remaining, not { error }.\n  - User impact: The report shows the step, why it stopped, what was written and what is left. Running repair again continues from the files, and a step's earlier writes are not repeated.\n- **The repair plan lists a problem, such as a renamed file colliding with a different existing one.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: planConversion lists it in plan.problems before any write.\n  - Response: It answers { error } naming the problems and writes nothing, as conversion does.\n  - User impact: The store is untouched and the conflicting files are named.\n- **A repair settlement fails after some of the unit's members were already completed, because members are written one at a time before the unit head.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: The settle step catches the write failure for that unit and re-reads each member's status.\n  - Response: The unit is listed in result.failed with reason and completedMembers. Other units continue. A later repair run completes the rest, and completeMember skips the members already terminal.\n  - User impact: The report names the unit and the members already completed; running repair again finishes it.\n- **A TASKS head lists a Task id that has no TASK head during repair.** (terminal)\n  - Detection: The repair's Task step compares the TASKS listing against the store's TASK heads.\n  - Response: The Story is listed in result.failed, is left unchanged and is not settled; createFromPlan is not run over it.\n  - User impact: The report names the Story and the missing Task for manual attention. This store has none today.\n- **A store file is unreadable or is not a recognised artifact when the board loads.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: liftStoreFile returns a RecordLoadFailure for the file.\n  - Response: The failure is reported as a load notice, as today, and the rest of the board is built.\n  - User impact: The board still opens and shows a notice for that file.\n- **repo.convert receives an unknown mode, or a repository path that is not a directory.** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: handleRepoConvert validates the mode against the accepted set and checks the path.\n  - Response: It answers { error } and writes nothing.\n  - User impact: The caller sees the reason and nothing changes.\n\n**Edge cases**\n\n| Input | Expected |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| A Story with an approved BUILD and clean review, no TASKS head, no child TASK heads and no PLAN at approved or later, such as a small bugfix or trivial route. | storyTasks answers none-required and it completes. |\n| A Story with an approved PLAN and no TASKS head or child TASK heads. | storyTasks answers not-created, and the Story is held unless the approval carries an override. |\n| A Story held by a failed Task, then the BUILD is approved again with an explicit override. | The override is saved on the approval and logged, the status, revision and approval time do not change, and the Story completes. |\n| A BUILD approved again with the override it already carries. | Nothing new is recorded; completion is attempted again. |\n| A held Story's override was recorded, and the Story is in signoff so it completes later. | The deferred completion reads the stored override and completes it. |\n| An Epic's signoff hold after its last Story completes. | The Story completes, the Epic stays open until its signoff finishes, and the outcome says so. |\n| A Task's earlier round passed and its latest round failed. | The latest round decides, so the Story is held back without an override. |\n| A listed Task is withdrawn or superseded. | It is not counted, and the cascade leaves it alone. |\n| An Epic whose DEF declares a Story that has no head. | completeThroughService creates the head first, and the Epic stays open until that Story is completed, withdrawn or superseded. |\n| An Epic with no DEF, such as a standalone ISSUE route. | declaredStories is empty and the Epic rolls up from its counted Stories only. |\n| A BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with Tasks whose latest round failed. | Repair settles it with the override 'settled from an approved BUILD', attributed to insrc:migration. |\n| A BUILD approved on or after COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with a failed latest round and no explicit override. | Repair does not complete it and lists it in result.held. |\n| Task t1 represents plan row t2 and Task t2 represents plan row t1. | A BUILD result for row t1 goes to Task t2 in repair, and the board joins each Task to its own row. |\n| A Task that already has a build round when repair back-fills. | Its rounds are left as they are. |\n| A head with an uppercase Story id and body.feedback. | Repair renames it first, then saves the feedback under the new id, then migrates it. |\n| An approved flat amendment. | Repair converts it to a head before migration, and it stays approved. |\n| Repair is run twice, or again after stopping part-way. | The second run after a complete one lists no changes, and a run after a stop lists only what remained, with no feedback line added twice. |\n| A repository with no artifact records. | Repair reports an empty plan and writes nothing. |\n| An ISSUE with no DEF, LLD, PLAN, BUILD or CR naming its hash. | No EPIC or STORY head is created for it. |\n| A head with no lifecycle is loaded by the board, including an EPIC, STORY or TASK head. | Its approval state is 'unmigrated', a unit head has unit.status 'unmigrated', it raises needs-migration and it does not count as pending-decision. |\n| A DIAG head in the store. | It loads with no notice and is evidence of the Story its id names. |\n| A finished workflow artifact is written again over a head with a lifecycle and no Signoff entries, with changed content. | The head gets a draft lifecycle for the new revision, so it never has none. |\n| The same, with unchanged content. | The lifecycle is kept. |\n\n**Invariants to preserve**\n\n- An approval that was committed is never undone by a later completion failure. [[c1]]\n- A Task is completed only through its Story's cascade, so a held Story leaves its Tasks unchanged and an earlier status cannot hide a later failing round. A write failure part-way through a cascade can leave some members completed before the Story head; the next run finishes the unit. [[c2]]\n- Approved records stay approved through repair, and repair preview writes nothing. [[c3]]\n- Local feedback on a record is carried through head migration, and no line is added twice on a re-run. [[c4]]\n\n## 5. Test strategy\n\n**Test framework:** `node:test via tsx; vscode-plugin uses its own node:test run`\n\n**Test levels**\n\n- **unit** — The completion rule, evidence, cascade and board derivation, on in-memory fixtures.\n  - Subjects: `rollUp for STORY: approved BUILD with clean review and all listed Tasks' latest rounds passed completes`, `rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it`, `rollUp for STORY: a listed Task with no head holds back`, `rollUp for STORY: an approved PLAN with no Tasks holds back, and a Story with no PLAN and no Tasks completes`, `rollUp for STORY: a listed withdrawn or superseded Task is not counted; a clean review is not an override`, `rollUp for EPIC: a declared Story without a terminal head holds it; an Epic with no DEF rolls up from its counted Stories`, `unitMembers includes TASK heads, and a held Story leaves every Task unchanged`, `reopening a Story reopens only the Tasks it froze`, `record-override keeps status, revision and approval time, logs the actor and reason, and is refused from a completed BUILD`, `liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and a valid DIAG with no notice, gives a head with no lifecycle the state unmigrated, and TESTS stays skipped`, `buildWorkItemGraph: TASKS-listed membership, withdrawn and superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, unit, planRowId and taskOrder, and a Task whose number differs from its plan row has no number alias in sourceIds`, `buildWorkItemGraph: unit is null for a missing head and has status unmigrated for a head with no lifecycle`, `a missing or unmigrated unit raises needs-migration and not pending-decision`, `gate sorts tasks by taskOrder then id`, `storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head, and an approved BUILD otherwise stays build-recorded with text giving the head's status, that it is not migrated, or that there is no head`, `board-details joins on planRowId, falling back to sourceIds only when it is null`, `board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status`, `TaskRowView carries a Task's unit status, including unmigrated`, `the storage helper: a first write gets a draft lifecycle; a rewrite with unchanged content keeps the lifecycle; a rewrite with changed content gets a draft and keeps Signoff entries, with no Signoff entries and with them`\n  - Fixtures: `src/workflow/__tests__/lifecycle-fixtures.ts`, `in-memory delivery records as in src/workflow/delivery/__tests__`\n- **integration** — Real store writes through approval, first write and repair.\n  - Subjects: `handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD: the outcome merges the approval's own followOn with the seam's, and the Story, its Tasks and its Epic complete`, `a walk failure leaves the approval standing and reports ok false`, `a live approval with a listed Task missing its head is held and named in the note`, `initial approval held, then re-approval with an override records it and completes the Story, then a failure injected in that completion is finished by a later re-approval using the stored override`, `a held Story in signoff completes later from the stored override`, `an Epic with a signoff hold stays open after its Story completes`, `the CLI adapter exposes the story-completion outcome`, `both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle`, `guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle`, `repair-preview writes nothing, and the changes 'repair' applies are the ones the preview listed, including proposed head creation and settlement`, `repair on a store with an uppercase head holding body.feedback and an approved flat amendment: the head is renamed, the feedback survives under the new id, and the amendment stays approved`, `repair on an already converted repository creates missing EPIC, STORY, TASKS and TASK heads, including from a PLAN at a status beyond approved`, `repair with crossed Task numbers and plan rows gives each BUILD result to the Task with that planTaskId and leaves existing rounds alone, before the live rule settles the Story`, `repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override`, `repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed and lists it in result.held`, `a failure injected in the head migration step answers a RepairReport with stoppedAt, applied and remaining and settles nothing, and the next run finishes with no feedback line added twice`, `a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit`, `a TASKS head listing a missing Task is reported failed and not settled`, `a plan with a rename collision answers an error and writes nothing`, `a second repair lists no changes`, `an unknown mode answers an error and writes nothing`, `verifyConversion keeps passing on a converted fixture with the changed loader, graph and gates`\n  - Fixtures: `a temporary repository with a seeded .insrc/artifacts store`\n- **contract** — The daemon and plugin agree on the new board fields and labels.\n  - Subjects: `src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts carries unit (including status unmigrated), planRowId, taskOrder, unmigrated and needs-migration through the snapshot`, `vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/delivery-client.test.ts reads the same shape`\n- **smoke** — The Task status renders in the real board webview.\n  - Subjects: `Render the board webview during the build and confirm a Task row shows its unit status, including an unmigrated one`\n\n**Acceptance mapping**\n\n| Criterion | Proving tests |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `ac1` | `liftStoreFile admits EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS and a valid DIAG with no notice`, `buildWorkItemGraph: TASKS-listed membership, withdrawn and superseded exclusion, PLAN fallback, unit, planRowId and taskOrder`, `the contract tests carry the new fields` |\n| `ac2` | `handleWorkflowApprove on a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and its Epic`, `storyStage is complete only with a completed STORY head`, `board-views shows an Epic complete only from its unit status` |\n| `ac3` | `rollUp for STORY: an earlier pass followed by a failing latest round holds back, and an explicit override completes it`, `a live approval with a listed Task missing its head is held and named in the note`, `initial approval held, then re-approval with an override records it and completes the Story`, `a held Story leaves every Task unchanged` |\n| `ac4` | `both first-write sites give a new head a draft lifecycle`, `the storage helper: a rewrite never leaves a head with no lifecycle`, `guard: a production content write of a delivery kind cannot create a head without a lifecycle` |\n| `ac5` | `repair on an already converted repository creates missing heads`, `repair on a store with an uppercase head holding body.feedback and an approved flat amendment`, `repair with crossed Task numbers and plan rows`, `repair settles a BUILD approved before COMPLETION_RULE_FROM with the attributed override`, `repair holds a later BUILD whose latest round failed`, `verifyConversion keeps passing on a converted fixture` |\n| `ac6` | `repair-preview writes nothing, and the changes 'repair' applies are the ones the preview listed`, `a second repair lists no changes`, `a failure injected in the head migration step answers a RepairReport, and the next run finishes`, `a failure injected after earlier members commit is listed with completedMembers, and the next repair run finishes the unit` |\n\n## 6. Migration\n\n**State before:** No unit ever reaches completed: the walk in src/workflow/gates.ts:959 starts at the STORY, rollUp (src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336) needs every Task completed, and nothing completes a Task. The store has EPIC 53 draft, STORY 250 draft, TASK 1,972 approved and 42 draft, and 252 approved builds have no STORY head. A second approval of an approved BUILD records nothing (src/workflow/gates.ts:690). Two sources leave heads with no lifecycle. First, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts:93 and src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:349 still write a new head without one, and src/workflow/storage.ts:178 only reconciles a lifecycle the next head carries; 4 records created on 2026-11-09 and awaiting approval have none (3 ISSUE, 1 LLD). Second, the installed daemon ran commit 5c5bc0cf1 from main, which has no lifecycle code, until 2026-11-07. In all, 273 records have no lifecycle, and 152 heads have an uppercase Story id. The board (src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35) admits neither EPIC, STORY, TASK, TASKS nor DIAG, and storyStage calls any approved BUILD complete. planConversion (src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121) does nothing at schema version 2, so a converted repository cannot be repaired.\n\n**State after:** Approving a BUILD completes the Story, its Tasks and, when every declared Story is done, its Epic, or reports why not. A Task whose latest round failed, or that is unfinished, holds its Story back unless the approval carries an explicit override, which can be recorded after the first approval and is kept with an audit entry. Every workflow head has a lifecycle from its first write and through any rewrite. Repair brings existing records into the common model and settles units at any schema version, and is previewable, re-runnable and reports each step. The board reads the status of Epics, Stories and Tasks from their heads, labels anything not yet migrated, and no longer calls an approved BUILD complete on its own.\n\n**Zero downtime:** no — **Data rewrite:** yes\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Ship the code: the completion rule, the record-override operation, the first-write lifecycle, the follow-on merge, the board's new kinds and fields, and the repair modes. Write COMPLETION_RULE_FROM as a fixed UTC timestamp in that commit. — ↩ rollbackable\n2. Update and restart the daemon, and release the plugin with the new fields and labels. — ↩ rollbackable\n3. Run repair-preview on the repository and read the plan, including the renames and the Stories it would settle. — ↩ rollbackable\n4. Make sure no workflow is writing to the repository, then copy .insrc/artifacts and the docs folder aside. Repair renames files and rewrites references, so this copy is the way back. — ↩ rollbackable\n5. Run repair, with the steps in order: rename ids and files, stamp, convert flat amendments, save body.feedback, migrate heads, create missing EPIC and STORY heads, create missing TASKS and TASK heads, move Story history, settle units. — ✕ non-rollbackable\n6. Read result.applied, remaining, stoppedAt, held and failed. Re-run repair after a stop or a failed unit that can finish, and act by hand on those it cannot. — ✕ non-rollbackable\n7. Open the board and confirm that no record still raises needs-migration, then commit the changed store. — ↩ rollbackable\n\n**Backward compat:** New fields on the board's types, FollowOnOutcome, the new lifecycle operation and the repair modes are additive. The existing preview and apply modes of repo.convert and the schema marker are unchanged. handleWorkflowApprove now returns the approval's own outcomes and the seam's together instead of only the seam's. A second approval of an approved BUILD with a new override now records it, where before it did nothing. A consumer of the operation list sees one more operation. applyTasks no longer matches a BUILD result on a Task's number or id; every Task in this store has a planTaskId. An older plugin against the new daemon ignores the new fields but will see Stories it used to call complete shown as build-recorded until repair settles them. The STORY rule deliberately diverges from S007:FR001: a Task completes with its Story rather than before it, so a held Story cannot be hidden by an earlier Task status. Heads written by a daemon on main still have no lifecycle; the board labels them needs-migration and repair handles them. writeArtifact itself is unchanged. Steps 5 and 6 cannot be rolled back automatically; restoring the copy made in step 4 undoes them.\n\n## 7. Alternatives considered\n\n### 7.1 a1: Tasks complete with their Story at BUILD approval — **CHOSEN**\n\nAt BUILD approval a Story completes, with all its open Tasks, when every Task it lists has a latest round that passed or the approval carries an explicit override.\n\nThe Story roll-up reads the Tasks the TASKS head lists and each one's latest build round rather than its status. When the rule holds, completing the Story freezes its open Tasks through the cascade; when it does not, the Story and its Tasks stay as they are, and the outcome names the Tasks. A later explicit override is saved on the approved BUILD by its own audited operation. New records carry a draft lifecycle from their first write. A repair mode runs the conversion's ordered steps at any schema version, then settles units, applying the old approval rule only to approvals older than the new one. The board publishes unit status, a plan row key and an order.\n\n### 7.2 a2: Complete passing Tasks first, then roll up\n\nBUILD approval completes each passing Task, then rolls up the Story by Task status.\n\nWalk each counted Task so passing ones complete, then roll up the Story by Task status, reopening a completed Task when a later round fails. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\n\n**Rejected because:** Partial on status-is-reliable: a Task completed before its Story can be hidden by a later failing round, and it would need its own reopen path.\n\n### 7.3 a3: Any approved BUILD completes the Story\n\nA Story completes on an approved BUILD with a clean or overridden review, whatever its Tasks show.\n\nDrop the Task condition from the Story roll-up and cascade to all open Tasks. Repair and the board change are the same as a1.\n\n**Rejected because:** Violates failed-task-holds-story: any approved BUILD would complete a Story with a failed Task.\n\n## 8. References\n\n- **[[c1]]** `code` `src/workflow/gates.ts:959`\n- **[[c2]]** `code` `src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:336`\n- **[[c3]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts:29`\n- **[[c4]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts`\n- **[[c5]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/plan.ts:121`\n- **[[c6]]** `code` `src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35`\n- **[[c7]]** `doc` `docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md`\n- **[[c8]]** `prior-artifact` `docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md`\n- **[[c9]]** `doc` `docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md`\n- **[[c10]]** `doc` `/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon` — \"git reflog: 756d5adf4 HEAD@{2026-11-07 17:54:07 +0530} checkout: moving from main to v2\"\n- **[[c11]]** `code` `src/workflow/gates.ts:690`\n- **[[c12]]** `code` `src/workflow/convert/apply.ts:126`\n"},"capturedAt":"2026-11-09T13:17:25.557Z"},"inventory":{"units":[{"id":"/body/summary","selector":"/body/summary","title":"summary","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/hldContextSlice","selector":"/body/hldContextSlice","title":"hldContextSlice","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/contractDetails","selector":"/body/contractDetails","title":"contractDetails","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/dataModelChanges","selector":"/body/dataModelChanges","title":"dataModelChanges","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/interactionWithShared","selector":"/body/interactionWithShared","title":"interactionWithShared","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/errorPaths","selector":"/body/errorPaths","title":"errorPaths","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/testStrategy","selector":"/body/testStrategy","title":"testStrategy","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/migration","selector":"/body/migration","title":"migration","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered","title":"alternativesConsidered","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/chosenAlternative","selector":"/body/chosenAlternative","title":"chosenAlternative","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/openQuestions","selector":"/body/openQuestions","title":"openQuestions","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","title":"a1","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","title":"a2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","title":"a3","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/citations/0","selector":"/citations/0","title":"Citation 1","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/1","selector":"/citations/1","title":"Citation 2","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/2","selector":"/citations/2","title":"Citation 3","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/3","selector":"/citations/3","title":"Citation 4","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/4","selector":"/citations/4","title":"Citation 5","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/5","selector":"/citations/5","title":"Citation 6","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/6","selector":"/citations/6","title":"Citation 7","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/7","selector":"/citations/7","title":"Citation 8","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/8","selector":"/citations/8","title":"Citation 9","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/9","selector":"/citations/9","title":"Citation 10","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/10","selector":"/citations/10","title":"Citation 11","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/11","selector":"/citations/11","title":"Citation 12","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:24","selector":"document:line:24","title":"1. HLD context","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned scope sections align with the originating ISSUE and applicable common-model requirements. Recorded owner decisions support real unit status and explicit overrides for failed or unfinished Tasks. The design addresses lifecycle preservation, repeatable repair and reporting, preserves the issue’s exclusions, and correctly claims no parent HLD. No blocking scope or traceability defects were found.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","document:line:24","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-eedc4519199b24b4.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md — functional requirements, constraints k3/k8, acceptance ac7–ac10 and ac27–ac29","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — completion, revision and conversion requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:310","src/workflow/storage.ts:175","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:218","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:404","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:433"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"completion","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Reviewed all assigned selectors against the issue, owner decisions, applicable common-model requirements and current implementation. Two gaps remain in partial Task creation and durable-override retry behavior.","findings":[{"id":"completion-r4-001","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:218","message":"storyTasks treats existing child TASK heads as a complete listing whenever TASKS is absent, even with an approved PLAN. Task creation writes individual heads first and TASKS last, so an interrupted creation can leave only part of the planned set. If those existing Tasks have passing rounds, the proposed rule completes the Story without an override while uncreated plan Tasks disappear from the condition. Distinguish an incomplete set from a verified complete set before using this fallback, and cover partial creation with at least one existing Task.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §3.1 CompletionEvidence: child-head fallback precedes the approved-PLAN not-created condition","LLD.md §2.1 and §4: unfinished Task creation must hold completion without an override","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:148-183: createFromPlan writes TASK heads sequentially and the TASKS completion marker last","LLD.md §5: proposed incomplete-creation test covers zero Task heads but not a partial set","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md: unfinished Tasks require an explicit BUILD approval override"]},{"id":"completion-r4-002","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:227","message":"The durable-override design updates the approval writer and completion evidence, but leaves the preceding approveWorkflowTarget code-review gate without a stored-override contract. That gate passes only req.overrideReview and skips the artifact on a blocked review before reaching either approveArtifactByJsonPath or completeThroughService. Consequently, an approval made over review findings followed by interrupted completion cannot be retried through normal re-approval using only its stored override, as the design promises. Specify how this outer gate recognizes a current standing BUILD approval and its persisted override, and test the retry with an actually blocking task-based review and no override in the retry request.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §3.2: overrides must remain usable after request context is gone","LLD.md §4: re-approval finishes a failed completion without undoing the committed approval","LLD.md §5 integration: later re-approval must recover using the stored override","src/workflow/gates.ts:974-986: enforceCodeReviewGate receives only the request override and returns early on blocked","src/workflow/gates.ts:994-1010: approval and completion occur only after that outer gate","src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts:14-27: a blocking task-review gap is overridden only by the supplied option","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: storedOverride is consumed downstream of the rejecting gate"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/10","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: common-model constraints and S007 requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/approval-view.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts: operation validation","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: child discovery","src/workflow/gates.ts: approval gates and completion hook","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: Task creation and membership","src/workflow/storage.ts: lifecycle reconciliation and Signoff preservation","src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts: production content write","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts: production content write","src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts","src/cli/services/workflow.ts: approval outcome adapter","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: deferred completion","src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/storage-signoff-history.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/approve-build-freshness.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/completion-evidence.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-members.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"repair","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the issue, applicable common-model requirements and conversion code. Repair ordering, historical eligibility and Task identity handling are specified, but partial-write reporting and rollback remain defective.","findings":[{"id":"repair-r4-001","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:257","message":"Computing applied changes solely by subtracting the remaining plan cannot accurately report committed writes. applyFeedback appends sidecar records while leaving body.feedback intact; feedbackRule therefore reports exactly the same change after those writes. If feedback or subsequent head migration fails, the proposed report omits feedback already committed. Similarly, tasksRule stops listing a Story once TASKS exists, although applyTasks can still backfill missing rounds, including after an interrupted run. Specify sidecar-aware planning and granular write accounting, or collect actual phase results. Add failure tests asserting that committed feedback, migration log entries and Task rounds appear accurately in applied/remaining and retry previews.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §3.5: applied is every planned change absent from the recomputed plan","LLD.md §2.6 and §4: preview fidelity and reporting of writes before failure","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts:88 — feedbackRule examines body.feedback without checking existing sidecar records","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts:114 — applyFeedback appends records and strips nothing","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts: writeMigratedHead appends log entries before replacing the head","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:64 — tasksRule skips existing TASKS heads","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:82 — applyTasks backfills rounds even when TASKS already exists","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-feedback-rule.test.ts: interrupted append and head-replacement fixtures"]},{"id":"repair-r4-002","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:428","message":"The stated rollback restores only .insrc/artifacts and docs, but repair's unit creation and settlement also stage durable operations under .insrc/journal. A failed write can leave a pending operation outside that backup. After restoring the prescribed copy, the next lifecycle write can replay the repair operation when the restored head matches its prior hash, or encounter a persistent conflict when it does not. Thus restoring this copy does not reliably undo repair as §6 promises. Include journal state in the quiesced backup/restore procedure and define removal of repair-created pending operations before restarting writers. Cover rollback after a staged write fails before head replacement.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §6 steps 4–6 and Backward compat: restoring the step-4 copy is claimed to undo repair","src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts:32 — JOURNAL_DIR is .insrc/journal","src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-lifecycle.ts: createRepoLifecycle installs the durable file journal","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts:371 — staging precedes log append and head replacement","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts:410 — completePending replays staged operations or raises a head conflict","src/workflow/convert/units.ts: applyUnits creates heads through ArtifactStore.write"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9","/citations/11","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md: migration requirements and recorded conversion decisions","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts","src/workflow/convert/run.ts","src/workflow/convert/rename.ts","src/workflow/convert/stamps.ts","src/workflow/convert/amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/story-history.ts","src/workflow/convert/marker.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: readPlan and createFromPlan","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar-store.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: durable writes and pending-operation recovery","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts: rollUp and unitMembers","src/workflow/gates.ts: approved-or-beyond approval handling","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-feedback-rule.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: git reflog confirming the cited main-to-v2 checkout"],"limitations":[],"advice":["When implementing PLAN eligibility beyond approved, account for TaskSets.readPlan's current approved-only guard and test creation from signed-off and completed PLANs."]},{"chunkId":"board","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the originating ISSUE, applicable common-model and delivery requirements, and current daemon/client code. Unit status, migration labeling and Task identity contracts are substantially specified, but BUILD-only validation preservation and DIAG evidence reads have end-to-end gaps.","findings":[{"id":"board-r4-001","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:184","message":"The proposed task derivation uses TASKS membership, otherwise PLAN rows, without preserving BUILD-only validation entries. With no TASKS head, a PLAN containing t1 and a BUILD containing failed t3 would omit t3 entirely. The current gate computes validation and conflicts by walking graph task children, so this removes the unplanned result, failed count and potentially the validation-conflict signal. Preserve unmatched BUILD evidence independently of authoritative active-task membership, and test both PLAN-plus-extra-BUILD and BUILD-without-PLAN cases.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.9: tasks come from TASKS when present, otherwise PLAN","LLD §3.8: validation remains sourced from BUILD","LLD §5: membership tests omit BUILD-only validation regression cases","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts: addTasks currently collects PLAN and BUILD task ids","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts: storyValidation derives task results and conflicts through story.childIds","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts:284 — unmatched BUILD results remain visible as unplanned","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts:362 — BUILD tasks without PLAN remain visible","docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/DEF.md:156 — S003 ac4 requires unmatched BUILD results and unplanned marking"]},{"id":"board-r4-002","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:189","message":"DIAG is added as Story evidence, but the design does not extend the evidence-read handler's artifact-id validation. Its regex permits only one suffix after the hash, whereas valid DIAG ids contain both Story and sequence suffixes, such as DIAG-aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa-s1-2. Adding DIAG to the loader's kind list therefore displays an evidence row whose read action still returns 'invalid artifact id'. Specify kind-aware validation for this endpoint and add a client/handler test opening a valid sequenced DIAG while retaining invalid-id and containment checks.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.9 and §3.7: DIAG heads become Story evidence","LLD §5: DIAG coverage currently checks loader admission rather than evidence retrieval","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:85 — DIAG requires Story and sequence","src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-ids.test.ts:42 — valid DIAG id has two suffixes","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts: ARTIFACT_ID_RE allows only one suffix","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts:110 — handleDeliveryEvidence rejects ids before reading the record","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts:124 — evidence actions call workflow.deliveryEvidence"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/5","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json — inventory and completed dependency chunks","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md — common-model requirements and completion constraints","docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/DEF.md — independent validation signals and unplanned results","docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/HLD.md — graph, gate and evidence-read contracts","src/workflow/delivery/types.ts","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts","src/workflow/delivery/stage.ts","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts","src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts","src/workflow/delivery/markdown.ts","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tasks/lookup.ts","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/delivery-handler-contract.test.ts","src/cli/services/workflow.ts — approval outcome adapter","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-contract.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-views.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-model.ts","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts — TaskRowView","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts:224 — actual task-table rendering source","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/labels.ts","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt — current approval IPC consumer; no workflow.delivery consumer found"],"limitations":[],"advice":["The prose adequately describes the relationship changes and small status-display addition; no new diagram or UX companion is supplied. Webview rendering source was inspected, but no rendered UI was visually verified. Retain the planned build-stage smoke test for Task status beside validation, including unmigrated status."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"passed","summary":"Completed fresh whole-design reconciliation against the originating ISSUE, owner decisions, common-model requirements and all four completed substantive chunks. Current files match the checkpoint baseline. No additional distinct defect was found. The substantive chunks retain six MED findings; this consistency chunk passing does not clear those findings.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: completion, revision, migration and non-goal requirements","docs/plans/core-data-model.md:84-90, revision requirements and recorded conversion decisions",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json: attempt 3 report and attempt 4 completedChunks scope, completion, repair and board","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:125-183","src/workflow/gates.ts:945-1020","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts: CompletionEvidence, countedChildren, rollUp and unitMembers","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts: completion, member freezing and reopening","src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts:32-120","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts:360-447","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:55-116","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts:88-145","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts: artifact-id validation and evidence retrieval","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001: file inventory; canonical artifact contains no visual definitions or attachments"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Address completion-r4-001 across live completion, repair reconstruction and board membership: existing Task heads do not prove that an interrupted TASKS creation produced the complete planned set.","Address completion-r4-002 before relying on re-approval recovery. The stored override must reach the outer code-review gate as well as downstream completion evidence.","Address repair-r4-001 and repair-r4-002 together: accurate partial-write reporting and rollback must account for sidecar writes, Task rounds and durable journal operations.","Retain board-r4-001 and board-r4-002: authoritative active membership must preserve unmatched BUILD validation evidence, and DIAG admission must extend through evidence retrieval.","Define the requirement text behind acceptance labels ac1–ac6, or replace them with identifiable ISSUE requirement references.","Relationship prose adequately describes the proposed model. No authored or generated visual artifacts accompany this LLD, and no visual verification is claimed. Perform the specified Task-status webview rendering check during implementation."],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":3,"chunkId":"completion","findingId":"completion-001"},"rationale":"The current design validates explicitly listed missing Task heads and distinguishes taskless routes from zero-head incomplete creation. Its child-head fallback still permits partially created sets to appear complete. The fresh completion finding identifies this remaining membership defect more precisely.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:44","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:218","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:148-183",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json: attempt 4 completion finding completion-r4-001"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["completion","consistency"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"completion","findingId":"completion-r4-001"}},{"source":{"attempt":3,"chunkId":"completion","findingId":"completion-002"},"rationale":"The LLD now defines an audited record-override operation, its permitted statuses, unchanged approval/revision fields, persistent evidence readers and deferred-completion tests. This resolves the missing persistence contract. The separate outer-gate retry defect remains recorded as completion-r4-002.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:82-90","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:225-233","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:397",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json: attempt 4 completion assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["completion","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":3,"chunkId":"repair","findingId":"repair-001"},"rationale":"Repair now explicitly runs renaming and amendment conversion before feedback and head migration, preserves the prerequisite ordering, and includes uppercase-head/feedback and approved-flat-amendment fixtures.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:267","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:397","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:429",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json: attempt 4 repair assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["repair","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":3,"chunkId":"repair","findingId":"repair-002"},"rationale":"The design extends RepairReport and stopping behavior across every mutating phase, but its plan-subtraction accounting still cannot report committed sidecar writes and Task rounds accurately. The fresh finding replaces the former missing-contract diagnosis with the demonstrated defect in that contract.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:257","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts:88-145","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:64-116",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json: attempt 4 repair finding repair-r4-001"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["repair","consistency"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"repair","findingId":"repair-r4-001"}},{"source":{"attempt":3,"chunkId":"repair","findingId":"repair-003"},"rationale":"applyTasks now has an explicit planTaskId-only matching contract, preserves existing rounds and requires a crossed-identity fixture before settlement. The board also publishes the same plan-row identity.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:148-163","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:294-296","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:368-369","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:397"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["repair","board","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":3,"chunkId":"board","findingId":"board-001"},"rationale":"DIAG is now explicitly included in loader admission, the kind expansion, Story evidence ownership and loader tests, while TESTS remains deliberately excluded. The separate evidence-read validation gap remains recorded as board-r4-002.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:175","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:192","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:283","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:394",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json: attempt 4 board assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["board","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":3,"chunkId":"board","findingId":"board-002"},"rationale":"UnitStatus now explicitly includes unmigrated, reserves null for an absent head, defines stage