us including unmigrated, null-only-for-missing-head semantics, migration notices and pending-decision exclusion through graph, gates, snapshot and client contracts.","Check complete versus build-recorded derivation, Epic progress and Task unit status beside BUILD validation, including the documented difference from latest-round completion evidence.","Inspect daemon, CLI where applicable, VS Code details, TaskRowView, labels and actual webview rendering source; check current JetBrains IPC consumers without imposing deprecated-client requirements.","Assess necessary relationship/UX artifacts and inspect actual renderings where available; distinguish design evidence from the future implementation smoke test.","Check unit, integration, snapshot/client contract and conversion-verification coverage for changed and unchanged board behavior."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Fresh whole-design consistency and requirement traceability","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile all substantive assessments against the originating ISSUE, applicable common-model requirements and owner decisions.","Check end-to-end agreement among live membership, durable overrides, revision handling, repair settlement and board status.","Check contract/error consistency, ownership, dependency order, release compatibility, acceptance mapping and citation support.","Reconcile all seven carried findings only after fresh inspection; distinguish demonstrated defects, limitations and optional advice.","Check necessary artifact verification and enforce the specified final-status precedence."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 27 current inventory units are assigned to substantive chunks. The four implementation responsibilities from attempt 3 are preserved, with new citation ownership added and concerns expanded for the revised contracts. Broad contract, model, error and test selectors intentionally recur so each responsibility retains its interfaces, logic, failure behavior and verification. The issue is the workflow ancestor; the common-model DEF and recorded decisions are applicable references, not invented Epic/HLD ancestry. Every substantive chunk is selected for fresh review, followed by fresh final consistency.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["board"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/8","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/9","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/10","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/11","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"document:line:24","chunkIds":["scope"]}]},"impact":{"baselineAttempt":3,"mode":"full","changes":["Compared the current live LLD and canonical artifact with attempt 3's captured content, accepted plan and completed feedback. The live document matches attempt 4's captured document.","The summary now explicitly includes unfinished Tasks, overrides after initial approval and stepwise repair reporting. The context, shared-interaction, chosen-alternative and open-question fields remain unchanged.","CompletionEvidence gains storyTasks with listed, not-created and none-required outcomes. Live roll-up now addresses missing listed heads and distinguishes incomplete Task creation from taskless routes.","A new approveArtifactByJsonPath contract and record-override lifecycle operation persist later overrides with audit entries while retaining status, revision and approval time; deferred completion and retry tests are added.","Workflow-head lifecycle handling now specifies unchanged-content preservation and changed-revision reset with Signoff retention through a helper at the two write sites.","Repair now specifies the conversion prerequisite sequence, rename-collision preflight, immutable UTC cutoff, no marker/progress writes and expanded recovery reporting through stoppedAt, applied and remaining.","applyTasks gains an explicit planTaskId-only backfill contract, existing-round preservation and PLAN eligibility beyond approved, with crossed-identity tests.","The board adds DIAG acceptance and Story association, UnitStatus including unmigrated, explicit missing-versus-unmigrated representation, broader migration notices and Task status propagation to the webview.","Tests expand across membership, stored overrides, signoff holds, lifecycle rewrites, normalization, partial repair failure, preview parity, client snapshots and conversion verification. Migration adds downtime and backup/restore steps.","The inventory grows from 25 to 27 units through citations for gates.ts:690 and convert/apply.ts:126; the loader citation changes from load.ts:58 to load.ts:35. No authored visual definitions or attachments are present in the current canonical artifact."],"directChunkIds":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"indirectChunkIds":[],"rationale":"Full review is selected because every substantive responsibility contains changed assigned content. Scope's summary changes its promises; completion introduces membership and durable-override contracts; repair changes ordering, evidence assignment and reporting; board changes kind acceptance and unit representation. Indirect effects also require inspection within these selected chunks: unchanged owner decisions constrain the new override operation; unchanged cascade/reopen and signoff behavior consume new membership and stored evidence; repair-created identities and rounds feed live completion and board joins; lifecycle rewrite rules affect approval validity; shared loader/graph changes affect conversion verification; client contracts and UX consume the new status union. The unchanged issue exclusions, common-model requirements, declared-Story rules and absence of HLD ancestry must remain satisfied. Attempt 3 is the immediately preceding complete same-party baseline and has no limitations. Attempt 2 was invalidated and supplies no reusable coverage; attempt 1's incomplete result is not used to bypass newer evidence. No coverage is retained, and all seven effective attempt-3 findings remain carried until fresh inspection. Final consistency is always fresh.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["scope"],"currentIds":["scope"],"explanation":"Same responsibility and selectors; the changed summary requires fresh scope and upstream traceability assessment."},{"priorIds":["completion"],"currentIds":["completion"],"explanation":"Same implementation responsibility and dependency on scope, expanded for storyTasks, record-override, lifecycle rewrite behavior and new /citations/10. Broad selectors retain completion interfaces, failures and tests."},{"priorIds":["repair"],"currentIds":["repair"],