nical alternatives additionally retain pros and cons"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Retain completion-r5-001 from the completed completion chunk. An existing TASKS listing must be checked against the current approved PLAN revision before it proves completeness. This also affects board membership after interrupted reconciliation; repair already rejects that mismatch.","Preserve granular recorder coverage through nested Task creation, settlement and pending-operation replay when implementing the committed-write reporting contract.","Correct the documented approveWorkflowTarget signature to match its exported request/result contract, as noted in the completion assessment.","Relationship prose adequately describes the proposed ownership and cardinality. No visual verification is claimed; the specified webview rendering check belongs to implementation validation. Proposed tests were assessed, not executed."],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":4,"chunkId":"completion","findingId":"completion-r4-001"},"rationale":"The current storyTasks contract treats an approved-or-later PLAN without a finished TASKS head as not-created even when partial TASK heads exist. Edge cases and tests explicitly cover a partial set whose existing Tasks passed. This resolves the original absent-TASKS defect; the distinct stale-listing defect remains recorded as completion-r5-001.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:276 — approved PLAN takes precedence over child-head fallback when TASKS is absent","LLD.md:424","LLD.md:469","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: createFromPlan publishes TASKS last","Checkpoint attempt 5 completedChunks: completion"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["completion","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":4,"chunkId":"completion","findingId":"completion-r4-002"},"rationale":"The design now supplies the persisted override to the outer code-review gate for a standing approved-or-later BUILD, excludes draft revisions and requires a retry test with an actually blocking revi