equested","summary":"The assigned sections cover revision-aware membership, lifecycle status, migration notices, evidence access and client propagation. One identity-contract gap remains: synthetic PLAN/BUILD rows can collide with real TASK board IDs after re-planning.","findings":[{"id":"board-a6-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/11 — buildWorkItemGraph; LLD.md §2.12","message":"The fallback promises a separate node for each current PLAN row, including rows without TASK heads, but does not define collision-free identities between those synthetic rows and real Tasks. For example, existing TASK t4 can represent plan row t9; an interrupted re-plan can introduce row t4 without its head. Under the existing board-ID contract, both resolve to :T004. The same collision occurs with an unmatched BUILD result for row t4. Removing the Task number from sourceIds prevents join aliases but does not prevent graph-key collisions, which can merge or overwrite distinct rows, mix validation results and defeat the promised unit-null/migration behavior. Specify the identity policy for synthetic rows versus real TASK nodes and add regression coverage for both cases.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:243 — PLAN fallback, unmatched BUILD preservation and sourceIds postconditions","src/workflow/path-scheme.ts:112 — board task IDs use the numeric :T<nnn> suffix","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts:addTasks — drafts are keyed by board ID and an existing ID merges evidence","src/workflow/tasks/__tests__/task-set-reconcile.test.ts:41 — TASK t4 represents plan row t9","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts:storyValidation — validation rows reference graph task item IDs","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts:taskRows — details resolve task rows by taskItemId","/body/testStrategy — crossed-number and stale-listing tests do not specify synthetic-row ID collisions"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contr