on":"All 29 current inventory units are assigned to substantive chunks. The four implementation responsibilities and their dependency order remain intact; /citations/13 is newly assigned to completion. Broad contract, model, error, test and migration selectors intentionally overlap so each responsibility retains its interfaces, logic, failure handling and verification. The originating ISSUE and recorded owner decisions govern this standalone issue LLD; applicable upstream designs are supporting requirements, not invented Epic/HLD ancestry. All substantive chunks receive fresh review, followed by fresh final consistency. No prior coverage is retained or presented as newly reviewed. The current canonical envelope has no visual-definition or attachment fields, and the subject directory contains LLD.md and DECISIONS.md; the board assessment must independently determine visual sufficiency and inspect any linked artifacts discovered.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["board"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/8","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/9","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/10","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/11","chunkIds":["repair"]},{"unitId":"/citations/12","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"/citations/13","chunkIds":["completion"]},{"unitId":"document:line:24","chunkIds":["scope"]}]},"impact":{"baselineAttempt":5,"mode":"full","changes":["Compared the current live document and canonical artifact with attempt 5's captured baseline, accepted plan, completed assessments, advice, finding decisions and effective finding origins; inspected earlier accepted plans for responsibility and provenance continuity.","storyTasks now requires a nonempty TASKS listing whose planRevision equals the approved-or-later PLAN revision, normalized to at least 1 as readPlan does. Missing, empty or stale listings answer not-created despite existing child heads.","The completion outcome and error contract now describe an unfinished Task set for the current plan. New edge cases and unit/integration tests cover failed reconciliation, interrupted reconciliation with newly created unlisted Tasks, explicit override and leaving held Tasks unfrozen.","buildWorkItemGraph now qualifies TASKS membership by current PLAN revision and falls back to PLAN rows matched to heads by planTaskId after interrupted reconciliation. A corresponding edge case and unit test were added.","approveWorkflowTarget's documented signature now uses WorkflowApproveRequest and WorkflowApproveResult, addressing attempt 5's signature advice.","Repair integration coverage now explicitly includes nested Task creation and settlement failures after log append but before head replacement, with pending-operation replay or completion.","Acceptance mapping ac3, migration's resulting-state description and the chosen alternative now mention revision-current membership. Citation /citations/13 was added for src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:241.","Canonical summary, HLD context slice, interactionWithShared, chosenAlternative identifier and openQuestions are unchanged. No authored/generated visual artifact was added in the canonical envelope or subject directory."],"directChunkIds":["completion","repair","board"],"indirectChunkIds":["scope"],"rationale":"Use full review against the immediately preceding complete attempt 5. Completion and board now share a revision-qualified membership rule whose consequences cross unchanged ownership, cascade, override, lifecycle, migration-notice and validation requirements. Repair's new failure tests directly affect verification, while its unchanged stale-set rejection, historical cutoff and live-rule settlement must be checked against the revised completion semantics. The unchanged scope selectors still require fresh end-to-end tracing because current-plan qualification changes when the owner's failed-or-unfinished-Task requirement is satisfied and how missing work appears on the board. Shared contract, error, test and migration sections therefore require coordinated fresh assessment rather than isolated wording review. Attempt 5 contains completed same-party assessments without limitations, but no retention is claimed: all current substantive chunks are selected and final consistency is fresh. Its accepted history leaves exactly one effective finding, completion-r5-001, which remains carried without a resolution decision. The six attempt-4 findings were resolved in attempt 5 and are not carried as effective findings.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["scope"],"currentIds":["scope"],"explanation":"Same selectors, scope responsibility and lack of dependencies. Fresh review checks indirect effects of cu