ns. It specifies ordered prerequisites, revision-qualified Task eligibility, bounded historical settlement, per-Story isolation, committed-write reporting, recovery tests, and backup/restoration procedures. No blocking defect was demonstrated.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9","/citations/11","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md — k8, ac9 and ac10","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — storage integrity, Tasks, migration and raw-write adoption","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts","src/daemon/lifecycle-registry.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/run.ts","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts","src/workflow/convert/rename.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/story-history.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts — writeUnlocked, finishPending and completePending","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts — completion, member cascade and recovery","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/migrated-head.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-repeat.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon — git reflog confirms the cited 2026-11-07 main-to-v2 checkout"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Implement RepairRecorder at the actual store/history commit points, including completePending and nested Task creation. Recording only after a public operation returns would miss log entries committed before head replacement fails.","Add cutoff-boundary fixtures for an approval exactly at COMPLETION_RULE_FROM and a later approval carrying a persisted explicit override.","Existing tests were inspected as evidence; execution belongs to implementation validation."]},{"chunkId":"board","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned sections cover revision-aware membership, lifecycle status, migration notices, evidence access and client propagation. One identity-contract gap remains: synthetic PLAN/BUILD rows can collide with real TASK board IDs after re-planning.","findings":[{"id":"board-a6-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/11 — buildWorkItemGraph; LLD.md §2.12","message":"The fallback promises a separate node for each current PLAN row, including rows without TASK heads, but does not define collision-free identities between those synthetic rows and real Tasks. For example, existing TASK t4 can represent plan row t9; an interrupted re-plan can introduce row t4 without its head. Under the existing board-ID contract, both resolve to :T004. The same collision occurs with an unmatched BUILD result for row t4. Removing the Task number from sourceIds prevents join aliases but does not prevent graph-key collisions, which can merge or overwrite distinct rows, mix validation results and defeat the promised unit-null/migration behavior. Specify the identity policy for synthetic rows versus real TASK nodes and add regression coverage for both cases.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:243 — PLAN fallback, unmatched BUILD preservation and sourceIds postconditions","src/workflow/path-scheme.ts:112 — board task IDs use