us including unmigrated, null-only-for-missing-head semantics, migration notices and pending-decision exclusion through graph, gates, snapshot and client contracts.","Check complete versus build-recorded derivation, Epic progress and Task unit status beside BUILD validation, including the documented difference from latest-round completion evidence.","Inspect daemon, CLI where applicable, VS Code details, TaskRowView, labels and actual webview rendering source; check current JetBrains IPC consumers without imposing deprecated-client requirements.","Assess necessary relationship/UX artifacts and inspect actual renderings where available; distinguish design evidence from the future implementation smoke test.","Check unit, integration, snapshot/client contract and conversion-verification coverage for changed and unchanged board behavior."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Fresh whole-design consistency and requirement traceability","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile all substantive assessments against the originating ISSUE, applicable common-model requirements and owner decisions.","Check end-to-end agreement among live membership, durable overrides, revision handling, repair settlement and board status.","Check contract/error consistency, ownership, dependency order, release compatibility, acceptance mapping and citation support.","Reconcile all seven carried findings only after fresh inspection; distinguish demonstrated defects, limitations and optional advice.","Check necessary artifact verification and enforce the specified final-status precedence."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 27 current inventory units are assigned to substantive chunks. The four implementation responsibilities from attempt 3 are preserved, with new citation ownership added and concerns expanded for the revised contracts. Broad contract, model, error and 