,"mode":"full","changes":["Compared the current live LLD and canonical artifact with attempt 3's captured content, accepted plan and completed feedback. The live document matches attempt 4's captured document.","The summary now explicitly includes unfinished Tasks, overrides after initial approval and stepwise repair reporting. The context, shared-interaction, chosen-alternative and open-question fields remain unchanged.","CompletionEvidence gains storyTasks with listed, not-created and none-required outcomes. Live roll-up now addresses missing listed heads and distinguishes incomplete Task creation from taskless routes.","A new approveArtifactByJsonPath contract and record-override lifecycle operation persist later overrides with audit entries while retaining status, revision and approval time; deferred completion and retry tests are added.","Workflow-head lifecycle handling now specifies unchanged-content preservation and changed-revision reset with Signoff retention through a helper at the two write sites.","Repair now specifies the conversion prerequisite sequence, rename-collision preflight, immutable UTC cutoff, no marker/progress writes and expanded recovery reporting through stoppedAt, applied and remaining.","applyTasks gains an explicit planTaskId-only backfill contract, existing-round preservation and PLAN eligibility beyond approved, with crossed-identity tests.","The board adds DIAG acceptance and Story association, UnitStatus including unmigrated, explicit missing-versus-unmigrated representation, broader migration notices and Task status propagation to the webview.","Tests expand across membership, stored overrides, signoff holds, lifecycle rewrites, normalization, partial repair failure, preview parity, client snapshots and conversion verification. Migration adds downtime and backup/restore steps.","The inventory grows from 25 to 27 units through citations for gates.ts:690 and convert/apply.ts:126; the loader citation changes from load.ts:58 to load.ts:35. No authored visual definitions or attachments are present in the current canonical artifact."],"directChunkIds":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"indirectChunkIds":[],"rationale":"Full review is selected because every substantive responsibility contains changed assigned content. Scope's summary changes its promises; completion introduces membership and durable-override contracts; repair changes ordering, evidence assignment and reporting; board changes kind acceptance and unit representation. Indirect effects also require inspection within these selected chunks: unchanged owner decisions constrain the new override operation; unchanged cascade/reopen and signoff behavior consume new membership and stored evidence; repair-created identities and rounds feed live completion and board joins; lifecycle rewrite rules affect approval validity; shared loader/graph changes affect conversion verification; client contracts and UX consume the new status union. The unchanged issue exclusions, common-model requirements, declared-Story rules and absence of HLD ancestry must remain satisfied. Attempt 3 is the immediately preceding complete same-party baseline and has no limitations. Attempt 2 was invalidated and supplies no reusable coverage; attempt 1's incomplete result is not used to bypass newer evidence. No coverage is retained, and all seven effective attempt-3 findings remain carried until fresh inspection. Final consistency is always fresh.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["scope"],"currentIds":["scope"],"explanation":"Same responsibility and selectors; the changed summary requires fresh scope and upstream traceability assessment."},{"priorIds":["completion"],"currentIds":["completion"],"explanation":"Same implementation responsibility and dependency on scope, expanded for storyTasks, record-override, lifecycle rewrite behavior and new /citations/10. Broad selectors retain completion interfaces, failures and tests."},{"priorIds":["repair"],"currentIds":["repair"],"explanation":"Same responsibility and dependencies, expanded for prerequisite conversion steps, cross-phase reporting, planTaskId backfill and new /citations/11."},{"priorIds":["board"],"currentIds":["board"],"explanation":"Same responsibility and dependencies; fresh assessment covers DIAG, unmigrated unit status, client rendering and indirect changes from completion and repair. The loader citation retains its inventory selector but changes its source location."},{"priorIds":["consistency"],"currentIds":["consistency"],"explanation":"Same final consistency role, dependent on every current substantive chunk and always executed fresh. No chunks are removed or regrouped."}],"retainedCoverage":[],"carriedFindingIds":["[3,\"completion\",\"completion-001\"]","[3,\"completion\",\"completion-002\"]","[3,\"repair\",\"repair-001\"]","[3,\"repair\",\"repair-002\"]","[3,\"repair\",\"repair-003\"]","[3,\"board\",\"board-001\"]","[3,\"board\",\"board-002\"]"],"consistencyChunkIds":["consistency"]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"impact","phase":"impact","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"completion","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"repair","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"board","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"delivery-board-lld-s1","attempt":4,"artifactId":"LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1","status":"changes_requested","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":6,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned scope sections align with the originating ISSUE and applicable common-model requirements. Recorded owner decisions support real unit status and explicit overrides for failed or unfinished Tasks. The design addresses lifecycle preservation, repeatable repair and reporting, preserves the issue’s exclusions, and correctly claims no parent HLD. No blocking scope or traceability defects were found.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","document:line:24","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-eedc4519199b24b4.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md — functional requirements, constraints k3/k8, acceptance ac7–ac10 and ac27–ac29","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — completion, revision and conversion requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:310","src/workflow/storage.ts:175","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:218","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:404","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:433"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"completion","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Reviewed all assigned selectors against the issue, owner decisions, applicable common-model requirements and current implementation. Two gaps remain in partial Task creation and durable-override retry behavior.","findings":[{"id":"completion-r4-001","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:218","message":"storyTasks treats existing child TASK heads as a complete listing whenever TASKS is absent, even with an approved PLAN. Task creation writes individual heads first and TASKS last, so an interrupted creation can leave only part of the planned set. If those existing Tasks have passing rounds, the proposed rule completes the Story without an override while uncreated plan Tasks disappear from the condition. Distinguish an incomplete set from a verified complete set before using this fallback, and cover partial creation with at least one existing Task.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §3.1 CompletionEvidence: child-head fallback precedes the approved-PLAN not-created condition","LLD.md §2.1 and §4: unfinished Task creation must hold completion without an override","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:148-183: createFromPlan writes TASK heads sequentially and the TASKS completion marker last","LLD.md §5: proposed incomplete-creation test covers zero Task heads but not a partial set","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md: unfinished Tasks require an explicit BUILD approval override"]},{"id":"completion-r4-002","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:227","message":"The durable-override design updates the approval writer and completion evidence, but leaves the preceding approveWorkflowTarget code-review gate without a stored-override contract. That gate passes only req.overrideReview and skips the artifact on a blocked review before reaching either approveArtifactByJsonPath or completeThroughService. Consequently, an approval made over review findings followed by interrupted completion cannot be retried through normal re-approval using only its stored override, as the design promises. Specify how this outer gate recognizes a current standing BUILD approval and its persisted override, and test the retry with an actually blocking task-based review and no override in the retry request.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §3.2: overrides must remain usable after request context is gone","LLD.md §4: re-approval finishes a failed completion without undoing the committed approval","LLD.md §5 integration: later re-approval must recover using the stored override","src/workflow/gates.ts:974-986: enforceCodeReviewGate receives only the request override and returns early on blocked","src/workflow/gates.ts:994-1010: approval and completion occur only after that outer gate","src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts:14-27: a blocking task-review gap is overridden only by the supplied option","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts: storedOverride is consumed downstream of the rejecting gate"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/10","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: common-model constraints and S007 requirements","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/approval-view.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts: operation validation","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: child discovery","src/workflow/gates.ts: approval gates and completion hook","src/workflow/tasks/types.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: Task creation and membership","src/workflow/storage.ts: lifecycle reconciliation and Signoff preservation","src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/synthesize.ts: production content write","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts: production content write","src/daemon/workflow-approve.ts","src/cli/services/workflow.ts: approval outcome adapter","src/workflow/team/signoff.ts: deferred completion","src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/storage-signoff-history.test.ts","src/workflow/__tests__/approve-build-freshness.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/completion-evidence.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-members.test.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/__tests__/lifecycle-completion.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"repair","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the issue, applicable common-model requirements and conversion code. Repair ordering, historical eligibility and Task identity handling are specified, but partial-write reporting and rollback remain defective.","findings":[{"id":"repair-r4-001","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:257","message":"Computing applied changes solely by subtracting the remaining plan cannot accurately report committed writes. applyFeedback appends sidecar records while leaving body.feedback intact; feedbackRule therefore reports exactly the same change after those writes. If feedback or subsequent head migration fails, the proposed report omits feedback already committed. Similarly, tasksRule stops listing a Story once TASKS exists, although applyTasks can still backfill missing rounds, including after an interrupted run. Specify sidecar-aware planning and granular write accounting, or collect actual phase results. Add failure tests asserting that committed feedback, migration log entries and Task rounds appear accurately in applied/remaining and retry previews.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §3.5: applied is every planned change absent from the recomputed plan","LLD.md §2.6 and §4: preview fidelity and reporting of writes before failure","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts:88 — feedbackRule examines body.feedback without checking existing sidecar records","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts:114 — applyFeedback appends records and strips nothing","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts: writeMigratedHead appends log entries before replacing the head","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:64 — tasksRule skips existing TASKS heads","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts:82 — applyTasks backfills rounds even when TASKS already exists","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-feedback-rule.test.ts: interrupted append and head-replacement fixtures"]},{"id":"repair-r4-002","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:428","message":"The stated rollback restores only .insrc/artifacts and docs, but repair's unit creation and settlement also stage durable operations under .insrc/journal. A failed write can leave a pending operation outside that backup. After restoring the prescribed copy, the next lifecycle write can replay the repair operation when the restored head matches its prior hash, or encounter a persistent conflict when it does not. Thus restoring this copy does not reliably undo repair as §6 promises. Include journal state in the quiesced backup/restore procedure and define removal of repair-created pending operations before restarting writers. Cover rollback after a staged write fails before head replacement.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §6 steps 4–6 and Backward compat: restoring the step-4 copy is claimed to undo repair","src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts:32 — JOURNAL_DIR is .insrc/journal","src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-lifecycle.ts: createRepoLifecycle installs the durable file journal","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts:371 — staging precedes log append and head replacement","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts:410 — completePending replays staged operations or raises a head conflict","src/workflow/convert/units.ts: applyUnits creates heads through ArtifactStore.write"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9","/citations/11","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md: migration requirements and recorded conversion decisions","src/daemon/repo-convert.ts","src/workflow/convert/types.ts","src/workflow/convert/plan.ts","src/workflow/convert/apply.ts","src/workflow/convert/run.ts","src/workflow/convert/rename.ts","src/workflow/convert/stamps.ts","src/workflow/convert/amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/repair-amendments.ts","src/workflow/convert/feedback-rule.ts","src/workflow/convert/migrated-head.ts","src/workflow/convert/units.ts","src/workflow/convert/tasks.ts","src/workflow/convert/story-history.ts","src/workflow/convert/marker.ts","src/workflow/convert/verify.ts","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts: readPlan and createFromPlan","src/workflow/artifact-core/history.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar-store.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/sidecar.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-lifecycle.ts","src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts: durable writes and pending-operation recovery","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts: rollUp and unitMembers","src/workflow/gates.ts: approved-or-beyond approval handling","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-feedback-rule.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-tasks.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-apply.test.ts","src/workflow/convert/__tests__/convert-verify.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/daemon: git reflog confirming the cited main-to-v2 checkout"],"limitations":[],"advice":["When implementing PLAN eligibility beyond approved, account for TaskSets.readPlan's current approved-only guard and test creation from signed-off and completed PLANs."]},{"chunkId":"board","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the originating ISSUE, applicable common-model and delivery requirements, and current daemon/client code. Unit status, migration labeling and Task identity contracts are substantially specified, but BUILD-only validation preservation and DIAG evidence reads have end-to-end gaps.","findings":[{"id":"board-r4-001","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:184","message":"The proposed task derivation uses TASKS membership, otherwise PLAN rows, without preserving BUILD-only validation entries. With no TASKS head, a PLAN containing t1 and a BUILD containing failed t3 would omit t3 entirely. The current gate computes validation and conflicts by walking graph task children, so this removes the unplanned result, failed count and potentially the validation-conflict signal. Preserve unmatched BUILD evidence independently of authoritative active-task membership, and test both PLAN-plus-extra-BUILD and BUILD-without-PLAN cases.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.9: tasks come from TASKS when present, otherwise PLAN","LLD §3.8: validation remains sourced from BUILD","LLD §5: membership tests omit BUILD-only validation regression cases","src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts: addTasks currently collects PLAN and BUILD task ids","src/workflow/delivery/gate.ts: storyValidation derives task results and conflicts through story.childIds","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts:284 — unmatched BUILD results remain visible as unplanned","src/workflow/delivery/__tests__/gate.test.ts:362 — BUILD tasks without PLAN remain visible","docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/DEF.md:156 — S003 ac4 requires unmatched BUILD results and unplanned marking"]},{"id":"board-r4-002","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:189","message":"DIAG is added as Story evidence, but the design does not extend the evidence-read handler's artifact-id validation. Its regex permits only one suffix after the hash, whereas valid DIAG ids contain both Story and sequence suffixes, such as DIAG-aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa-s1-2. Adding DIAG to the loader's kind list therefore displays an evidence row whose read action still returns 'invalid artifact id'. Specify kind-aware validation for this endpoint and add a client/handler test opening a valid sequenced DIAG while retaining invalid-id and containment checks.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.9 and §3.7: DIAG heads become Story evidence","LLD §5: DIAG coverage currently checks loader admission rather than evidence retrieval","src/workflow/artifact-ids.ts:85 — DIAG requires Story and sequence","src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-ids.test.ts:42 — valid DIAG id has two suffixes","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts: ARTIFACT_ID_RE allows only one suffix","src/workflow/delivery/handlers.ts:110 — handleDeliveryEvidence rejects ids before reading the record","vscode-plugin/src/delivery/delivery-client.ts:124 — evidence actions call workflow.deliveryEvidence"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/5","/