cy and meaningful unit/integration coverage.","Freshly reassess completion-r4-001 and completion-r4-002 without presuming their resolution."],"dependsOn":["scope"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"repair","title":"Repair planning, committed-write accounting and recovery","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/9","/citations/11"],"concerns":["Inspect repair-preview and repair at every schema version while preserving existing conversion modes, progress behavior and schema-marker semantics.","Check ordered prerequisites across renames, stamps, amendments, feedback, head migration, units, Tasks, Story history and settlement.","Inspect RepairRecorder propagation and commit boundaries for feedback lines, migration and batch log entries, heads and Task rounds; verify written remains accurate after failures and remaining accurately describes retry work.","Check planner visibility of backfill-round and settle-unit changes, including existing TASKS heads, proposed head creation and preview/write correspondence.","Inspect createFromPlan acceptLaterStatus, default approved-only behavior for live callers and reconcile, partial-set recovery, missing members, revision mismatches and per-Story failure isolation.","Verify planTaskId-only BUILD joins, preservation of existing rounds, fixed historical cutoff and attributed migration overrides versus the live completion rule.","Check idempotency, collisions, feedback preservation, stopped-step behavior, completedMembers, dependent-step stopping and conversion-verification regression coverage.","Assess deployment order and quiesced backup/restore of artifacts, journal and docs, including staged-write failure recovery and pending-operation replay.","Freshly reassess repair-r4-001 and repair-r4-002 without presuming their resolution."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"bo