ubstantive assessment against the originating ISSUE, applicable upstream requirements and recorded owner decisions.","Check end-to-end agreement among membership completeness, persisted overrides, revision handling, repair reconstruction, committed-write reporting, rollback and board status.","Check acceptance mapping, contracts, errors, ownership, dependency order, deployment compatibility and citations across the live document and canonical artifact.","Reconcile all six carried findings only after fresh inspection, using their canonical provenance keys.","Check necessary visual inspection and coverage declarations; distinguish demonstrated defects, limitations and optional advice and enforce the required status precedence."],"dependsOn":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 28 current inventory units are assigned to substantive chunks, including the newly added /citations/12. The four implementation responsibilities and dependency order from attempt 4 remain intact. Broad contract, data-model, error and test selectors intentionally overlap so each responsibility retains its interfaces, logic, failure handling and verification. The originating ISSUE is the workflow ancestor; applicable common-model and delivery designs are supporting requirements, not invented Epic/HLD ancestry. All substantive chunks receive fresh review, followed by fresh final consistency. No prior chunk is retained or represented as newly reviewed. The current canonical body has no visual-definition fields, and the subject directory contains LLD.md and DECISIONS.md; the board chunk must independently assess visual sufficiency and inspect any linked artifacts it discovers.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["completion","repair","board"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","ch