 adds retry tests with blocking review findings. Citation /citations/12 targets src/workflow/gates.ts:979.","createFromPlan gains repair-only acceptLaterStatus, with default live behavior preserved; repair specifies per-Story TaskSetError handling and exclusion of invalid sets from settlement.","RepairReport replaces inferred applied changes with recorded committed RepairWrite entries. Optional recorders cover sidecars, logs, heads and rounds; retry planning explicitly includes missing rounds on existing TASKS heads.","Migration backup and rollback now include .insrc/journal and require stopping the daemon before restoring artifacts, journal and docs; a staged-write rollback test is added.","Board derivation now preserves unmatched BUILD validation items while separating them from active Tasks and migration notices, with extra-result and no-PLAN cases.","handleDeliveryEvidence gains a contract for valid two-suffix TASK/DIAG identifiers while retaining legacy identifier acceptance and containment checks; handler/client tests cover sequenced DIAG retrieval.","Summary, error paths, migration behavior, chosen alternative, test subjects and acceptance mapping change accordingly. The acceptance table now states the requirement text behind ac1–ac6, and the feedback citation gains a line location."],"directChunkIds":["scope","completion","repair","board"],"indirectChunkIds":[],"rationale":"Full review is warranted because every substantive responsibility contains changed assigned content. Scope changes through the summary and must be retraced against the ISSUE and owner decisions. Completion changes affect both membership completeness and the gate preceding durable approval; they also alter repair eligibility and the board's interpretation of held work. Repair introduces shared Task-set API behavior and granular accounting across ordered conversion phases, with indirect effects on unchanged historical-cutoff, signoff, idempotency and conversion-mode requirements. Board changes couple authoritative membership with retained validation evidence and identifier retrieval across daemon/client boundaries. Unchanged ownership, terminal-state handling, declared-Story completeness, lifecycle preservation, test coverage and upstream constraints therefore require fresh checks alongside the direct edits. The baseline is the immediately preceding complete attempt 4 from the same daemon reviewer; no older result is substituted. All current substantive chunks are selected, so no selective retention claim or provenance shortcut is needed. The six effective findings remain carried until fresh inspection decides their disposition.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["scope"],"currentIds":["scope"],"explanation":"Same selectors and scope responsibility; concerns now include revised acceptance text and the cross-cutting effect of the new contracts. Fresh review replaces retention."},{"priorIds":["completion"],"currentIds":["completion"],"explanation":"Same completion, override and lifecycle responsibility, with new /citations/12 assigned here and explicit outer-gate and partial-set concerns. Existing dependency on scope remains."},{"priorIds":["repair"],"currentIds":["repair"],"explanation":"Same repair selectors and dependency order; concerns expand for committed-write recording, round-aware planning, repair-only PLAN eligibility and journal restoration."},{"priorIds":["board"],"currentIds":["board"],"explanation":"Same board selectors and dependencies; concerns expand for unmatched BUILD validation and end-to-end TASK/DIAG evidence retrieval."},{"priorIds":["consistency"],"currentIds":["consistency"],"explanation":"Fresh final consistency retains dependencies on all substantive chunks and reconciles the six effective attempt-4 findings. No substantive chunk is added, removed, split or merged."}],"retainedCoverage":[],"carriedFindingIds":["[4,\"completion\",\"completion-r4-001\"]","[4,\"completion\",\"completion-r4-002\"]","[4,\"repair\",\"repair-r4-001\"]","[4,\"repair\",\"repair-r4-002\"]","[4,\"board\",\"board-r4-001\"]","[4,\"board\",\"board-r4-002\"]"],"consistencyChunkIds":["consistency"]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"impact","phase":"impact","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"completion","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"repair","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"board","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"delivery-board-lld-s1","attempt":5,"artifactId":"LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1","status":"changes_requested","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":1,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned scope aligns with the originating ISSUE and recorded owner decisions. The LLD addresses lifecycle creation, repeatable repair, genuine unit completion and lifecycle-based board status without inventing parent HLD ancestry. Revised requirements cover partial Task creation, persisted override retries, granular repair reporting, unmatched BUILD evidence and evidence retrieval.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","document:line:24","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md:5-38","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md: functional requirements, constraints k3/k8, acceptance ac7-ac10 and ac27-ac29","docs/plans/core-data-model.md: Gaps 1-4, 7-8, 11-12; scope rulings; s3 binding requirements; s7 and s9 hand-offs; raw-content-writer decision","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:276-286,315-389,479-509","src/workflow/artifact-core/completion-evidence.ts:41-88","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:110-185","src/workflow/delivery/load.ts:35-90"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"completion","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The current design addresses partial initial Task creation, durable override retries, lifecycle initialization, cascade recovery and outcome propagation. One completion defect remains: an existing TASKS listing can represent an older PLAN revision after failed reconciliation, yet the live completion rule accepts it as complete.","findings":[{"id":"completion-r5-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/0 — CompletionEvidence; LLD.md:276","message":"storyTasks accepts any nonempty TASKS listing without checking that its planRevision matches the current approved-or-later PLAN. Re-planning updates TASKS last, and reconciliation failures preserve the PLAN approval, so an interrupted reconciliation can leave the previous listing in place while newly planned Tasks remain uncreated or unlisted. If the old listed Tasks have passing rounds, the proposed live rule completes the Story without an override; unitMembers can also freeze newly created but unlisted Tasks without checking their rounds. Repair explicitly rejects this revision mismatch, but live completion has no equivalent protection. Treat a listing from an unreconciled PLAN revision as unfinished, and add live completion tests for failed and partially completed re-plan reconciliation.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:276 — nonempty TASKS takes precedence without a planRevision check","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:327 — revision mismatch blocks settlement during repair","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md:469 — live incomplete-set tests cover absent TASKS, not an outdated existing listing","src/workflow/tasks/task-set.ts:241 — reconcile applies changes and additions before updating TASKS at the end","src/daemon/tasks-sync.ts:66 — reconciliation failure is reported without reversing PLAN approval","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md:9 — unfinished Tasks require an explicit BUILD approval override"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/10","/citations/12","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-eedc4519199b24b4-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/delivery-board-lld-s1.json","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/make-delivery-board-read-common-artifact-E20261109eedc4519/S001/DECISIONS.md","docs/epics/one-common-model-every-artifact-E202610192f27754d/DEF.md","docs/plans/core-data-model.md — completion, revision and re-plan contracts","src/workflow/artifa